{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted","id":855790,"title":"In what ways are Solar the most powerful among the Exalted ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T10:50:49-07:00","id":855790,"title":"In what ways are Solar the most powerful among the Exalted ?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgbox.com/qyO09QAh.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Solar: </b>Why are you so surprise when you're the one who is puking out rainbow ?<br /> <hr /></div><br /> <br /> The book and the fan often said what in the title, but it's always declared in a vague and kinda fluffy way. Now that we have the charms for Solar, are these the parts of Solar powerset that'll make a Sidereal go &quot;It's a good thing we tried to kill them in the past&quot; and a DB go &quot;It's NOT fair !&quot;:<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if Supernal is what make the Solar the most powerful, but their charms sure does, some of the effects are just crazy strong, like, Eye of Conky bullshit-ly strong (I'm not salty about Resplendent Destiny being dispel-able, I swear). Death Ray is a Scene-long AoE Decisive attack that don't reset you to base Initiative, a Tyrant Lizard getting buffed with Deadly Predator Method is horrifying, and of course, the infamous Doom-Bot and Meteor Shitting Shriek (though I don't understand why they name it after a bird). And some of the effects are perfect, like the Night's anima or some of the Larceny charms.<br /> <br /> Being the only one who can do a Solar 3 Working which is unspammable Shinmaic Communion (too bad I have no idea what qualify as &quot;subtle alterations&quot;)<br /> <br /> Mastery effect for MA, maybe ? Since everyone will get them if they practice the appropriate MA so it's probably not.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if this is the intent, but........shitting out N/A Artifact with the right Craft build.<br /> <br /> Errhh...Does being the only splat with powerful Bureaucracy charms count ?<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, Deadly Predator Method is only <b><i>Essence 3</i></b> (\u0ca0\u256d\u256e\u0ca0)........This have to be a typo, right ? I just can't imagine what an Essence 5 Survival charm look like if essence 3 can turn your Tyrant Lizard into a gigantic tornado of death-puking dinosaur who can shoot eye beams and force choke people with its tiny arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:59:22-07:00","id":855796,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Solars got a big buff in Ex3. <br /> <br /> Now, whether Solars are so powerful they make other Exalts look like kids playing with bottle rockets compared to the Solar's F-15 fighter jets, we will have to wait and see. Right now, we can only compare Ex3 Solars to Ex2 verison of the other splats. Frankly that is an unfair comparison. The Ex3 Solars make the <i>Ex2 Solars</i> look like kids playing with bottle rockets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:01:26-07:00","id":855799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855796#post855796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ex3 Solars make the <i>Ex2 Solars</i> look like kids playing with bottle rockets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really, 2e had the definitely more busted Charms in a lot of ways, and &quot;better&quot;/more absolute perfects of course (which also made playing them boring, but that's another subject).<br /> <br /> What's really changed with 3e is the granularity of effects, and being able to combine them all whenever you want (which was not the case for 99% of the life of 2e due to the combo tax).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted#post855790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastery effect for MA, maybe ? Since everyone will get them if they practice the appropriate MA so it's probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no reason to believe this is true. Sids probably will, sure. The rest, doubtful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:07:38-07:00","id":855806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855799#post855799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, not really, 2e had the definitely more busted Charms in a lot of ways, and &quot;better&quot;/more absolute perfects of course (which also made playing them boring, but that's another subject).<br /> <br /> What's really changed with 3e is the granularity of effects, and being able to combine them all whenever you want (which was not the case for 99% of the life of 2e due to the combo tax).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I wasn't considering broken charms. Ex3 Solars have more &quot;Holy shit! A PC can do that?!&quot; charms than Ex2 with out having to exploit flaws in the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:09:53-07:00","id":855810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855806#post855806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit I wasn't considering broken charms. Ex3 Solars have more &quot;Holy shit! A PC can do that?!&quot; charms than Ex2 with out having to exploit flaws in the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note; by &quot;busted&quot; I simply mean stuff like your garden variety Solar paranoia combo, not dumb bullshit stuff like pre-errata Zeal, aka stuff written by people who didn't grasp system fundamentals <i>at all</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:16:29-07:00","id":855819,"title":"","content":"Yeah, old 2E Solars could rewrite the entirety of a society's social mores by having a chat with a dude in a cupboard. If anything, Solars were reined back from the kind of unfun bullshit they tossed around. <br /> <br /> In any case, to answer Jen's question, historically it's been a combination of things. Solars got the most encompassing charms, the most efficient mote costs, the best XP costs, access to the best sorcery, incredible long-lasting dice advantages like Infinite Mastery, and so on. Basically, they held a superiority in all individual aspects that, when taken as a whole, meant Solars (and their offshoots) were playing in an entirely different league from everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:18:38-07:00","id":855820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855799#post855799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no reason to believe this is true. Sids probably will, sure. The rest, doubtful.</div> </div> </div> </div>People said that DB will get Mastery effects for the Immaculate Style since both are kinda elementally, this mean that as long as a Style has resonance themes with a splat, they should get the Mastery effect for that style too, like Lunar and White Reaper Style for exam.........wait, they <i>don't </i>get the Mastery benefit, tccch, freaking Solar <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:19:52-07:00","id":855823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855820#post855820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People said that DB will get Mastery effects for the Immaculate Style since both are kinda elementally, this mean that as long as a Style has resonance themes with a splat, they should get the Mastery effect for that style too, like Lunar and White Reaper Style for exam.........wait, they <i>don't </i>get the Mastery benefit, tch, freaking unfair <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>DBs getting Mastery for the Immaculate styles would make sense for a very obvious, specific reason that is not reasonable to extrapolate back to the other styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:55:37-07:00","id":855852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855823#post855823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs getting Mastery for the Immaculate styles would make sense for a very obvious, specific reason that is not reasonable to extrapolate back to the other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DBs shouldn't get Mastery effect for any style. They can get rid of terrestrial keywords with training and it should be enough. I dont want my DBs to be better then Lunars in MA, or Equal to a sidereal or a solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:00:36-07:00","id":855859,"title":"","content":"Bigger dice pools and dice tricks that squeeze more successes out of those dice pools. Sure, everything else they get helps a lot, but when it comes down to it, the basic advantage is how much effort Solars can put towards accomplishing a task. <br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded Excellency allows them to succeed at most mundane tasks, but they can't get as much insurance against bad rolls as Solars do. <br /> <br /> I <i>think</i> Sidereals have Solars beat at lower difficulties in terms of efficiency, but they won't have the sheer power needed to make high-end Artifacts. The upside is that they can get a <i>lot</i> of mileage out of their circumstantial bonuses. <br /> <br /> Lunar dice pools are on par with Solars, but the nature of Attribute-based Charms means that they can apply themselves to certain tasks the way Solars can. <br /> <br /> Liminals are at their best when they're burning enough motes to flare their anima, which suggests that they're equipped to deal with tough challenges when they're backed into a corner. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:09:05-07:00","id":855867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855820#post855820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People said that DB will get Mastery effects for the Immaculate Style since both are kinda elementally, this mean that as long as a Style has resonance themes with a splat, they should get the Mastery effect for that style too, like Lunar and White Reaper Style for exam.........wait, they <i>don't </i>get the Mastery benefit, tccch, freaking Solar <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a wait and see, but it makes since as masters of martial arts Sidereal get mastery.<br /> <br /> What really makes solar the most powerful, is a narrow margin. Access to what looks like every artifact, and mastery, and solar circle sorcery. <br /> <br /> We know on the artifact level Dragon blooded are right behind them. Since all evocations of the same artifact level are logically on the same power curve then easier access to artifacts could give Dragon blooded a advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:19:34-07:00","id":855879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855852#post855852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs shouldn't get Mastery effect for any style. They can get rid of terrestrial keywords with training and it should be enough. I dont want my DBs to be better then Lunars in MA, or Equal to a sidereal or a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm <i>very </i>comfortable with DBs being &quot;equal&quot; (in this very specific way, probably the only way) to a Solar <i>within the context of</i><i> the MA Styles totally designed to fight Solars and Lunars</i>.<br /> <br /> now we must fight with knives<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855867#post855867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all evocations of the same artifact level are logically on the same power curve then easier access to artifacts could give Dragon blooded a advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts already have a number of inherent limitations, and I dunno, the Evocations are really cool, but I don't see them as making as big a difference as, say, investing in more Charms. Super general statement I know. Complicated narrative unlocks and resets make Evocations look a lot less useful to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:22:26-07:00","id":855883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855823#post855823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs getting Mastery for the Immaculate styles would make sense for a very obvious, specific reason that is not reasonable to extrapolate back to the other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to stick my neck out here with a theory on Immaculate martial arts.<br /> <br /> No mastery keywords... at all.<br /> Terrestrial keyword are still a restriction.<br /> DBs have a way of overcoming the Terrestrial keyword on ALL martial arts. Probably a charm with lots of prereqs and some special restrictions.<br /> Some charms work better if you have an elemental anima flux at a certain level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:30:16-07:00","id":855886,"title":"","content":"re: Martial Arts Mastery<br /> <br /> Here's who gets benefits of the Mastery Keyword that we know for certain: The Solars and the Abyssals, since they're both Solaroids. The book also mentions that Sidereals have &quot;their own esoteric methods for accessing these effects&quot; (pg 427).<br /> <br /> We can assume that unless things get changed more significantly that the Infernals will probably also get the benefits for the Mastery Keyword. Plus, in the layout leak, the explanation of the Mastery Keyword did in fact namedrop Infernals. (&quot;The Solar Exalted, and their dark reflections, the Abyssal and Infernal Exalted&quot;).<br /> <br /> Most Terrestrials are bound by the effects of the Terrestrial keyword in their Martial Arts, but it's rumored that there's ways around this for the Immaculates. Possibly through some kind of merit. We don't know if the Immaculate Styles will have Mastery benefits, or which groups can access them, and we won't know until the DB book drops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:53:20-07:00","id":855907,"title":"","content":"I know we all know Jen's art is the highest of quality but I want some of these Charm names in the actual books. Meteor Shitting Shrike is what we call &quot;iconic&quot;. <br /> (Also, it's Death Ray, not Dead Ray. Tiny nitpick, but I'm saving Dead Ray for Void Circle Necromancy.)<br /> <br /> The Solar capstones/high-end stuff are pretty powerful, but in a Solar way: Eye of the Unconquered Sun lets you be Aware, but of <i>everything</i>. I can only imagine what Neighborhood Relocation Scheme or Generalized Ammunition Technique will look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:30:09-07:00","id":855943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855852#post855852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs shouldn't get Mastery effect for any style. They can get rid of terrestrial keywords with training and it should be enough. I dont want my DBs to be better then Lunars in MA, or Equal to a sidereal or a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing analogous to a Mastery keyword for non-Hero martial arts in 2e was the set of small benefits Dragon-Bloods gained from using the Immaculate styles. Errata written by the current team for 2.5 clarified that <i>only</i> Dragon-Bloods could gain these benefits, meaning that Dragon-Bloods were explicitly meant to be the best at using the Immaculate styles.<br /> <br /> I really hope they haven't changed their minds on this point, but apparently you do? I don't see the problem with Dragon-Bloods being good at doing their own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:36:25-07:00","id":855950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855943#post855943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope they haven't changed their minds on this point, but apparently you do? I don't see the problem with Dragon-Bloods being good at doing their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't see the problems with giving Dragon-Blooded a full Solar-level combat suite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:41:23-07:00","id":856019,"title":"","content":"Drawings are funny and all, er... are we talking about Dragonblooded martial arts because already had this thread like a week ago - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851393-what-is-the-solar-advantage-in-3ed?\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...antage-in-3ed?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:42:50-07:00","id":856021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855950#post855950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't see the problems with giving Dragon-Blooded a full Solar-level combat suite?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a series of effects in a defined and limited tree intended to make them actually reasonably terrifying for a Solar to deal with, I don't see a problem. An MA supernal Solar will still race through the trees faster than a Terrestrial of equivalent age.<br /> <br /> But I would be frankly livid if Solars\u2014or any other Exalt\u2014could use the Dragon-bloodeds' designated toys more adeptly than their owners could ever hope to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:53:37-07:00","id":856029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855950#post855950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't see the problems with giving Dragon-Blooded a full Solar-level combat suite?</div> </div> </div> </div>lmao x-tremeeeeeee hyperbole","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:59:55-07:00","id":856032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856021#post856021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a series of effects in a defined and limited tree intended to make them actually reasonably terrifying for a Solar to deal with, I don't see a problem. An MA supernal Solar will still race through the trees faster than a Terrestrial of equivalent age.<br /> <br /> But I would be frankly livid if Solars\u2014or any other Exalt\u2014could use the Dragon-bloodeds' designated toys more adeptly than their owners could ever hope to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not a fan of the idea that &quot;Well this is your martial art, YOURS.... buuuuut i'm better at it than you! I get better use out of it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:15:33-07:00","id":856037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856032#post856032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not a fan of the idea that &quot;Well this is your martial art, YOURS.... buuuuut i'm better at it than you! I get better use out of it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Solar</b>: He got a real pretty martial art ain't he?<br /> <b>Lunar:</b> That's the truth<br /> <b>Solar:</b> You gonna do some prayin' for me, Dragonblooded. And you better pray good cause I'm gonna fuck you up with your own Martial Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:00:15-07:00","id":856054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856021#post856021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would be frankly livid if Solars\u2014or any other Exalt\u2014could use the Dragon-bloodeds' designated toys more adeptly than their owners could ever hope to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get to claim a martial art as yours like that. By their very nature, all non-SMA martial arts are generic and universal; you can't block Solars from using or being supremely skilled at a certain martial art just by declaring it to be important to your culture. The Dragon-Bloodeds' designated toys are their charms, not the martial arts styles they happen to favour, and Solars are indeed completely unable to use DB charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:20:52-07:00","id":856063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855950#post855950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't see the problems with giving Dragon-Blooded a full Solar-level combat suite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I would, but that's not what is being suggested.<br /> <br /> A Solar Martial Artist uses more than just Martial Arts Charms; they can use Solar Resistance and Dodge for defence, Solar Awareness to boost their join battle pools and Solar Athletics to enhance their attacks and mobility. They also have Solar Excellency caps and mote pools.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded martial artist with identical Martial Arts Charms would be at a disadvantage in all these areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-30-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:28:48-07:00","id":856066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we have the charms for Solar, are these the parts of Solar powerset that'll make a Sidereal go &quot;It's a good thing we tried to kill them in the past&quot; and a DB go &quot;It's NOT fair !&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div> The flashiest high-Essence Charms are probably the kind of thing that produce iconic feats that people would tell stories about for generations, but in practical terms Solars are consistently going to come off as highly effective at asserting themselves through utilitarian application of their regular Charms from Essence 1 to 3. The might of the Solars is a holistic thing; you have to look at the sum of their parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:31:50-07:00","id":856069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855883#post855883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to stick my neck out here with a theory on Immaculate martial arts.<br /> <br /> No mastery keywords... at all.<br /> Terrestrial keyword are still a restriction.<br /> DBs have a way of overcoming the Terrestrial keyword on ALL martial arts. Probably a charm with lots of prereqs and some special restrictions.<br /> Some charms work better if you have an elemental anima flux at a certain level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because everyone seems to have hang-ups about Mastery, this is probably the best way to do it. I might make the &quot;avoid Terrestrial keyword&quot; tied to a prereq Charm (a la the Enlightening Charms of yore). I like the idea of a Merit but that also seems too easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:54:39-07:00","id":856080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856032#post856032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not a fan of the idea that &amp;quot;Well this is your martial art, YOURS.... buuuuut i'm better at it than you! I get better use out of it!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing a DB or a Lunar or whatever because you want to be the best at something you should probably play a solar instead. DBs have the inane advantage of being despised but not hunted everywhere they go, anyone who plays a solar outside of the deep threshold probably thinks that's quite unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:03:46-07:00","id":856087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856080#post856080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're playing a DB or a Lunar or whatever because you want to be the best at something you should probably play a solar instead. DBs have the inane advantage of being despised but not hunted everywhere they go, anyone who plays a solar outside of the deep threshold probably thinks that's quite unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You're always being hunted&quot; is a paper tiger of an issue honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:11:52-07:00","id":856090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856054#post856054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon-Bloodeds' designated toys are their charms, not the martial arts styles they happen to favour, and Solars are indeed completely unable to use DB charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This warstrider has been passed down through my family for generations. In each generation, when the pilot dies, his consciousness joins with the warstrider, lifting its spirit and filling its limbs with vigor so long as one of their descendents is at the helm. It has been designed from the ground up to be leavened by the anima of a Dragon; wood gives it life, air gives it breath, fire gives it fury, water gives it flexibility, earth gives it stability. It is the pinnacle of a Dragon's craft...<br /> <br /> ...so WHY is a Solar crashing around in it?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, I sort of stuck my giant Solar cock in it and it all worked out even better than how you'd been doing it.&quot;<br /> &quot;You wh- it wh- that's not how that works! That's not how <i>anything</i> works!&quot;<br /> &quot;It does now!&quot;<br /> &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> &quot;Because my cock is huuuuuuuuugeeeeee!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:18:39-07:00","id":856094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856090#post856090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oh, I sort of stuck my giant Solar cock in it and it all worked out even better than how you'd been doing it.&quot;<br /> &quot;You wh- it wh- that's not how that works! That's not how <i>anything</i> works!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of is how it works, and always has worked. The Solars are the best at doing stuff, that's always been the whole point of them. Trying to make Terrestrials just as strong as Solars or stronger is totally missing the point of Exalted; they are weaker and less skilled than Solars and that's a big part of what defines them. They'd be far less interesting as a splat if they weren't the underdog in terms of individual power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:27:07-07:00","id":856100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856054#post856054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get to claim a martial art as yours like that. By their very nature, all non-SMA martial arts are generic and universal; you can't block Solars from using or being supremely skilled at a certain martial art just by declaring it to be important to your culture. The Dragon-Bloodeds' designated toys are their charms, not the martial arts styles they happen to favour, and Solars are indeed completely unable to use DB charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I could have phrased that slightly better. But to claim that the 5 Immaculate Dragon Styles are not aligned to the Terrestrial Exalted above other known Exalted requires a certain degree of deliberate obtuseness. As martial arts, they're in the public domain, so to speak, and nobody's saying (at least I don't think anyone's saying) that Solars shouldn't be able to benefit from a Mastery keyword, were one to exist. The objection comes from the Solars being to use those charms being able to use them better than the Exalted host to whom they are iconic. A solar wielding Immaculate MA could very well defeat a Terrestrial Immaculate because:<br /> <br /> 1.) He has better stats.<br /> 2.) He has better luck<br /> 3.) He's supplementing his attacks with the power of the Solar charmset.<br /> 4.) He has Martial Arts as his Supernal, so he's able to reach the pinnacle of that style far, far faster than a Dragon-Blooded monk.<br /> <br /> There is plenty of room for a Solar to step in and which her natural prowess unlock secrets that have stymied and/or eluded Terrestrial savants of all stripes for centuries. This particular incident is not one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856080#post856080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're playing a DB or a Lunar or whatever because you want to be the best at something you should probably play a solar instead. DBs have the inane advantage of being despised but not hunted everywhere they go, anyone who plays a solar outside of the deep threshold probably thinks that's quite unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm playing a Dragon-Blood I want to play an elementally empowered champion, and that's <i>absolutely</i> what I should be playing if that's my goal. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:29:39-07:00","id":856101,"title":"","content":"<b>Glorious Solar Dickslap</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3A<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Forever<br /> <b>Type</b>: Bi-Winning<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Obvious, Tiger Blood<br /> <i>&quot;You know what? All of you better duck. Because I'm about to turn left...&quot;</i><br /> <b>Effect</b>: robble robble Lawgivers robble robble First Age robble robble Divine Right robble fluff. The Solar's anima hardens into a giant golden protrusion extending from his (or her) groin, which he immediately uses to strike whatever challenge happens to obstruct him. This is a perfect effect; the Solar immediately wins because Solar, because having discrete strengths and weaknesses is tautologically for people who aren't Solars. If they wanted those, they'd be playing something else!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:35:40-07:00","id":856103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856090#post856090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This warstrider has been passed down through my family for generations. In each generation, when the pilot dies, his consciousness joins with the warstrider, lifting its spirit and filling its limbs with vigor so long as one of their descendents is at the helm. It has been designed from the ground up to be leavened by the anima of a Dragon; wood gives it life, air gives it breath, fire gives it fury, water gives it flexibility, earth gives it stability. It is the pinnacle of a Dragon's craft...<br /> <br /> ...so WHY is a Solar crashing around in it?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, I sort of stuck my giant Solar cock in it and it all worked out even better than how you'd been doing it.&quot;<br /> &quot;You wh- it wh- that's not how that works! That's not how <i>anything</i> works!&quot;<br /> &quot;It does now!&quot;<br /> &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> &quot;Because my cock is huuuuuuuuugeeeeee!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of a false equivalence. Immaculate Martial Arts are Sidereal-created disciplines, designed to a) be effective element-themed martial arts, which by definition any of the Exalted can learn, that happens to b) coincide with and reinforce the elemental natures of the Dragon-Blooded. In past editions, there's never been anything to suggest that the Dragon-Blooded are inherently superior practitioners of Immaculate Martial Arts, just that mastering them conveys on them an additional benefit, potentially negating an innate weakness.<br /> <br /> What you're describing is an interesting heritage artifact that may provide additional benefits when attuned by a member of a specific lineage. Seems like perfectly valid and intriguing design space. Because of the way Artifacts work, it seems likely that a generic Solar would be at least as good with that Artifact as a generic Dragon-Blooded, but a true heir could very well gain some real benefit.<br /> <br /> I love the concept, but I'm not sure how it would be interpreted as equivalent to the actual topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:51:39-07:00","id":856109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856101#post856101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Glorious Solar Dickslap</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dumb exaggeration aside, Solars being the best at using abilities is kind of the central thesis of Solars. If you don't like that I'd recommend playing a game other than Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:04:31-07:00","id":856116,"title":"","content":"The problem with DB Immaculates being on par with or better than Solar Immaculates is that both varieties of Immaculate have to be balanced against other members of their splat.<br /> <br /> If you're a Dragonblood, taking Snake Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. And if you're a Solar, taking Water Dragon Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. But Solar-level Snake Style is much much better than Terrestrial-level Snake Style. The only way (I can think of) for Snake vs Water Dragon to be a non-obvious choice for both Solars and Terrestrials is for Solar Water Dragon to be much better than Terrestrial Water Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:06:16-07:00","id":856117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856116#post856116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with DB Immaculates being on par with or better than Solar Immaculates is that both varieties of Immaculate have to be balanced against other members of their splat.<br /> <br /> If you're a Dragonblood, taking Snake Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. And if you're a Solar, taking Water Dragon Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. But Solar-level Snake Style is much much better than Terrestrial-level Snake Style. The only way (I can think of) for Snake vs Water Dragon to be a non-obvious choice for both Solars and Terrestrials is for Solar Water Dragon to be much better than Terrestrial Water Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:17:52-07:00","id":856124,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that previously, Immaculates only accessed Immaculate martial arts after at least a year of meditation and eating only bread and water, had to learn special initiation charms from an Immaculate Master, and still had to pay extra xp to get them.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's still the case. Maybe Immaculates get to ignore the Terrestrial keyword on Immaculate styles but only because of a special training regime (extra 5 dot merit maybe? Perhaps a bit cheap. I'm sure the devs can balance it). Meanwhile, other Dragonblood can learn the styles at a weaker level because they didn't do the special training regime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:18:16-07:00","id":856125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856116#post856116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with DB Immaculates being on par with or better than Solar Immaculates is that both varieties of Immaculate have to be balanced against other members of their splat.<br /> <br /> If you're a Dragonblood, taking Snake Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. And if you're a Solar, taking Water Dragon Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. But Solar-level Snake Style is much much better than Terrestrial-level Snake Style. The only way (I can think of) for Snake vs Water Dragon to be a non-obvious choice for both Solars and Terrestrials is for Solar Water Dragon to be much better than Terrestrial Water Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the opportunity cost of the Terrestrial Immaculate charms: while there's no assurance XP costs won't change in this new edition (and I want to say we've heard they might), the terrestrial in previous editions has been paying a non-negligible surcharge for their Martial Arts, as well as a serious hit in chargen resources--and is paying through the goddamn nose next to the Solar. There are several factors historically that have also made it a daunting proposition for a Terrestrial to take those charms, even when they were objectively some of their most powerful combat options.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:18:48-07:00","id":856126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856109#post856109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like that I'd recommend playing a game other than Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man this persistent fallacy/dismissal needs to diaf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:19:34-07:00","id":856128,"title":"","content":"I find the Idea of a style without any Charms with a Mastery effect to be unlikely.<br /> <br /> It is not like that is something the creator of a style decides to add - it is just an OOC thing to represent the Solars superior skill at Martial Arts when applied to that particular style, bumping it up to the capacity of native Solar Charms. I can't make sense of a MA in which Solars can't manage to apply their skill to the fullest because it was &quot;designed for the Dragon Blooded&quot;. So was every MA made by Dragon Blooded, yet they will likely still have to deal with Terrestrial Keywords in those, making the Lunars better than them at it, as Mastery Keywords, making Solars and Sidereals even better still.<br /> <br /> Personally, If I wanted to make the Dragon Styles particularly attractive choices, mechanically instead of only culturally, for DBs,I think I'd go for good synergies with the particularities of their Charmset and/or Animas. I can make more sense of that as something that would be feasible in-setting, even with native Charms not being discrete in-setting things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:24:24-07:00","id":856133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856116#post856116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with DB Immaculates being on par with or better than Solar Immaculates is that both varieties of Immaculate have to be balanced against other members of their splat.<br /> <br /> If you're a Dragonblood, taking Snake Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. And if you're a Solar, taking Water Dragon Style shouldn't be a complete sucker choice. But Solar-level Snake Style is much much better than Terrestrial-level Snake Style. The only way (I can think of) for Snake vs Water Dragon to be a non-obvious choice for both Solars and Terrestrials is for Solar Water Dragon to be much better than Terrestrial Water Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is, not every DB will have a chance to learn Water Dragon*, while many might be able to learn Snake. Narrative aside there were mechanical restrictions in place in past eds from having your cake and eating it too at least at chargen, and certainly until you found a teacher for the enlightening Charms, and while I don't necessarily like the narrow mechanical positions they represented, something similar wouldn't be terrible.<br /> <br /> I would bet the intent is for even fewer Solars to have the opportunity to learn Water Dragon either - maybe one in the entirety of the setting, leaving individual tables aside (&quot;Solar Dynast&quot; trope aside, and I don't see the need to let you auto-activate latent Charms or w/e when you Exalt just because you bought the Ability dots in the Style hence learning the actual Charms as a Solar might be a problem).<br /> <br /> The way I see it, Water Dragon may be the best option for DBs, but that doesn't mean most DBs will have an opportunity to learn it. That doesn't devalue Snake for DBs in any way. Nor does it devalue Snake if the Immaculate DB Styles inherently don't incorporate the main weakness of DBs with MAs, namely the Terrestrial Keyword.<br /> <br /> *insert element here, used for example only","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:44:02-07:00","id":856144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856094#post856094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are the best at doing stuff, that's always been the whole point of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856109#post856109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like that I'd recommend playing a game other than Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why my responses to you have been satire...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I see it like this.<br /> <br /> The aristocratic themes of the Dragon-Blooded square <i>really</i> well with their martial artists being, for want of a better term, excessively orthodox. There's probably a specific term for &quot;your kung fu is too mired in tradition and you are afraid to innovate too much&quot; that comes with the genre but I don't know what it is. But if you spend a hundred years mastering a martial art that was specifically designed for you and you are adamant in your orthodoxy with it, shouldn't you be<i> really fucking good at it</i>? Is the giant-dicked power fantasy that is (apparently?) the default Solar tale really worth that much worfing that you have to be better than everyone at everything in all circumstances or else your tent will fall down?<br /> <br /> Doesn't it make some measure of sense that as long as Peleps Deled and Wind are having a match with Water Dragon Style (which is Deled's fucking <i>jam</i>) that they be equal in power and skill?<br /> <br /> But then Wind starts bringing in powers from, I dunno, Crane or Single Point and Peleps Deled is like oshit what do<br /> <br /> Doesn't that make a much better fight, a much better narrative than &quot;Wind is inherently better at Water Dragon than Deled because reasons&quot;?<br /> <br /> What's better? That the rebel martial artist uses his giant protagonist-cock to perform the orthodox-art <i>better</i> than the orthodox-user, or that he masters different arts that the orthodox-kung-fu-man was afraid to touch and uses not giant-cock-powers but versatility, strategy and open-mindedness to humble him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:47:28-07:00","id":856145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856103#post856103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Immaculate Martial Arts are Sidereal-created disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div>This also needs to go. &quot;Oh you cute little not actually exalts... here you can't be trusted to break your limitations on your own.... we'll do it for you...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:57:30-07:00","id":856151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856144#post856144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you spend a hundred years mastering a martial art that was specifically designed for you and you are adamant in your orthodoxy with it, shouldn't you be<i> really fucking good at it</i>? Is the giant-dicked power fantasy that is (apparently?) the default Solar tale really worth that much worfing that you have to be better than everyone at everything in all circumstances or else your tent will fall down?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you spend a hundred years mastering a martial art then you will be really fucking good at it. You don't actually need Solar-level charms to be good at things. You'll have dots all over the place, all its charms and essence 3+, and all that experience may well allow you to defeat a young upstart Solar who's only been Exalted for a few years, as your vast experience overcomes their raw power. But if you have a Lawgiver with 100 years of experience and dedication learning a specific martial art against a Dragon-Blood with the same experience at the same MA, the Solar will be better and more skilled with that martial art, exactly like if you have a century-old DB using Melee against a century-old Solar who also uses Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:15:37-07:00","id":856164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856021#post856021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a series of effects in a defined and limited tree intended to make them actually reasonably terrifying for a Solar to deal with, I don't see a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I would like to be able to play a DB who is not an Immaculate Martial Artist without feeling like an idiot. The ability it remove the Terrestrial keyword is already potentially problematic enough, but adding the Mastery keyword substantially compounds the issue.<br /> <br /> Second, we're talking about ~50 charms across five styles. That's not exactly limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An MA supernal Solar will still race through the trees faster than a Terrestrial of equivalent age. </div> </div> </div>Any other Solar will advance no faster than a Terrestrial. The more relevant comparison here is with a 50-year old Immaculate Master or a 100-year old Immaculate Double Master leading a Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I would be frankly livid if Solars\u2014or any other Exalt\u2014could use the Dragon-bloodeds' designated toys more adeptly than their owners could ever hope to. </div> </div> </div>Much as Black Claw is vastly more terrifying when combined with Solar Socialize, I expect that part of their utility for Dragon-Blooded will be found in synergistic interactions with native Dragon-Blooded charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:17:50-07:00","id":856168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856144#post856144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that make a much better fight, a much better narrative than &quot;Wind is inherently better at Water Dragon than Deled because reasons&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, a resounding NO, because there are, in fact, reasons for that. Solars will be superior at Martial Arts than DBs, just like like they are at every single other Ability. It doesn't matter to me if it is DB Tiger master VS a Solar Tiger master or if it is a DB Earth Dragon Master VS a Solar Earth Dragon master. If they are both masters and the Solar was not better at it as far as the style go, that would hit verissimillitude pretty hard for me, given how Solars are supposed to be in terms of skills.<br /> <br /> By the way I view it, Deled being the equal of Wind (assuming they both mastered Water Dragon) is what would be weird and &quot;because reasons&quot;. It is not a certain defeat for Deled, of course, especially since he is a lot older and has a bunch of additional Charms and Artifacts that may equalize the playing field or even give him the edge, but Wind would still have the &quot;impossible&quot; Solar Skill and be superior to Deled if their Water Dragon techniques existed in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:25:59-07:00","id":856175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856145#post856145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also needs to go. &quot;Oh you cute little not actually exalts... here you can't be trusted to break your limitations on your own.... we'll do it for you...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that's what you think Immaculate Martial Arts should be? An inherent limitation-breaker? That's... not really in line with the Martial Arts system presented in Third Edition as I understand it, and a huge change to the setting.<br /> <br /> The Martial Arts system allows an Exalted of any type to express their Essence in similar ways, representative of their philosophy and their training instead of their nature as a Lunar, Abyssal, Dragon-Blooded, or whatever. The Mastery and Terrestrial keywords exist as they do to try to balance Martial Arts Charms against the user's native Charms. This means that the Terrestrial keyword and inability to use the Mastery keyword is inherently limiting to the Dragon-Blooded under the existing system.<br /> <br /> Turning the Immaculate Martial Arts into a limit-breaker for Dragon-Blooded that other Exalted can't use as well as they can... that's not the Martial Arts system. That's just simply not what that system does. That's some kind of native Charm, and not really inherently affiliated with the Immaculate Philosophy.<br /> <br /> If it's a Martial Art, then I don't particularly see why it's a terrible thing if it is taught to them by the setting's foremost martial arts experts.<br /> <br /> Because of the way the system is structured, the Immaculate styles as used by the Dragon-Blooded need to be balanced in some form against Terrestrial Charms. Similarly, the way that the Immaculate styles are used by Solars needs to be balanced against Solar Charms. It's not about who is the Bigger Protagonist with the Bigger Dick. It's about how the system and the setting work. For all the complaining, I'm not really seeing a mechanically balanced, setting consistent way around this being proposed. Instead, there's accusations of juvenile power fantasy, phrased in terms of Whose Dick Is Bigger. Real mature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:31:52-07:00","id":856178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856128#post856128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the Idea of a style without any Charms with a Mastery effect to be unlikely.<br /> Personally, If I wanted to make the Dragon Styles particularly attractive choices, mechanically instead of only culturally, for DBs,I think I'd go for good synergies with the particularities of their Charmset and/or Animas. I can make more sense of that as something that would be feasible in-setting, even with native Charms not being discrete in-setting things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this here is a good idea, maybe allow some DB Combat Ability Charms to be used simultaneously with some Immaculate Style Charms. It would play up to the &quot;designed for me&quot; theme using the nature of DB power, and not something inherent to a martial art that for some reason cannot be mastered by a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:35:26-07:00","id":856182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856168#post856168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are both masters and the Solar was not better at it as far as the style go, that would hit verissimillitude pretty hard for me, given how Solars are supposed to be in terms of skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, really?<br /> <br /> I mean, I sound radical and hyperbolic because that's sort of how I talk but, um, that's how it's been for two editions running. Solars haven't gotten to be better at Water Dragon just 'cuz Solar for, uh... a little under fourteen years now, and Immaculate Masters have been a match or huge trouble for Solars (even solars with Immaculate Martial Arts) ever since they were introduced. (Edit: 2e Fire Immaculates are actually <i>way</i> better, <i>leagues</i> better at Fire Dragon than Solars, because of how the charms key into their anima. Which I guess is sort of what you're advocating for, so, props.)<br /> <br /> Is your verisimilitude okay? Because it seems like it should want to quit boxing and open up a little deli if it's been getting hit in the face for fourteen years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-30-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:47:22-07:00","id":856187,"title":"","content":"Given two exactly similar scenarios, excepting that one is a Solar and the other is a DB, the Solar should have developed the Ability further. That is the predicament of their Essence. That is not to say that the DB wouldn't be powerful and a force to reckon with and might even win in a clash. But that should come from factors that are external to the Ability itself.<br /> <br /> If all you are examining is the Ability, the Solar should be better.<br /> <br /> I'm all for interactions with DB Anima and Charms though. It would be a feat that a Solar would be unable to replicate, not because he can't master the Ability to a certain level, but because he needs things that his Essence doesn't provide to achieve a certain outcome.<br /> <br /> Following the same thought thread, I'm also in favor of Mastery. The DB just can't achieve a certain outcome because that is not what their Essence is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:47:45-07:00","id":856280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856066#post856066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The flashiest high-Essence Charms are probably the kind of thing that produce iconic feats that people would tell stories about for generations, but in practical terms Solars are consistently going to come off as highly effective at asserting themselves through utilitarian application of their regular Charms from Essence 1 to 3. The might of the Solars is a holistic thing; you have to look at the sum of their parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's the bread-and-butter Essence 1-3 charms that will help you win fight, but it's the high Essence charms that the enemies will mention when they go on a &quot;Why Solar is dangerous&quot; rant.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think that due to how those charms tend to be the least &quot;discreet technique&quot;, it's the only kind of Solar power the enemies will be able to remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:02:11-07:00","id":856288,"title":"","content":"Yeah, half the melee charms are just going to remembered as &quot;they were really, really good at swordfighting&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, back to Immaculate styles. They could write them with a Mastery effect for Solars, which would be a straight &quot;get more successes&quot; or whatever, and an elemental benefit for DBs. Though that's perhaps too complex.<br /> <br /> I will say thought, that when, in 2nd ed, a Water Aspect Water Dragon Master fought a Solar Water Dragon Master... the Solar was better. Because a)they had better Martial Arts excellencies, b)they had more motes, and b)the cost of getting that entire style was only 2/3rds of the xp that it was for a Dragonblood, so presumably they had a bunch of other charms that might be useful too (for example, dodge charms, the charms for having extra motes, more ox-bodies, etc). And most of those things are definitely still true, and it wouldn't surprise me if the XP costs were still like that as well (not sure). I'm not worried about the fact that Immaculate charms work as well for DBs as they do for Solars means that DBs are as good as Solars, because they're still not. In fact, DB excellencies have been nerfed hard compared to 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:10:10-07:00","id":856292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856126#post856126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man this persistent fallacy/dismissal needs to diaf</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! Solars aren't everything in Exalted y'know! People keeping acting like they're this shonen anime hero who has their name in the title, y'know? like, as if they're Naruto and they are required to get the most amount of wins in the series, while all the other ninja get the shaft....because they're not Naruto, and no other reason. its really annoying. honestly, we need a thread for reasons why they DON'T win everything.... the game is called Exalted, not Solars.<br /> <br /> like y'know.being scattered, alone, having to build their own power structure, being really specialized, powerful individuals with larger than life personalities have this tendency to argue and fight with one another when they disagree, things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:05:09-07:00","id":856318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856292#post856292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed! Solars aren't everything in Exalted y'know! People keeping acting like they're this shonen anime hero who has their name in the title, y'know? like, as if they're Naruto and they are required to get the most amount of wins in the series, while all the other ninja get the shaft....because they're not Naruto, and no other reason. its really annoying. honestly, we need a thread for reasons why they DON'T win everything.... the game is called Exalted, not Solars.<br /> <br /> like y'know.being scattered, alone, having to build their own power structure, being really specialized, powerful individuals with larger than life personalities have this tendency to argue and fight with one another when they disagree, things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's saying that Solars always win.<br /> <br /> What <i>is </i>being said is that the system explicitly spells out that, in the Martial Arts rules, there is the Mastery keyword, which a Solar automatically gets access to, which adjusts the baseline effects of certain Martial Arts Charms to make them more powerful, because they're Solars, and they need these Charms to be more powerful to bring them into balance with native Solar Charms. There is also the Terrestrial keyword, which also makes an adjustment from the baseline Charm. In this case, the adjustment is <i>down,</i> to balance them with Dragon-Blooded Charm options.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded are not less heroic demigods than Solars, Lunars, or Sidereals. What they are is <b>explicitly</b> less individually powerful. That's why Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals continue to survive, and continue to be relevant, despite being, in total, outnumbered by Terrestrials <i>several hundred times over.</i><br /> <br /> So, please explain how you can justify, crunch or fluff, arguing that the Martial Arts system should invert itself for a handful of styles and make Dragon-Blooded the most powerful practitioners? How would this not have immense implications that turn the entire game upside down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":". 03-31-2016, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:31:09-07:00","id":856326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856280#post856280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's the bread-and-butter Essence 1-3 charms that will help you win fight, but it's the high Essence charms that the enemies will mention when they go on a &quot;Why Solar is dangerous&quot; rant.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think that due to how those charms tend to be the least &quot;discreet technique&quot;, it's the only kind of Solar power the enemies will be able to remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, although I don't think powers should necessarily crowd out achievements.<br /> <br /> When a Solar is infamous for sacking Nassau port without firing a single shot, it's probably something that would be conveyed in gameplay by a sequence of Charms that would not be overtly visible in-character. Still the kind of thing people take notice of.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:38:30-07:00","id":856327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856182#post856182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I sound radical and hyperbolic because that's sort of how I talk but, um, that's how it's been for two editions running. Solars haven't gotten to be better at Water Dragon just 'cuz Solar for, uh... a little under fourteen years now, and Immaculate Masters have been a match or huge trouble for Solars (even solars with Immaculate Martial Arts) ever since they were introduced. (Edit: 2e Fire Immaculates are actually <i>way</i> better, <i>leagues</i> better at Fire Dragon than Solars, because of how the charms key into their anima. Which I guess is sort of what you're advocating for, so, props.)<br /> <br /> Is your verisimilitude okay? Because it seems like it should want to quit boxing and open up a little deli if it's been getting hit in the face for fourteen years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this gets to the heart of a lot of this. The Immaculate Styles were *not* designed (by the Sidereals in universe or the Exalted 1st Edition designers out) to be just another martial art, with no special essence of its own, that is just a series of movements that naturally a Solar Exalted will be able to take to greater heights than a Dragonblooded Exalted, with Solar Essence. <br /> <br /> They're supposed to be Shaolin evoking secret, special styles in which the greatest mastery and fruits are unlocked by filling the techniques with elemental essence, which, well, the Dragonblooded have. While Solars do not have (and the Sidereals don't have, and the Lunars don't have, and....).<br /> <br /> This has had verisimilitude for a pretty long time!<br /> <br /> Now in practical terms, though, the only legitimate reason, for me, to care about whether Solars should get Mastery type effects for these styles, is whether Solars with a mortal Immaculates background have to take these styles for story reasons, and then should not be getting hosed relative to Solars who have a background where they've learned Heaven's Ladder or whatever as mortals.<br /> <br /> (That's sort of why I see that Mastery present in a way. So that players of Solars who take martial arts instead of Solar Charms, for story reasons that make sense, aren't unhappy. To make martial arts not a trap.).<br /> <br /> So for that reason<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856288#post856288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow, back to Immaculate styles. They could write them with a Mastery effect for Solars, which would be a straight &quot;get more successes&quot; or whatever, and an elemental benefit for DBs. Though that's perhaps too complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>though complex, would probably be the best compromise option. The Dragonblooded can access the greatest elemental mastery of the style, while the Solars can take only the mere &quot;surface&quot; movements, with their essence dead to the true pulse and heart of the style, but can do with those those movements what they do with all movements. Solars would be sort of using the styles in a way that would look technically horrible to a Sidereal sifu visualizing how a matching essence and excellence should come together to support the style, but it's still competitive with their other martial arts Charms, because there's enough for their excellence to get its foot in the door of the style and barge in there.<br /> <br /> (Although like all compromises, not necessarily satisfying to all parties by its nature, and if there's a better option, I'd like to hear it though.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:52:02-07:00","id":856331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856029#post856029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lmao x-tremeeeeeee hyperbole</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Consider the case of the Immaculate Grand Master. I think it's fair to assume that a Solar who has mastered all five Immaculate Styles is roughly comparable to a Solar who mastered all the Melee charms in the core. If a Dragon-Blooded Grand Master is just as good as the Solar Immaculate Grand Master then he's just as good as a maxed Solar Swordsman...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T01:01:23-07:00","id":856335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856133#post856133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would bet the intent is for even fewer Solars to have the opportunity to learn Water Dragon either - maybe one in the entirety of the setting, leaving individual tables aside (&quot;Solar Dynast&quot; trope aside, and I don't see the need to let you auto-activate latent Charms or w/e when you Exalt just because you bought the Ability dots in the Style hence learning the actual Charms as a Solar might be a problem).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Solars don't need a trainer for martial arts, so really any Solar could learn Water Dragon Style even if they don't even know the immaculate order exists. They just have to practice being like water and BAM, martial art style! The justification for learning those charms can literally be &quot;I wanted to fight by wreathing my fists in fire and punching people.&quot;. Er...well not for Water Dragon, obviously, but you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856100#post856100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm playing a Dragon-Blood I want to play an elementally empowered champion, and that's <i>absolutely</i> what I should be playing if that's my goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what you want to do then being a DB is a way easier way of doing that than a Solar. A Solar CAN do it, but they'd probably do it by getting, lets say fire is their element of choice, paired short daiklaves and light armor, all of red jade, and learning fire dragon style, pairing it with red jade evocations. They can do it, but it's hard and they have to take a fairly specific path. DBs can just learn DB melee, or athletics or something. Or maybe even other abilities but I'm not sure how well that's working out right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856292#post856292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like y'know.being scattered, alone, having to build their own power structure, being really specialized, powerful individuals with larger than life personalities have this tendency to argue and fight with one another when they disagree, things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, Solars also have great ways of overcoming those challenges. The infighting, not so much, but they build followers and power fast and easy.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, DBs are awesome! They're right up there with Solars and Abyssals in my favourite exalt splats*. But the thing is they're not awesome because they're powerful, part of what makes them awesome is that they kind of suck. Most of them might be decadent, corrupted, selfish, cowardly or cruel, but they come from a culture that praises duty, and a lot of them stick to that duty in spite of their lack of power. Some of them go out and face down anathema, or raksha, or Deathlords, and most of the time they die, but it doesn't stop the next group of heroes from fighting on. Hell, the MoW made a cloak out of the skinned hide of the Exalted defenders of Thorns, and I'm pretty sure all that did to some of the DB commanders in the Realm was make them more resolute about taking it back.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Solars are Doctor Who, DBs are Torchwood, or Brigadier Alistair Gordon Lethbridge-Stewart. If Solars are Space Marines, DBs are Imperial Guard. If Solars are the Avengers, DBs are the shield agents. If Solars are the Jedi generals DBs are the clone commandos. Asking why DBs don't get to be as good at Fire Dragon as a Solar is like asking why republic crack pilots can't fly a starfighter as well as the trained Jedi pilots. Their position in the narrative just doesn't support it. It doesn't mean they're not cool, or can't do great things, but they don't have the Force, and when a Force user focuses and applies that to their already considerable skill in piloting, it goes beyond mortal limits.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to start taking about Solars always getting one over on Sids or Lunars, then yeah that's a conversation there. There should definitely be times where a Lunar pulls something off and makes a Solar go &quot;Damn I wish I could do that.&quot; or a Sid does something that leaves a Solar wondering &quot;wtf even happened there?&quot;.<br /> <br /> *Sids and Lunars are wonderful, but I've just never gotten super into them and Alchemicals aren't part of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:08:24-07:00","id":856345,"title":"","content":"......question.<br /> <br /> if their narrative importance is minion, then why aren't they serving the Celestial Exalts?<br /> <br /> Because the whole spiel about DB's being that would make a lot more sense if they actually fulfilled that place in the narrative. if Solars were the big heroes doing all the big world-saving stuff and the DB's were serving them and having their own little stories that are focused on while the Celestial Exalts serve as big background pieces.....you'd be right.<br /> <br /> except. they don't. they are their own splat. the Sidereals don't entirely control them, they only pull the strings from shadows and there is only so much you can control in secret. the DB's are all controlling themselves, mostly. Mostly because they murdered the people whose narrative is &quot;the hero who wins&quot; and took their place as rulers. the &quot;wise old mentor&quot; narrative meanwhile got broken when the Sidereals stopped advising and teaching and went full treacherous betrayer on them. just like the Solars stopped being the heroes who win when they started being corrupt, decadent god-kings who didn't listen to anybody.<br /> <br /> so. all the Exalts pretty much broke their narrative role during the Usurpation. and haven't really adhered to them since. so. screw narrative roles? because they kinda died the moment the Hero stopped winning, the Mooks won and the Mentor lived to fight another day. so trying to adhere to said role when said roles are dead are kind of nonsensical. especially when your entire setting is kind of built on those roles being broken. <br /> <br /> so Dragon-Blooded aren't really in that narrative role, because they haven't been for thousands of years. Their narrative role has been &quot;new rulers of the world&quot; for quite some time now, and if they found out the Sidereal conspiracy, I don't think they'd be happy about it. I think they'd pretty much rebel on their own because of it. so no. that is not really their narrative role. because that was the role they played back in the First Age, they are their own Exalt now and kind of really important all by themselves. We should really stop judging everything on First Age views of narrative importance. Kind of outdated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:45:14-07:00","id":856355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856345#post856345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">......question.<br /> <br /> if their narrative importance is minion, then why aren't they serving the Celestial Exalts?<br /> <br /> Because the whole spiel about DB's being that would make a lot more sense if they actually fulfilled that place in the narrative. if Solars were the big heroes doing all the big world-saving stuff and the DB's were serving them and having their own little stories that are focused on while the Celestial Exalts serve as big background pieces.....you'd be right.<br /> <br /> except. they don't. they are their own splat. the Sidereals don't entirely control them, they only pull the strings from shadows and there is only so much you can control in secret. the DB's are all controlling themselves, mostly. Mostly because they murdered the people whose narrative is &quot;the hero who wins&quot; and took their place as rulers. the &quot;wise old mentor&quot; narrative meanwhile got broken when the Sidereals stopped advising and teaching and went full treacherous betrayer on them. just like the Solars stopped being the heroes who win when they started being corrupt, decadent god-kings who didn't listen to anybody.<br /> <br /> so. all the Exalts pretty much broke their narrative role during the Usurpation. and haven't really adhered to them since. so. screw narrative roles? because they kinda died the moment the Hero stopped winning, the Mooks won and the Mentor lived to fight another day. so trying to adhere to said role when said roles are dead are kind of nonsensical. especially when your entire setting is kind of built on those roles being broken.<br /> <br /> so Dragon-Blooded aren't really in that narrative role, because they haven't been for thousands of years. Their narrative role has been &quot;new rulers of the world&quot; for quite some time now, and if they found out the Sidereal conspiracy, I don't think they'd be happy about it. I think they'd pretty much rebel on their own because of it. so no. that is not really their narrative role. because that was the role they played back in the First Age, they are their own Exalt now and kind of really important all by themselves. We should really stop judging everything on First Age views of narrative importance. Kind of outdated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing an important point. The Dragon Blooded Host as a whole is an almost unstoppable force. On the other hand, a single dragon blooded is not so much. If you match their personal power to a celestial, all setting loses it coherence, and meaning, let alone a solar.<br /> <br /> Why would the dragon blooded had to go all the trouble of the usurpation, when a 2-3 DB per solar could have done the job while rest of the 9000+ DB eat their popcorn and cheered?.<br /> <br /> Why bother with a jade prison when you can make these matches as a League of Solar Bashing, in an arena next to you this weekend! You can keep the dawns as premier matches since they can actually present a challenge abit.<br /> <br /> The entire sociality of DB, is based upon unity and strength in numbers. They have great and compelling stories involving that theme. They are not Solars painted in fire/earth/water.<br /> <br /> When you give too much personal power to the DB, or reduce a solar's power, the whole setting collapses, as nothing that happened in the past would make sense.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:50:35-07:00","id":856357,"title":"","content":"DBs are the weakest of the Exalted, but they aren't minions. They're Captain America, not generic SHIELD agents, but they're also not Thor or the Hulk. Portraying them as wussy faceless mooks messes with the setting just as much as making them Solar-tier does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:57:16-07:00","id":856360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856335#post856335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Solars don't need a trainer for martial arts, so really any Solar could learn Water Dragon Style even if they don't even know the immaculate order exists. They just have to practice being like water and BAM, martial art style! The justification for learning those charms can literally be &quot;I wanted to fight by wreathing my fists in fire and punching people.&quot;. Er...well not for Water Dragon, obviously, but you know what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's true. I think you do have to learn a style, not just make it up. You don't need a trainer for all the charms necessarily, those are expressions of the style, but you do need a trainer for learning the Water Dragon Style ability. Same with Tiger, Snake, etc.<br /> I think.<br /> It's kind of important thematically. If you just keep punching so hard that your fists burnt into golden fire... that's Solar Brawl.<br /> <br /> (Also, Water Dragon Style is emulating the Water Dragon, not Water. Though obviously that's not all that different)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> The most important thing is I need Immaculate Styles to be competitive so I can have my 5 PCs match up with 5 Immaculates and it actually be a decent fight rather than just wiping the floor with them. I need the Wyld Hunt to be a boss fight, not a mid-level encounter.<br /> (Obviously the PCs are still going to win. They've got Solar excellencies, bigger mote pools, more charms because their charms are cheaper, etc. And they're being run by 5 players who can think about what they're doing much better than I can with my 5 characters that I'm not so familiar with.)<br /> <br /> <br /> One final thing I'd point out. Look at the Immaculate style charms in the back of the Core. How do they match up to other martial arts? How do they match up to Terrestrial styles?<br /> They're clearly better than Dragonblooded charms. Not sure if they're as good as Mastery effects though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:17:38-07:00","id":856365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856182#post856182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, really?<br /> <br /> I mean, I sound radical and hyperbolic because that's sort of how I talk but, um, that's how it's been for two editions running. Solars haven't gotten to be better at Water Dragon just 'cuz Solar for, uh... a little under fourteen years now, and Immaculate Masters have been a match or huge trouble for Solars (even solars with Immaculate Martial Arts) ever since they were introduced. (Edit: 2e Fire Immaculates are actually <i>way</i> better, <i>leagues</i> better at Fire Dragon than Solars, because of how the charms key into their anima. Which I guess is sort of what you're advocating for, so, props.)<br /> <br /> Is your verisimilitude okay? Because it seems like it should want to quit boxing and open up a little deli if it's been getting hit in the face for fourteen years.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's untrue. For every practical definition of better, a Solar Immaculate Stylist was better than a DB Immaculate Stylist. The Solar had a higher dice cap, bigger mote pool, and much higher survivability thanks to his superior (or downright broken, depending on who you ask) native Dodge and Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> This was in a game that stated outright in the core that a Solar is limiting himself by pursuing MA over his native Charms. In 3e, the Mastery keyword exists specifically to offset that and bring MA Charms roughly on par with Solar Charms when used by a Solar. That's because Solars are supposed to be peerless masters of every Ability, and MA is an Ability. The idea that this won't be the case with Immaculate Styles is a delusion born from the misapplied sense of niche protection and a gross exaggeration of the Immaculate Monks' narrative place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:00:59-07:00","id":856386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to assume that a Solar who has mastered all five Immaculate Styles is roughly comparable to a Solar who mastered all the Melee charms in the core</div> </div> </div> </div> Do people expect Immaculate Martial Arts to work anything like the Martial Arts we already have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:14:07-07:00","id":856422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856386#post856386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do people expect Immaculate Martial Arts to work anything like the Martial Arts we already have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect them to work exactly like the styles we have, plus perhaps some special bonus for DBs learning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:20:46-07:00","id":856455,"title":"","content":"Okay, so...a few thoughts here.<br /> <br /> 1: DBs should continue to be, alone, weaker than an equivalent Solar. However...if the Wyld Hunt comes for a Solar, they won't be equivalent and they won't be fighting one on one. They know how scary Anathema can be, and you are going to get hit by a significant number of DBs, many of whom are older and more experienced than you. That's kinda always been their whole thing...not a huge threat to a Celestial when alone, but absolutely terrifying enmasse. (And I hope we see a decent number of DB charms that synergize with the charms of other DBs...kinda tying together the fact that their greatest power is when they work together). One of my most memorable moments as a ST was the first time my players had a run in with the Wyld Hunt. They were like 'Oh, they are just Dragonblooded' and joined battle. It did not end well for my players...2 ended up incapacitated, and the other 3 ended up burning Essence like crazy trying to get away...they managed, but all invested in escape charms immediately thereafter and resolved to be a <b>lot </b>more careful about bringing the Shaolin Death Squads down on their heads. Even rumors of the Wyld Hunt were enough to send them scurrying away.<br /> <br /> 2: As has been mentioned, the Immaculate Styles were specifically designed for the Terrestrials, to give them enough umph to take on rogue gods (really, that was the original intent...they were created during a time when the Solars were mostly locked away and the Lunars were in hiding). I'm not sure how to handle the initiation into the styles...but the simplest solution is that those styles simply do not have Terrestrial limitations on them...and some charms may work better for a terrestrial as it makes use of their elemental anima. I mean, if you are designing a martial art for the Terrestrials, why would you design an art for them that they couldn't actually wield freely?<br /> <br /> 3: So, back to the OP...<br /> <br /> Solars are generally rated as the 'most powerful' because of Mastery, because of their Supernal, because they get access to the best Sorcery, because they have lower XP costs (and thus develop faster), and because they have a bigger Essence Pool and more efficient/effective Charms. In short, Solars are generally considered the most powerful because they can just face a problem and bulldoze their way through it with raw power.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that they will always be the ideal choice for a situation though. Solars tend to be the 'brute force solutions' type of powerhouse, and have a tendency to specialize towards being really good at only a few roles...their ability spread is a good indication of this. The other splats tend to be good at other sorts of solutions. (Note: what follows is more going off of flavor/lore, and thus how I hope the splats will be written for 3E...rather than how they have necessarily been written in the past.) Lunars are ridiculously adaptable and can change themselves to suit a situation as it develops...they are generally the most 'multi-purpose' of the splats. Siddies are the best at long term thinking and planning, because they can literally look ahead, and modify destinies to make their plans happen...and solve most of their problems by cheating. (An actually good example of Siddie cheating is how their Perfect Dodge worked. A Solar's perfect is either a flawless parry, or turning themselves invulnerable, or impossibly dodging...a Siddie's perfect was basically them just saying &quot;Nope, you missed. No, I <i>don't</i> care that you saw your sword hit me in the throat...you missed.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:02:25-07:00","id":856480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856455#post856455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to handle the initiation into the styles...but the simplest solution is that those styles simply do not have Terrestrial limitations on them...and some charms may work better for a terrestrial as it makes use of their elemental anima. I mean, if you are designing a martial art for the Terrestrials, why would you design an art for them that they couldn't actually wield freely?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not designing them for Terrestrials, though. You're designing them for a dedicated sect of Terrestrial warrior-monks who undergo a hellish training regimen so they can transcend the normal limits of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Under the 3e paradigm of Martial Arts, it makes no sense whatsoever for Immaculate Styles to stray from the norm. They're gonna have a Terrestrial keyword for DBs using them, and a Mastery keyword for Solars and Sidereals using them, and the Immaculate Monks will get either a Charm or a Merit that lets them ignore the Terrestrial keyword on MA Charms. They may also get some special benefit, just like they used to get bonuses for wielding style weapons in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:41:53-07:00","id":856501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856365#post856365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For every practical definition of better, a Solar Immaculate Stylist was better than a DB Immaculate Stylist. The Solar had a higher dice cap, bigger mote pool, and much higher survivability thanks to his superior (or downright broken, depending on who you ask) native Dodge and Resistance Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. The Water Dragon Solar is better than the Water Immaculate in the same way that an Eclipse is better than a Sidereal at Sidereal Martial Arts - he can match the technique, and then has a better supporting skillset on top of that.<br /> <br /> I would actually be stoked if Immaculate MA had no Mastery effects but a number of effects that synergized with the Terrestrial anima, in much the same way as... well, here.<br /> <br /> Lunar: &quot;This martial art has been designed from the ground up and through long study and struggle to be used in the form of a giant snake. Intimidate with your rattle or hood, constrict your enemy with your coils - literal coils, by the way, and enhance your natural venoms. I call it... The Real Slim Snakey Style.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;But... I don't understand. I don't have a rattle, or a hood, or coils, or natural venom.&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;Yes, that's the point.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;I can't use any of those techniques with anything approaching effectiveness.&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;<i>Yes, that's the point.</i>&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;B-b-but, h-how can I be better than you at it?&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;You can't. It's not <i>for</i> you.&quot;<br /> Solar: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ociMBfkDG1w\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;But usually everything is!&quot;</a><br /> Lunar: &quot;Well, this isn't.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;*uncontrollable sobbing* B-but my cock is huuu-&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;Oh shut up and kick my ass with Snake Style instead, you big baby.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-31-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:09:38-07:00","id":856518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect them to work exactly like the styles we have, plus perhaps some special bonus for DBs learning it.</div> </div> </div> </div> So probably not really equivalent to a full Solar combat Ability. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not for you</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think you're really proving anything when you make something up specifically to exclude Solars that isn't really following the conventions of the system in the first place. I mean, is this a thing worth having in its own right, or just to make an elaborate point about Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:19:18-07:00","id":856525,"title":"","content":"@Guancyto<br /> <br /> That would not be a Martial Art, which in Exalted's definition consists of techniques which use a human physiology to perform. What you got are custom snake themed whatever attribute Lunar Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:20:59-07:00","id":856529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856357#post856357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs are the weakest of the Exalted, but they aren't minions. They're Captain America, not generic SHIELD agents, but they're also not Thor or the Hulk. Portraying them as wussy faceless mooks messes with the setting just as much as making them Solar-tier does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic agents of SHIELD, not very often. Sometimes, but not super often. They're more like Agent Phil Coulson. Republic Commandos and Torchwood were probably better examples. Especially since both of those groups have times when they interact with the Jedi and the Doctor, and each time it's usually incredible.<br /> <br /> Like just look at <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ss1nFJC197M\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>clip from Clone Wars, those jetpack troopers and maybe commander Cody are kind of filling the DB role here. Not the random rank-and-file troopers but the elite backup for the dude who leaped off a 10 story building onto a mech and started deflecting tank mounted weapons fire with his laser sword. Okay, so now <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_rWciV_WBh8?t=370\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is what a bit of the story looks like when there's not a Solar around. They're not mooks, but in a scene that's got the most powerful people in the setting in it, that fact can get missed a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856360#post856360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway.<br /> The most important thing is I need Immaculate Styles to be competitive so I can have my 5 PCs match up with 5 Immaculates and it actually be a decent fight rather than just wiping the floor with them. I need the Wyld Hunt to be a boss fight, not a mid-level encounter.<br /> (Obviously the PCs are still going to win. They've got Solar excellencies, bigger mote pools, more charms because their charms are cheaper, etc. And they're being run by 5 players who can think about what they're doing much better than I can with my 5 characters that I'm not so familiar with.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you've got 5 PCs vs 5 immaculate masters in combat that shouldn't be too hard. 4/5th of the party aren't dawns, and while a Dawn can take 2 Immaculate masters easy, an immaculate master might be able to take both your Twilight AND Eclipse at once if they're not super invested into combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856360#post856360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One final thing I'd point out. Look at the Immaculate style charms in the back of the Core. How do they match up to other martial arts? How do they match up to Terrestrial styles?<br /> They're clearly better than Dragonblooded charms. Not sure if they're as good as Mastery effects though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually has an explanation, also an explanation for why the DB charms seem so damn good. Basically the antagonists in the antagonist chapters are supposed to be scary enough to pose whatever kind of threat they're supposed to. So a young DB is scary to a newly exalted, non-combat character, a Lunar warlord is scary to a lone warrior, ect. The thing is, they've got 3-5 charms to do that in, when the Solars have 15-20. The QCs HAVE to have charms far and above what their splat will get in their book because that one soak booster the DBs get is trying to make up for their entire resistance tree. Hammer on Iron is so good because it's basically the only melee charm they've got. You can't pick one Solar melee charm and say &quot;Well if you've got that you're basically as good as any Solar sword master.&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> Same goes for the immaculate MA's. Avenging Wind Strike, for example, is not going to be in the DB book anywhere. That charm is good. Damn, damn good, way way too good, even if it can't be comboed with any other charms, which it can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:24:32-07:00","id":856533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856518#post856518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you're really proving anything when you make something up specifically to exclude Solars that isn't really following the conventions of the system in the first place. I mean, is this a thing worth having in its own right, or just to make an elaborate point about Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely not proving anything (at least until someone comes in to say &quot;no a Solar should totally be better than a Lunar at that too&quot;). More like, providing an illustration of my viewpoint in a marginally more entertaining way than a wall of text?<br /> <br /> And shit yeah I'd make a martial art that was specifically designed to be used in the form of a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AEsOok-mJZg\" target=\"_blank\">mothafuckin' T-Rex</a>. (Probably not a giant snake though; turning into one never helps.)<br /> <br /> (Also, yes, I know that they made the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LxXjsQbCZR8\" target=\"_blank\">Cow Fu clip</a> impossible in 3e by redefining Martial Arts. What an udderly tiresome decision that was.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:45:03-07:00","id":856543,"title":"","content":"How is there going to be meaningful engagement on something that has a flawed premise?<br /> <br /> There is no way a Solar can be better than a Lunar in that because what you presented is not a Martial Art Ability, or any Ability whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Solars are masters of Abilities. If anything could be achieved through enough mastery of an Ability a Solar should be able to do it.<br /> <br /> If it isn't an Ability in the first place there is nothing to talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:59:07-07:00","id":856552,"title":"","content":"How is it a flawed argument, and how is codified fighting based on forms and katas not an Ability by virtue of those forms and katas being based on nonhuman physiology? <br /> <br /> If a beastman with boneless tentacles for limbs develops a fighting style based on the kind of things you can do with complete freedom of jointless movement, why can't that be a Martial Art? How is it not an ability? If it's something he could set up a school for and teach to other boneless limbed creatures, what separates it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:01:02-07:00","id":856555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856525#post856525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Guancyto<br /> <br /> That would not be a Martial Art, which in Exalted's definition consists of techniques which use a human physiology to perform. What you got are custom snake themed whatever attribute Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not. Every style is an arbitrary collection of some holistic concept in general, perhaps for humans, or perhaps not. Certainly, all of the published styles are for the human body, but that doesn't really restrict future hypotheticals, especially if some of the Autochthonian styles teased for Alchemicals carry over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:06:27-07:00","id":856560,"title":"","content":"Not every fighting technique is a Martial Art, even if they are &quot;martial arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> This discussed and hotly debated with people disappointed that teaching Black Claw to their tyrant lizard pet is a non canon thing.<br /> <br /> For it to be a Martial Art in the sense that aligns with the mechanical Ability it has to respect that restraint. There should be no Martial Art a Solar or a Sidereal shouldn't be able to master.<br /> <br /> Though there can be many &quot;martial arts&quot;. But mechanically those will be only fluffed Brawl, Melee, Archery, Thrown and Dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:21:24-07:00","id":856573,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest that the importance of Immaculate Styles was blown out of proportion in 2e, where the DBs were weak as fuck on their own and Celestials could just lolnope everything coming at them at negligible cost, making DB players cling to that extra sliver of power they got by initiating into Immaculate Styles.<br /> <br /> I'd further suggest this is not something we want replicated in 3e. Myself, I want a DB Charmset that's good, well-rounded and fun to play, and Immaculate Styles that are powerful, but not so much so that they make their native combat Charms into trap options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:44:45-07:00","id":856586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856573#post856573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest that the importance of Immaculate Styles was blown out of proportion in 2e, where the DBs were weak as fuck on their own and Celestials could just lolnope everything coming at them at negligible cost, making DB players cling to that extra sliver of power they got by initiating into Immaculate Styles.<br /> <br /> I'd further suggest this is not something we want replicated in 3e. Myself, I want a DB Charmset that's good, well-rounded and fun to play, and Immaculate Styles that are powerful, but not so much so that they make their native combat Charms into trap options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly i'm not looking for them to be stronger than solars, i'm looking for it to resonate with them in a way that even when a solar masters it, he will look at the dragon blood and be like &quot;but i can't resonate with it like he can.&quot; whether it supplements anima, or things like that (Example was Fire Dragon in 2e where a non DB could get a terrestrial anima, but a fire aspect had theirs tripled in power)<br /> <br /> And to an earlier quote, yes i do have a problem with it being &quot;the sidereals made this for you, go play&quot; because it again implies the dragon blooded couldn't even do that on their own. The previous edition made it very clear that every terrestrial success was because a celestial did something for them. That is something that needs to go. The concept that you must be THIS exalted to innovate is a problem. <br /> <br /> It's like with craft, I don't want dragon bloods to be able to become artifact factories like solars, but a dragon blood, or even a circle should be able to with enough blood, sweat, and care, be able to produce a legendary item. It may take them longer, it may wind up enduring failure after failure, heck it may be something that requires multiple generations, but I want to be able to see something truly legendary come out of them. And I have this funny feeling that story wise this would feel even more awesome that a solar just farting em out every tuesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:50:03-07:00","id":856592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856357#post856357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs are the weakest of the Exalted, but they aren't minions. They're Captain America, not generic SHIELD agents, but they're also not Thor or the Hulk. Portraying them as wussy faceless mooks messes with the setting just as much as making them Solar-tier does.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your comparison has merit, there is a very real sense where Solars are Captain America, and the other Exalted are things like Thor and the Hulk. He very much describes the Zenith Solar Archetype, in all ways, there. See, the old Marvel SAGA RPG had a stat that existed to explain why Captain America is a solar. Their example of it was 'Imagine you have Venom and Captain America. Venom has an alien symbiote which makes him resilient as a tank, able to camouflage, strong enough to throw cars effortlessly and able to create tendrils. Cap is slightly superhuman and has a shield. You'd think them fighting was a no-brainer, but if you read comics, you'd know to vote on Cap!', and then goes on to describe the Edge stat, which was basically Badassdom (and which Cap had at its highest.)<br /> <br /> Solars draw from the human hero, the Dragonslayer, which goes, 1. The Dragonslayer will kill the Dragon, and 2. That is impressive because he is just a man, while the Dragon is an enormous engine of destruction able to melt metal and bring down armies. When you see a Solar fighting a DB, the Solar tends to appear weaker, most of the time. There is one guy shooting fire from his hands, becoming an elemental bonfire of destruction, raising the earth or bringing down lightning! And another, who... going by Second Age conventions, may as well be a peasant holding the chair leg of truth. And much like the cap example, you know to bet on the peasant in rags holding the chair leg of truth, because of what Solar power emulates: he will be faster, better, more precise, and just last longer than the juggernaut of elemental destruction.<br /> <br /> Going from there to the title of the thread, Solars are the most powerful because they are just able to DO better, but it is very much an intentional thing that they look somewhat unassuming doing it,whereas Sidereals and Lunars and Abyssals have powers meant to make you look and go '... OK, now that is just plain unfair.' Solars will likely win, but they cannot turn into a T-Rex, summon elemental dragons, rise all the dead on both sides as vengeful wraiths, or any other sort of power that really, half exists to just be that damn _impressive_.<br /> <br /> If the other Exalted do not come off as incredibly impressive and puissant, Exalted has failed. If the Solars cannot overcome them, then Exalted has failed, as they are the weaponized narrative of the human hero, who conquers the strange, the natural, the feral, and death itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:07:04-07:00","id":856604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=855796#post855796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Solars got a big buff in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree. Ex3 gave them a few new pop-off-the-page charms, but note that their workhorse superpowers were often nerfed. EotUCS, for instance, is now an instant charm rather than scenelong; and of course the big searchlight-eyes thing, while it looks powerful, is a lot weaker than 2e's &quot;you automatically see through everything for the rest of the scene fullstop.&quot; In 2e, you could just put up EotUCS and be totally immune to an entire category of strategies for the entire scene; if someone's build was focused entirely on combat illusions, their options were to run away or to die. 3e EotUCS is more like a super-move -- it'd be devastating to the illusion-guy in the one moment you use it, but it's not shutting him down for the entire scene.<br /> <br /> Other things are similar; there's a lot of powerful-looking charms, but fewer scenelong &quot;I win automatically for free&quot; powers. In particular, while the removal of IAM affects everyone, it hits Solar(oids) the hardest, because they have the largest dice pools -- in 2e, a Solar fighting DBs or Mortals could just max out their dice cap with IAM, at which point they had no reasonable chance of being hit without the enemy using charms and would hit nearly automatically with every attack. In 3e, a Solar has to actually spend motes to press their full advantage over a DB (or even a mortal!) And that's without getting into the removal of 2e-style perfects and paranoia combat, which, again, favored Solars due to them having the best perfects by far.<br /> <br /> A lot of the new &quot;pop-off-the-page powerful&quot; charms, meanwhile, are things that will maybe come up once a story, if that; God-King's Shrike or Soul Reprisal or Dual Magnus Prana are hardly going to come up every session the way the old scenelong buffs and perfects sometimes did.<br /> <br /> (Of course, Solars still generally have the best workhorse charms in many areas, but the structure of the game is no longer one where the default implementation of that kind of power is &quot;I activate Persistent Invulnerability Suite, I win.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:16:15-07:00","id":856607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856560#post856560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every fighting technique is a Martial Art, even if they are &quot;martial arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> This discussed and hotly debated with people disappointed that teaching Black Claw to their tyrant lizard pet is a non canon thing.<br /> <br /> For it to be a Martial Art in the sense that aligns with the mechanical Ability it has to respect that restraint. There should be no Martial Art a Solar or a Sidereal shouldn't be able to master.<br /> <br /> Though there can be many &quot;martial arts&quot;. But mechanically those will be only fluffed Brawl, Melee, Archery, Thrown and Dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern Spider Touch can probably enable the capacity to practice those styles, so it can all work out in the end. Just beware the lack of an easily flipped switch in comparison to Lunars, Alchemicals and what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:18:02-07:00","id":856609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856586#post856586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly i'm not looking for them to be stronger than solars, i'm looking for it to resonate with them in a way that even when a solar masters it, he will look at the dragon blood and be like &quot;but i can't resonate with it like he can.&quot; whether it supplements anima, or things like that (Example was Fire Dragon in 2e where a non DB could get a terrestrial anima, but a fire aspect had theirs tripled in power)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt that there will be some benefit to the Dragon-Blooded for mastering an elemental Martial Art. I <i>severely</i> doubt that, given the way that the Martial Arts system works and the nature of the Mastery keyword, a Solar who masters the style will feel in any way inadequate compared to the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856586#post856586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to an earlier quote, yes i do have a problem with it being &quot;the sidereals made this for you, go play&quot; because it again implies the dragon blooded couldn't even do that on their own. The previous edition made it very clear that every terrestrial success was because a celestial did something for them. That is something that needs to go. The concept that you must be THIS exalted to innovate is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you'll recall, in previous editions, the Immaculate Martial Arts were Celestial styles - a level to which Dragon-Blooded couldn't even aspire, ordinarily. I assume that you're also miffed that Dragon-Blooded can't learn Solar Circle Sorcery? The argument you're making applies to that, also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856586#post856586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like with craft, I don't want dragon bloods to be able to become artifact factories like solars, but a dragon blood, or even a circle should be able to with enough blood, sweat, and care, be able to produce a legendary item. It may take them longer, it may wind up enduring failure after failure, heck it may be something that requires multiple generations, but I want to be able to see something truly legendary come out of them. And I have this funny feeling that story wise this would feel even more awesome that a solar just farting em out every tuesday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there a story in the book about a Dragon-Blooded completing a daiklaive that an ancestor had started, building on a trophy claimed in battle?<br /> <br /> As I recall it - haven't looked at that section for a while - the base Crafting system allows for the crafting of great wonders. The Charms just make that easier. It seems likely that the Dragon-Blooded will be able to create great wonders, with the right investment, because that ability is built right into the system. Their Charms will just put their own unique spin on the process. This is not really equivalent to the Martial Arts or Sorcery systems, which limit the Dragon-Blooded or exclude them beyond a specific point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:49:24-07:00","id":856628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856609#post856609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you'll recall, in previous editions, the Immaculate Martial Arts were Celestial styles - a level to which Dragon-Blooded couldn't even aspire, ordinarily. I assume that you're also miffed that Dragon-Blooded can't learn Solar Circle Sorcery? The argument you're making applies to that, also.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Solar circle sorcery i'm perfectly ok with being solar level jams. Maybe they find a ritual that lets them briefly touch the celestial pedestal and learn a single spell from it perhaps, but nah. Sorcery I'm ok with since Sorcery already is breaking limitations.<br /> <br /> And given now that they can learn the charms without celestial help (The terrestrial keyword is actually wonderful for this now). Let them be the ones who transcend their own limitations in it. &quot;A sidereal did it&quot; is a weak reason for it. It once again falls back to &quot;big brother/sister has to take care of it for you&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856609#post856609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a story in the book about a Dragon-Blooded completing a daiklaive that an ancestor had started, building on a trophy claimed in battle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got dropped to a 3 dot artifact, and they removed that generational aspect of the story. Personally that latter part made me sad cause i think its an awesome artifact and that whole taking hundreds of years to make was cool to me.<br /> <br /> I'm talking N/A. the type of thing that should be the central aspect of a story for a dragon blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","user":"Kell_Tamer","date":". 03-31-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:54:12-07:00","id":856633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856592#post856592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars draw from the human hero, the Dragonslayer, which goes, 1. The Dragonslayer will kill the Dragon, and 2. That is impressive because he is just a man, while the Dragon is an enormous engine of destruction able to melt metal and bring down armies. When you see a Solar fighting a DB, the Solar tends to appear weaker, most of the time. There is one guy shooting fire from his hands, becoming an elemental bonfire of destruction, raising the earth or bringing down lightning! And another, who... going by Second Age conventions, may as well be a peasant holding the chair leg of truth. And much like the cap example, you know to bet on the peasant in rags holding the chair leg of truth, because of what Solar power emulates: he will be faster, better, more precise, and just last longer than the juggernaut of elemental destruction.<br /> <br /> Going from there to the title of the thread, Solars are the most powerful because they are just able to DO better, but it is very much an intentional thing that they look somewhat unassuming doing it,whereas Sidereals and Lunars and Abyssals have powers meant to make you look and go '... OK, now that is just plain unfair.' Solars will likely win, but they cannot turn into a T-Rex, summon elemental dragons, rise all the dead on both sides as vengeful wraiths, or any other sort of power that really, half exists to just be that damn _impressive_.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Solars can be unassuming to an extent. If you work at it. It just is work because...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, their fighting style (to the extent there is a single one) is probably characterized by an implausible degree of superspeed and superstrength, they pop lightshows like nobody's business with their animas and wave around sharpened surfboards for weapons. They throw around the mightiest evocations, Glorious Solar Saber, Solar Circle Sorcery. Flow Like Blood gives them (at least in 1e and 2e Charm text) straight up teleportation out of the way if they can't make a dodge. They transmute their skin into bronze to block attacks. They do sword beams.<br /> <br /> Generally, yes, true they do not throw around elemental power or beast shapes. Just, like if David and Goliath is the analogy, they're Goliath. More akin in their style to the still-human-but-an-enormous-freakishly-strong-giant than the simple shepherd boy, who happened to cunningly spot a weakness in his enemy and whose shot was guided by God.<br /> <br /> Or another way, it's not so much like the Dragon vs the simple village warrior turned plucky Dragonslayer, and with cunning he can pull out teh win. It's like the Dragon vs high level Cloud bloody Strife. (And in that match up you could be like &quot;Ah, poor dragon, facing such a mighty supernatural enemy. I'm rooting for an underdog like you, Dragon-senpai!&quot;)&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are, ridiculously, blatantly, supernatural. (Unless you specifically make the effort to walk away from the powers they have which aren't. Which.... you can sort of do that with most Exalted). And that's OK. That's why many (most?) people where attracted to the Solar Exalted in the first place. Just kind of... own it... don't let's be like they're summoning angelic swords of light and teleporting out the way of attacks and throwing house sized boulders around and running at the speed of sound and stuff and then giving you a look that say &quot;Me? I'm just an unassuming guy who's no stronger than Conan. Just really clever in a fight. Nothing supernatural to see here.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:17:11-07:00","id":856681,"title":"","content":"Guancyto, please stop with the penis talk. It makes it hard to take this conversation seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856609#post856609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall it - haven't looked at that section for a while - the base Crafting system allows for the crafting of great wonders. The Charms just make that easier. It seems likely that the Dragon-Blooded will be able to create great wonders, with the right investment, because that ability is built right into the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You need to get 100 threshold successes in six rolls against difficulty 5 to make a 5-dot Artifact. So your ability to make greater wonders depends entirely upon your access to roll-boosting Charms.<br /> <br /> An Essence 1 DB with max stats and an exceptional tool using a full excellency and spending 2wp rolls 18 dice, rerolls 1 failure, and adds 1 success. On average, they'll get 10.5 successes per roll. That's just barely enough to make a 2-dot Artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:29:56-07:00","id":856689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856633#post856633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, yes, true they do not throw around elemental power or beast shapes. Just, like if David and Goliath is the analogy, they're Goliath. More akin in their style to the still-human-but-an-enormous-freakishly-strong-giant than the simple shepherd boy, who happened to cunningly spot a weakness in his enemy and whose shot was guided by God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your description of David is literally a Solar. His name' s Elias Tremalion. He has a sling. And is an unassuming hero.<br /> <br /> So no, that is not what Solars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:34:19-07:00","id":856691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856455#post856455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: As has been mentioned, the Immaculate Styles were specifically designed for the Terrestrials, to give them enough umph to take on rogue gods (really, that was the original intent...they were created during a time when the Solars were mostly locked away and the Lunars were in hiding). I'm not sure how to handle the initiation into the styles...but the simplest solution is that those styles simply do not have Terrestrial limitations on them...and some charms may work better for a terrestrial as it makes use of their elemental anima. I mean, if you are designing a martial art for the Terrestrials, why would you design an art for them that they couldn't actually wield freely?</div> </div> </div> </div>You obviously wouldn't have an Immaculate style with whole charms that can't be accessed by DBs, because having disecrete techniques they can't use would indeed not make sense. But that's not what the Terrestrial keyword is. They don't represent extra-special things that only Celestials can do, they represent what happens when someone with more raw supernatural power uses a certain technique. A Solar using the same MA charm as a DB gets benefits because the Solar executes that technique with far more skill than the DB does; there's no way to make a martial art style that can't be used in a skillful way, and there's definitely no way to make a martial art that powers up its uses to a Celestial/Solar level of proficiency. That's like saying that a daiklave specifically forged for a Terrestrial should allow them to learn and use Solar melee charms through it, because why would they be stuck with Terrestrial charms if it was their own sword?<br /> <br /> Also, removing the Terrestrial keyword from all Immaculate styles doesn't make Immaculate martial artists better, it makes them pointless. The whole schtick of the Immaculate martial artists is that they can ignore Terrestrial limitations, if the primary martial art of the Dragon-Blooded doesn't even have those limitations then why bother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856592#post856592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While your comparison has merit, there is a very real sense where Solars are Captain America, and the other Exalted are things like Thor and the Hulk. He very much describes the Zenith Solar Archetype, in all ways, there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, definitely. Cap oozes Zenith in every way. I was only referring to power levels there, where Cap is clearly incredible in a way that no mere mortal could accomplish, but at the same time is clearly outclassed by the heavier hitters of the setting. Any time he does manage to beat Thor or the Hulk will be a triumph of the plucky underdog over a superior foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 03-31-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:55:17-07:00","id":856702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856689#post856689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your description of David is literally a Solar. His name' s Elias Tremalion. He has a sling. And is an unassuming hero.<br /> <br /> So no, that is not what Solars are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Elias Tremalion was an obviously supernatural expy James Bond (not a humble shepherd boy)? And, well, I did at least a couple times, say they can be unassuming &quot;if you work at it&quot; (i.e. specifically choose to make them so and pick Charms that support it) and &quot;unless you specifically make the effort to walk away from the powers they have which aren't&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just think that's much less common than blatantly supernatural Solars (hence, if you really, really had to choose between Solars being Goliath and David, Goliath), it's not the default, it's not particular common among Solars compared to other splats. I also don't think it makes sense to think of blatantly supernatural Solars (which is going to be most who even use a modicum of their Charmsets in any ability) as somehow less Solar than Solars who aren't, and that the idea of Solars as unassuming guys who undercut more obviously supernatural foes sort of does them as disservice (in how much of their style is from their very supernatural moves, and how appealing that is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:13:39-07:00","id":856711,"title":"","content":"Really that came across more negatively than I wanted. I love that Exalted is a setting where everything is high powered enough that people can claim, with absolute seriousness, that guys who, as a typical manifestation of their power, glow golden, throw sunfire around and routinely trump the natural law because of their ability to channel mystical chi, fight in an &quot;unassuming&quot; way... because they don't actually turn into werewolves or crackle with lightning (unless they have a magic sword or armour!). I appreciate it from the one angle, as much as it totally seems like &quot;If that's unassuming, what's our yardstick for people who are actually assuming?&quot; from the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:46:30-07:00","id":856726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856607#post856607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pattern Spider Touch can probably enable the capacity to practice those styles, so it can all work out in the end. Just beware the lack of an easily flipped switch in comparison to Lunars, Alchemicals and what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried hard but don't think I got what you wanted to say with this post.<br /> <br /> Are you saying Sidereals can overcome physiology to learn a MA and so that shouldn't be a concern?<br /> <br /> Sorry, its just not clear for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:05:54-07:00","id":856782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856726#post856726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried hard but don't think I got what you wanted to say with this post.<br /> <br /> Are you saying Sidereals can overcome physiology to learn a MA and so that shouldn't be a concern?<br /> <br /> Sorry, its just not clear for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it does kind of undermine Guancyto's point, but a Solar or Sidereal could be transformed and learn it. They just wouldn't be able to easily transform back like Lunars or refit themselves like Alchemicals, so they'd be stuck only using that style and other shape-compatible styles until someone changed them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:32:44-07:00","id":856793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856782#post856782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it does kind of undermine Guancyto's point, but a Solar or Sidereal could be transformed and learn it. They just wouldn't be able to easily transform back like Lunars or refit themselves like Alchemicals, so they'd be stuck only using that style and other shape-compatible styles until someone changed them back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think of it like this. A snake wouldn't make a style representing the movements of a snake, it would just move. If you already have the hood, scales, and fangs of a cobra, there is nothing more that martial arts can do to make you cobra like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:37:28-07:00","id":856796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856793#post856793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Think of it like this. A snake wouldn't make a style representing the movements of a snake, it would just move. If you already have the hood, scales, and fangs of a cobra, there is nothing more that martial arts can do to make you cobra like.</div> </div> </div> </div>A snake is not the one making it. Something with the shape of a snake is, say, a god, or a Lunar. The style in question utilizes these different pieces of anatomy in a way that Brawl does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:45:18-07:00","id":856800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856681#post856681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. You need to get 100 threshold successes in six rolls against difficulty 5 to make a 5-dot Artifact. So your ability to make greater wonders depends entirely upon your access to roll-boosting Charms.<br /> <br /> An Essence 1 DB with max stats and an exceptional tool using a full excellency and spending 2wp rolls 18 dice, rerolls 1 failure, and adds 1 success. On average, they'll get 10.5 successes per roll. That's just barely enough to make a 2-dot Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: you can get a stunt bonus too! But yeah, the essence of the point is correct. I just tested 30 iterations of a six-interval 20-die crafting roll with +1 autosucc (didn't do the reroll because it's complicated) and I got 25 results at 30+ successes, with two at 50+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:48:44-07:00","id":856801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856796#post856796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A snake is not the one making it. Something with the shape of a snake is, say, a god, or a Lunar. The style in question utilizes these different pieces of anatomy in a way that Brawl does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that sounds like Lunar brawl. 3E seems to be getting away from martial arts that can only be practiced by a select few. Remember that mortals can use <i>every</i> single martial art in the book and will presumably be able to use the dragon styles as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:01:44-07:00","id":856804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856800#post856800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: you can get a stunt bonus too! But yeah, the essence of the point is correct. I just tested 30 iterations of a six-interval 20-die crafting roll with +1 autosucc (didn't do the reroll because it's complicated) and I got 25 results at 30+ successes, with two at 50+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just add in one extra die if you want to factor in a single reroll. It works out exactly the same unless you scored a success on every single one of your initial 20 dice, which is a low enough probability that it's not worth accounting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:15:06-07:00","id":856814,"title":"","content":"I think that just isn't what the material proposes Martial Arts are about.<br /> <br /> I stand by what I initially said about it. Not every coded way of fighting is a Martial Art Ability (I write this in all caps when I'm referring to the specific game mechanic construct). If they were we wouldn't have the general combat Abilities. You wouldn't have Melee or Thrown, you would have Lookshyan Spear Fighting and Harborhead Slingshotting as discrete Abilities. That is not the case.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there is any esoteric value to &quot;I'm a snake, just better!&quot;. There is very little cultural potential. Martial Arts are are a sum of technique, culture, metaphysics (shallow and corny as some may be) tradition and shared experience. I see them as a &quot;human&quot; endeavor. <br /> <br /> There are 2 types of Martial Arts. Regular and Sidereal. For a Regular Martial Art, it should be something that can be learned and used by any &quot;regular mortal&quot; and accessible to any Exalt splat without requiring any other &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if you need shape shifting to use a martial art, it is not a Martial Art Ability. It is something else. I can understand some external (to the MA) power having a particular synergy with a MA, but that should come from outside the MA, like DB Anima enhancing a Immaculate Style. Not the Immaculate Style enhancing the DB Anima.<br /> <br /> Solars (roids?) are the undisputed masters of Abilities. Theirs, and Sidereal's, splat description specifically calls them out as Masters of Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I won't speak for Sidereal Martial Arts because we know close to nothing of their 3e iteration, and 3e is what I'm interested in discussing.<br /> <br /> Powers, or fighting techniques, that depend on alien physiology to even have use outside of Charms are not what I, or the book seems to, consider Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:15:47-07:00","id":856816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856681#post856681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guancyto, please stop with the penis talk. It <b>makes it hard</b> to take this conversation seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. Hehehehe.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> No, seriously guys, I'm just trying to make the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856681#post856681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. You need to get 100 threshold successes in six rolls against difficulty 5 to make a 5-dot Artifact. So your ability to make greater wonders depends entirely upon your access to roll-boosting Charms.<br /> <br /> An Essence 1 DB with max stats and an exceptional tool using a full excellency and spending 2wp rolls 18 dice, rerolls 1 failure, and adds 1 success. On average, they'll get 10.5 successes per roll. That's just barely enough to make a 2-dot Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you mean to say is that anyone who can get generate the right amount of Craft XP and roll the right amount of successes can make the sort of Artifact in question, right? There's not some uber-level project slot that is fundamentally denied to Dragon-Blooded? There's nothing gating things off, like Solar Circle Sorcery, right? It's just a question of generating the right numbers?<br /> <br /> That's what I meant in my post. 5-Dot Artifacts are surely difficult to create, but it's not fundamentally impossible. Dragon-Blooded are allowed to try, so I can't imagine they won't be allowed to succeed, with investment and effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:20:42-07:00","id":856818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856816#post856816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you mean to say is that anyone who can get generate the right amount of Craft XP and roll the right amount of successes can make the sort of Artifact in question, right? There's not some uber-level project slot that is fundamentally denied to Dragon-Blooded? There's nothing gating things off, like Solar Circle Sorcery, right? It's just a question of generating the right numbers?<br /> <br /> That's what I meant in my post. 5-Dot Artifacts are surely difficult to create, but it's not fundamentally impossible. Dragon-Blooded are allowed to try, so I can't imagine they won't be allowed to succeed, with investment and effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will only know when the DB Craft Charms come out. If they don't give you enough, it might as well be impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:51:03-07:00","id":856836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856816#post856816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you mean to say is that anyone who can get generate the right amount of Craft XP and roll the right amount of successes can make the sort of Artifact in question, right? There's not some uber-level project slot that is fundamentally denied to Dragon-Blooded? There's nothing gating things off, like Solar Circle Sorcery, right? It's just a question of generating the right numbers?<br /> <br /> That's what I meant in my post. 5-Dot Artifacts are surely difficult to create, but it's not fundamentally impossible. Dragon-Blooded are allowed to try, so I can't imagine they won't be allowed to succeed, with investment and effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really does all depend on what their Craft charms look like -- it's possible for a DB to create a five-dot artifact without Charms in the same sense that it's possible for a mortal to solo the Unconquered Sun due to the UCS getting a lot of really bad rolls. Going by a very rough back-of-the-envelope calculation, and assuming craft points aren't an issue, a Dragon-Blooded with 20 dice per roll is going to succeed at an Artifact 5 project about once every 300 billion years. I mean, that's not hyperbole, that's the actual number.<br /> <br /> Obviously, they're going to have Craft charms to take that down to the &quot;hard but possible&quot; range with sufficient investment, but the kind of &quot;possibility&quot; the baseline system permits really doesn't mean much above Artifact 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-31-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:03:32-07:00","id":856841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856681#post856681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guancyto, please stop with the penis talk. It makes it hard to take this conversation seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two reasons.<br /> <br /> First, penis jokes are the only way to make a discussion of how Solars are superior to everything tolerable. I will admit it is not a particularly mature coping mechanism, but my hip waders are in the shop.<br /> <br /> Second, although it's not a very <i>nice</i> way of doing it, I am answering the OP's question. Looking across this thread, are Solars masters of the supernatural? Titans of strength and hew that stand above everyone else? Masters of sorcery and wyld that shape the world to their whims? Are they masters of the ordinary, of taking unassuming human competence and driving it to absurd levels? Will they slay a dragon with a single arrow? With a slingstone? With a rain of fire? With a golden laser beam? With a wave of acid babies? With a demon army? With an awakened sentient blade that they are bonded to? With the power of being half-hollow half-Quincy half-death-god half-human half-dragon half-potato as the plot requires? With a thirty-minute flashback sequence while powering up? With an enemy's own kung fu, no matter what that kung fu might be? With a giant glowing golden rock concert? With a single word of terrible power? With an ordinary speech?<br /> <br /> Yes. In all cases, the answer appears to be &quot;yes.&quot; There's only one way in which the Solars are most powerful among the Exalted and that is, quite simply, that they are everything to everyone. To put it crudely but in no way sacrifice accuracy, their power is that they just plain outdick everyone else.<br /> <br /> And any exception to this rule is apparently something to be stamped out as aggressively as possible, it seems? Man, I remember the firestorms over Infernals. The lovely outrage! The wounded pride! How <i>dare</i> Infernals be better at doing certain things than Solars! How <i>dare</i> they be better at taking damage, don't you know Resistance is an ability? How <i>dare</i> they be better at making stuff from nothing, don't you know Wyld-Shaping has been Solar-exclusive since forever?Oh, the wonderful discussions that were had over Alchemical Craft. How <i>dare</i> the chosen of the Great Maker be better at making things, don't you know that Craft is an ability and that Solars are the best at anything that could be remotely construed as belonging to an Ability?<br /> <br /> Do you want to have those discussions again? Because if the writers and devs are even remotely competent at making the non-Solar splats attractive (and I think they are), as long as you maintain the Solars Must Be Better At Everything Including Other People's Things, you will have them again, and again, and again, and <i>again</i>.<br /> <br /> But if that's your jam then hey, forget everything I said, I'm just a guy who talks about dicks too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 03-31-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:08:42-07:00","id":856848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856801#post856801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that sounds like Lunar brawl. 3E seems to be getting away from martial arts that can only be practiced by a select few. Remember that mortals can use <i>every</i> single martial art in the book and will presumably be able to use the dragon styles as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars don't have Brawl Charms. They have bodily transformations and something likely related to spirit-channeling, given the stated themes of Warrior, Shaman, and Trickster, which all center on their inherent power. A style using a snake body to do esoteric combat maneuvers without shapeshifting, spiritual shenanigans or the like is definitely far away from being just like Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't believe there is any esoteric value to &quot;I'm a snake, just better!&quot;.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Admittedly, this part of Guancyto's thesis was flawed. That's probably not what a Martial Arts style requiring that you be in the shape of a snake would involve. Instead, it would be as weird as other styles are, centered on an esoteric concept that requires being a serpent, not entirely unlike how Dragon King martial arts are likely to go back to requiring that you be a Dragon King in order to use them. All of the styles thus far are intended for a default use for a game made by humans where humans are the main characters; branching out from there in a few years, we might see weirder examples.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:26:36-07:00","id":856863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856800#post856800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: you can get a stunt bonus too! But yeah, the essence of the point is correct. I just tested 30 iterations of a six-interval 20-die crafting roll with +1 autosucc (didn't do the reroll because it's complicated) and I got 25 results at 30+ successes, with two at 50+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't believe I left out the stunt bonus.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the reroll doesn't have to be complicated. Rerolling one die is the same as rolling one extra die unless every single die succeeds, which is pretty much never gonna happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856816#post856816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hehe. Hehehehe.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> No, seriously guys, I'm just trying to make the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I walked right into that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856841#post856841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, penis jokes are the only way to make a discussion of how Solars are superior to everything tolerable. I will admit it is not a particularly mature coping mechanism, but my hip waders are in the shop.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you find this sort of conversation unpleasant, maybe avoid it?<br /> <br /> For me, the worst thing in this thread is your sense of humour. I know I can't actually make you stop, but...you don't seem to be enjoying yourself, and you're making my life ever-so-slightly worse while you're at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:28:01-07:00","id":856865,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing that kind of argument here.<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that there shouldn't be any Ability that a Solar is not able to master. I'm not saying Solar Craft must be &quot;better&quot; than Alchemical Craft. All I'm saying is that the Alchemical's advantage must come from something other than Ability mastery.<br /> <br /> The basic thing a Martial Art is is an Ability. Therefore Solars should be able to master them. Can another splat be more effective with them because of their other powers? Sure thing. Just not because of the Ability itself cannot be mastered by a Solar.<br /> <br /> Imagine an Immaculate Style Form grants the Charm user Elemental Anima +1, +2 for Mastery. Lets say DBs can naturally flare to 3, with the Style they hit the legendary 4, Solars can at their best hit 2. Who is the &quot;better&quot; Stylist? Arguably the Solar gets more out of the MA Abilty, as they should. But the Ability is much more effective for the DB, who can achieve an exponentially higher Anima with it. If you were watching the display, who would you think &quot;won&quot;?<br /> <br /> You seem to be having a dick measuring contest while wanting to establish a category for &quot;blue dicks&quot; and saying that no matter how big the other guy is since this other one is blue he has to win. I just don't see why that must be so, why is there a dick measuring contest in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:38:06-07:00","id":856868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856365#post856365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's untrue. For every practical definition of better, a Solar Immaculate Stylist was better than a DB Immaculate Stylist. The Solar had a higher dice cap, bigger mote pool, and much higher survivability thanks to his superior (or downright broken, depending on who you ask) native Dodge and Resistance Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and guess what? This would still be true in 3e if Immaculates got the Mastery keyword for Immaculate martial arts. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:42:53-07:00","id":856870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856865#post856865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be having a dick measuring contest while wanting to establish a category for &quot;blue dicks&quot; and saying that no matter how big the other guy is since this other one is blue he has to win. I just don't see why that must be so, why is there a dick measuring contest in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. All this dick-measuring crap is totally missing the point. Yes, Solars are the strongest, and there's nothing wrong with that. To continue with the superhero analogies, Superman is flat-out stronger than Batman, but that doesn't make Batman less interesting as a hero. Many people would argue the reverse, in fact - trying to give Batman superstrength, flight and laser vision because it's not fair that Superman gets to be the strongest isn't just missing the point of Batman, it's actively making him worse as a character because a large part of his appeal comes from being the one normal guy in a world full of gods. Yes, DBs are the weakest of the Exalted, and that's <i>why </i>they're my favourite Exalted. Trying to give them Solar-level power does them a tremendous disservice, and comes with this weird assumption that the only way a character can be worth playing is if they can beat everyone else in a dick-waving contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:51:20-07:00","id":856876,"title":"","content":"Eh! My thesis was more or less a hypothetical of, &quot;can you design a martial art specifically such that Solars are not better than you at it?&quot; To which the answer seems to be one of &quot;yes, if it's not actually a Martial Art, &quot;yes, if they're better than you at it in ways that are somewhat oblique to your design&quot; and &quot;CLEANSE THIS HERESY FOR THE GOD-EMPEROR.&quot; The response was informative! (The answers to the other hypothetical of &quot;can you design an artifact specifically such that a Terrestrial is head-and-shoulders better than anyone else at using it?&quot; were also informative!)<br /> <br /> I mean, SaurOps made much, much better points than me. Dragon King Martial Arts are a thing! Some of them required things like water breathing and flight, if I remember right, in ways that a Solar, no matter how Masterful, couldn't replicate, at least without some hard-core body modification. There's honestly little reason to believe that wouldn't also be true of a Martial Art designed by Pelagials, or the Blessed Cloth, or the talking lions of Origin.<br /> <br /> And of course you aren't seeing that kind of argument here, because there hasn't been a single charm written about any other splat. As soon as, I dunno, Getimians wind up with a build that's better at soak than Solars, or Alchemicals get to be really bloody good at Craft again, expect the <i>knives</i> to come out. I'm just saying that Solarum Uber Alles is <i>exactly</i> the viewpoint that leads to that kind of wankery. (as far as I can tell Solarum Uber Alles is <i>not</i> your viewpoint TGUEIROS, so good show on that and we really have no quarrel at all)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:15:14-07:00","id":856890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856876#post856876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh! My thesis was more or less a hypothetical of, &quot;can you design a martial art specifically such that Solars are not better than you at it?&quot; To which the answer seems to be one of &quot;yes, if it's not actually a Martial Art, &quot;yes, if they're better than you at it in ways that are somewhat oblique to your design&quot; and &quot;CLEANSE THIS HERESY FOR THE GOD-EMPEROR.&quot; The response was informative! (The answers to the other hypothetical of &quot;can you design an artifact specifically such that a Terrestrial is head-and-shoulders better than anyone else at using it?&quot; were also informative!)<br /> <br /> I mean, SaurOps made much, much better points than me. Dragon King Martial Arts are a thing! Some of them required things like water breathing and flight, if I remember right, in ways that a Solar, no matter how Masterful, couldn't replicate, at least without some hard-core body modification. There's honestly little reason to believe that wouldn't also be true of a Martial Art designed by Pelagials, or the Blessed Cloth, or the talking lions of Origin.<br /> <br /> And of course you aren't seeing that kind of argument here, because there hasn't been a single charm written about any other splat. As soon as, I dunno, Getimians wind up with a build that's better at soak than Solars, or Alchemicals get to be really bloody good at Craft again, expect the <i>knives</i> to come out. I'm just saying that Solarum Uber Alles is <i>exactly</i> the viewpoint that leads to that kind of wankery. (as far as I can tell Solarum Uber Alles is <i>not</i> your viewpoint TGUEIROS, so good show on that and we really have no quarrel at all)</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point. <br /> <br /> I just think its too early to establish that DK MAs are still a thing. If they were confirmed to be then my argument on the nature of Exalted's Martial Arts would be pretty moot (unless they could be practiced by ordinary &quot;humans&quot; using specific gear).<br /> <br /> I guess we will just have to wait and see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:23:07-07:00","id":856893,"title":"","content":"My hope is just that the power gap has been narrowed enough that a DB doesn't have to rely on a Celestial-Tier Martial Art &quot;cheat&quot; to be impressive. That a Dragonblooded should feel pigeonholed into Martial Arts to walk into a fight with a Solar and not melt is...troubling. It hurts diversity of combatants and diversity of characters. Though, I do think their martial arts should have very specific synergy with DB abilities; just the way Ebon Shadow really wishes you maxed Stealth and Black Claw wants you to have a very good guile, I think DB MA should be made better for having an anima flux/have synergy with other unique abilities DB have. Sure, the Solar can have a mastery effect, but can he casually toss fireballs (Without having punchsorbed them with Fire-Eating Fist?) Nah. And it should still work as an MA without anima flux and element-balls and being really rich and well-bred, but should have some nice stuff if you happen to have that.<br /> <br /> Immaculate Martial Arts should be Iconic, but by no means should they be The One Best Combat Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:10:50-07:00","id":856925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856893#post856893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immaculate Martial Arts should be Iconic, but by no means should they be The One Best Combat Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Joke] nope they are gonna be the FIVE best abiltiies [/Joke] <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:33:53-07:00","id":856937,"title":"","content":"I find it odd that people are discussing the Immaculate Martial Arts as if they were some kind of trump card against the Solars.They were created by the Sidereals to help the Dragonblooded bring wayward gods to heel. The Dragonblooded had already proved themselves <i>very</i> capable of killing Solars with their native charms by that point. The reason Wyld Hunts are assumed to have a whole bunch of Immaculate masters also has nothing to do with any kind of perceived superiority of the martial arts for fighting Anathema over the other abilities. All Dragonblooded warriors were expected to participate in Wyld Hunts, but in these tumultuous time many neglect their spiritual duty in favor of helping their House prepare for civil war. Those that remain are the most dedicated to the Immaculate faith, which for the most part are old, experienced monks and their young pupils. And old monks tend to have the highest essence, the most combat charms, and they have seen all your tricks already. That's what makes them scary for a Solar to face, not the Immaculate styles somehow being better than other Dragonblooded charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:51:18-07:00","id":856947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856876#post856876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh! My thesis was more or less a hypothetical of, &quot;can you design a martial art specifically such that Solars are not better than you at it?&quot; To which the answer seems to be one of &quot;yes, if it's not actually a Martial Art, &quot;yes, if they're better than you at it in ways that are somewhat oblique to your design&quot; and &quot;CLEANSE THIS HERESY FOR THE GOD-EMPEROR.&quot; The response was informative! (The answers to the other hypothetical of &quot;can you design an artifact specifically such that a Terrestrial is head-and-shoulders better than anyone else at using it?&quot; were also informative!)<br /> <br /> I mean, SaurOps made much, much better points than me. Dragon King Martial Arts are a thing! Some of them required things like water breathing and flight, if I remember right, in ways that a Solar, no matter how Masterful, couldn't replicate, at least without some hard-core body modification. There's honestly little reason to believe that wouldn't also be true of a Martial Art designed by Pelagials, or the Blessed Cloth, or the talking lions of Origin.<br /> <br /> And of course you aren't seeing that kind of argument here, because there hasn't been a single charm written about any other splat. As soon as, I dunno, Getimians wind up with a build that's better at soak than Solars, or Alchemicals get to be really bloody good at Craft again, expect the <i>knives</i> to come out. I'm just saying that Solarum Uber Alles is <i>exactly</i> the viewpoint that leads to that kind of wankery. (as far as I can tell Solarum Uber Alles is <i>not</i> your viewpoint TGUEIROS, so good show on that and we really have no quarrel at all)</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like Gunzosha armor the concept of relative advantage is useful here. The Solars could be head and shoulders better than everyone else at anything they touch but they can't be good at everything. There are martial arts and artifacts that are not as beneficial to a Solar as they are to someone else in a relative sense because the Solar has other, better options available. This is fine, working as intended, and raises the level of unique nice things people will actually use.<br /> <br /> Imagine an artifact bow that let you spend a wp to fire an arrow that exploded when it hit. For a mortal this is the closest they are likely to get to real magical power and is a powerful tool that they will use with great care. For a Solar it is a horrible option even if they get a flat twice the damage on the explosions because there are so many other things they can spend WP on that are so much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:20:04-07:00","id":856957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856876#post856876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh! My thesis was more or less a hypothetical of, &quot;can you design a martial art specifically such that Solars are not better than you at it?&quot; To which the answer seems to be one of &quot;yes, if it's not actually a Martial Art, &quot;yes, if they're better than you at it in ways that are somewhat oblique to your design&quot; and &quot;CLEANSE THIS HERESY FOR THE GOD-EMPEROR.&quot; The response was informative! (The answers to the other hypothetical of &quot;can you design an artifact specifically such that a Terrestrial is head-and-shoulders better than anyone else at using it?&quot; were also informative!)<br /> <br /> I mean, SaurOps made much, much better points than me. Dragon King Martial Arts are a thing! Some of them required things like water breathing and flight, if I remember right, in ways that a Solar, no matter how Masterful, couldn't replicate, at least without some hard-core body modification. There's honestly little reason to believe that wouldn't also be true of a Martial Art designed by Pelagials, or the Blessed Cloth, or the talking lions of Origin.<br /> <br /> And of course you aren't seeing that kind of argument here, because there hasn't been a single charm written about any other splat. As soon as, I dunno, Getimians wind up with a build that's better at soak than Solars, or Alchemicals get to be really bloody good at Craft again, expect the <i>knives</i> to come out. I'm just saying that Solarum Uber Alles is <i>exactly</i> the viewpoint that leads to that kind of wankery. (as far as I can tell Solarum Uber Alles is <i>not</i> your viewpoint TGUEIROS, so good show on that and we really have no quarrel at all)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with things said here.<br /> <br /> I specifically recall that the Devs were saying that there were specialized areas where other Exalts would better than the Solars in. <br /> <br /> though apparently from the responses in this thread, from are only three impossible things in Exalted:<br /> 1. no time travel<br /> 2. no resurrection<br /> 3. no beating a Solar at anything.<br /> <br /> what an annoying piece of fanon. assuming it is true though, I challenge all Solars to a &quot;beat yourself to death&quot; contest. Last one there out of 301 contestants has to rule all of Creation and shoulder all its responsibilities while still being alive. Go! Any Solar of course who doesn't accept is clearly too much of a coward to beat me at such an easy contest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T23:33:27-07:00","id":856976,"title":"","content":"Any Solar can be beaten at anything. But some people would rather the Solar Exalted as a splat be at least as good as every other Exalted splat at any straightforward task of skill.<br /> <br /> That's not my position. My position is that balancing a Martial Art against both Solar Brawl and Dragonblooded Brawl seems impossible unless the art is better for Solars.<br /> <br /> This idea isn't original to me, but I think it's a good one: Solars and DBs both get extra bonuses. The Solar ones are more powerful mechanically speaking, but the DB ones give more elemental effects and are like extra techniques. So in a very real sense, a DB can claim to have mastered the style more fully.<br /> <br /> How does that sound to y'all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:07:11-07:00","id":856989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856868#post856868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and guess what? This would still be true in 3e if Immaculates got the Mastery keyword for Immaculate martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only further proves it'd be pointless to give it to them, on top of it flying in the face of how MA are supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:07:31-07:00","id":856990,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I think I figured out part of the problem here. There isn't a worse comparison to make regarding power than the absolute limit of Exalted power (Solars) and the absolute weakest Exalted (DBs) especially in an area which is specifically designed to allow exalt splats to break out of their themes. So yes, a Solar using Breath of the Fire Dragon deals more damage than a terrestrial, and you can say that a Solar is &quot;better&quot; at breathing fire than a DB is, in this one particular worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> Really though, a DB can be a lot more versatile with fire than a Solar can. It's part of their anima and their native charms. They can do cool things like instantly rise from prone like a firecracker and stuff like that, while Solars are relegated to just the charms in Fire Dragon Style, and any evocations they unlock.<br /> <br /> So lets look at something else, Sidereal native charms. This is a way better way to compare Solar power. So Guancyto brouight up Getimian resistance charms. Those are not going to be able to soak damage better than a Solar, for sure. But look at what Sid resistance charms can do...well for one they can bind an elemental to your will! Yeah, there's NO logical connection to make for a Solar charm to be able to bind elementals because you shrug off damage and hardship. It's also powerful, it's like an instant summon elemental spell, it's great! A Solar just can't do that, they can't ever use a resistance charm to instantly bind an elemental.<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal did that in front of them they'd ask: &quot;How in the holy mother of fuck did you do that?&quot;<br /> To which the Sidereal replies: &quot;I don't know, you just have to be really tough and the elementals of the world obey you, they respect that I guess?&quot;<br /> <br /> And no matter how hard they try, no matter what they do, they never will be able to do that in the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, when you make it a martial art, that brings it right back into the Solar wheelhouse. It's not a native effect that only your exaltation can power, it's specifically something any exalt and many spirits. You're not taking the essence of fire within your soul and extruding it through your weapon, you're performing specific spiritual motions that anyone qualified can use to bring forth fire. That, combined with the mechanical effect, means Solars are the best at it. Yeah, it sucks for the DB PC who's facing off against a Solar who's laughing in his face because he can't do Air Dragon Style as well as the Solar can...but then that DB just screams a torrent of lightning at him from his native charms and proves that while the Solar merely adopted the wind, he was born to it.<br /> <br /> Of course things being equal that DB is going to get his ass handed to him, but at least he'll have proven that mastering Solar Air Dragon Style doesn't make you a chosen of Mela.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:20:20-07:00","id":856997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856990#post856990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not taking the essence of fire within your soul and extruding it through your weapon, you're performing specific spiritual motions that anyone qualified can use to bring forth fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument is though, for me, is that you are in fact doing both if you're a Dragonblooded. A Dragonblooded who practices Fire Dragon Style is hardly *not* &quot;taking the essence of fire within your soul&quot; and filling their technique with it. Of course they are. Otherwise for one it makes no sense for the Dragonblooded to be practicing these as spiritual martial arts that bring their inner essence closer to the essence of the Immaculate Dragons. Which they do. And that's why they can do (or in any sane world, should get to be able to do) effects with it that no Solar, elementally unattuned, can.<br /> <br /> Why should there be this idea of complete separation of drawing on native essence from practicing martial arts?<br /> <br /> (Kind of also occurs to me that if we accepted &quot;you're performing specific spiritual motions that anyone qualified can use to bring forth fire&quot;, as the Dragon Styles, that's just as much an argument for why the Solars should *not* get Mastery effects. After, they're not drawing on their inner essence in any way, just performing motions anyone can do. So why would they be able do it stronger? OTOH, if they are drawing on their inner essence, why are Dragonblooded not?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:47:20-07:00","id":857007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856990#post856990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets look at something else, Sidereal native charms. This is a way better way to compare Solar power. So Guancyto brouight up Getimian resistance charms. Those are not going to be able to soak damage better than a Solar, for sure. But look at what Sid resistance charms can do...well for one they can bind an elemental to your will! Yeah, there's NO logical connection to make for a Solar charm to be able to bind elementals because you shrug off damage and hardship. It's also powerful, it's like an instant summon elemental spell, it's great! A Solar just can't do that, they can't ever use a resistance charm to instantly bind an elemental.<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal did that in front of them they'd ask: &quot;How in the holy mother of fuck did you do that?&quot;<br /> To which the Sidereal replies: &quot;I don't know, you just have to be really tough and the elementals of the world obey you, they respect that I guess?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You reminded me why i kinna dislike sidereal charm set. I hope in this edition there will be a summary for sidereal abilities, like;<br /> <br /> Melee - you heal people<br /> Medicine - you craft things<br /> Bureaucracy - Resisting attacks and poisons<br /> Performance - Dodging stuff..<br /> etc...<br /> <br /> It is really confusing to find the right charms from the right abilities :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:25:42-07:00","id":857020,"title":"","content":"Blegh. I really should stop reading threads with Solar in the title in this forum. All this is doing is making me dislike Solars more with every page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:34:28-07:00","id":857022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=857020#post857020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blegh. I really should stop reading threads with Solar in the title in this forum. All this is doing is making me dislike Solars more with every page.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/Sideous] Good.....goood......let your hate flow through you, take up your daiklaive, strike down the Solars and take their place at my side as an Abyssal of the Dark Side of the Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> but seriously, if you like them yeah.....internet threads tend to devolve into attracting people who hate subjects while repelling the people who like subjects, making the latter avoid them. its weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T03:22:55-07:00","id":857045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856876#post856876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh! My thesis was more or less a hypothetical of, &quot;can you design a martial art specifically such that Solars are not better than you at it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean.<br /> <br /> It's trivial if that's your only goal. Just take what would usually be the Terrestrial effects, and make the whole style purely Terrestrial, with no Celestial or Mastery benefits. Done. But unfortunately there are some other issues here.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate styles need to be:<br /> <br /> 1. Effective for Dragon-Blooded, but not <i>so</i> effective that they're a dominating option. My understanding is that in 3e, DB MA isn't supposed to be dramatically better than Melee. This means you can't just straightforwardly give the DBs the style's Celestial benefits unless you make them a bit weak (or limit the way the DBs access them in some way, which potentially breaks your requirement that Solars not be better at the style than DBs.)<br /> <br /> 2. Powerful martial art styles. They're supposed to be legendary. Oops, if they're Terrestrial for everyone, they're instead the <i>worst Marital Arts in the game</i> for everyone except DBs. You can say &quot;well, the style is just for Dragon-Blooded&quot;, but... players are still going to notice and understand that the vaunted Immaculate styles are in fact the worst Martial Arts ever created.<br /> <br /> There isn't any easy way around this. Notice that the problem isn't even really just Solars, it's <i>Celestials</i>. Should Sidereals be better at Immaculate styles than DBs? Should Lunars? Alchemicals? Abyssals? If you go by the default way 3e styles are made, the only way to avoid this is to deliberately spike the style by removing the Celestial benefits and forcing everyone to take Terrestrial penalties (well, baking them into the charms with no Terrestrial / Celestial divide), which puts us back at &quot;the vaunted Immaculate styles are actually the weakest martial arts ever created.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are a few ways to finesse the problem, of course. The Immaculate styles could do weird stuff that doesn't fit into the normal power structure; this allows you to somewhat ignore the usual Terrestrial / Celestial / Mastery issues. There's certainly effects out there that are equally useful to all splats and which could be given to everyone evenly (even with some small cosmetic advantages for DBs) which wouldn't necessarily make DB Martial Artists dramatically better than DBs who focus on Melee, while still making the Immaculate Styles genuinely impressive... but I'm dubious that you could construct an entire style around this, let alone five, especially when you're also laboring under the requirement that these be some of the most impressive Martial Arts in the game.<br /> <br /> But I suspect what you're going to see instead is that the Immaculate Styles will look like a typical martial art (in terms of having the Terrestrial / Celestial divide and perhaps even some Mastery effects), plus some flashy-but-ultimately-not-that-powerful DB-only advantages and possibly ways for DBs to situationally boost to the Celestial or even Mastery advantages for those styles at some significant cost, so DBs don't feel like they're strictly worse than everyone else at their signature martial arts. This would mean that a DB who pulls out all the stops and pays whatever cost is necessary to boost all the way in the style could match a Sidereal or Solar at it (even if they're paying more for the privilege), and even exceed them in certain ways due to the unique benefits... while balancing both the costs and the available benefits so they don't break the game or render DB Melee obsolete. It'd still be a tricky thread-the-needle exercise, but it'd at least be <i>possible</i> to satisfy all the various goals that way.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, though, regarding whether the Immaculate Styles are just for Dragon-Blooded: They aren't. The Dragon-Blooded already have charms that are just for Dragon-Blooded, they're the <i>Dragon-Blooded charmset</i>. The fact that Sidereals, Abyssals, Lunars, and, yes, Solars can learn and excel at the Martial Arts that Dragon-Blooded consider iconic to their religion is a feature, not a bug; if they wanted the Immaculate Styles to be &quot;only for DBs&quot;, they would be sets of DB charms, not Martial Arts. The purpose of Martial Arts is to be something a wide variety of people can learn and excel at.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-01-2016, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:53:08-07:00","id":857175,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/p19ivWy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:05:08-07:00","id":857525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=857045#post857045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I suspect what you're going to see instead is that the Immaculate Styles will look like a typical martial art (in terms of having the Terrestrial / Celestial divide and perhaps even some Mastery effects), plus some flashy-but-ultimately-not-that-powerful DB-only advantages and possibly ways for DBs to situationally boost to the Celestial or even Mastery advantages for those styles at some significant cost, so DBs don't feel like they're strictly worse than everyone else at their signature martial arts. This would mean that a DB who pulls out all the stops and pays whatever cost is necessary to boost all the way in the style could match a Sidereal or Solar at it (even if they're paying more for the privilege), and even exceed them in certain ways due to the unique benefits... while balancing both the costs and the available benefits so they don't break the game or render DB Melee obsolete. It'd still be a tricky thread-the-needle exercise, but it'd at least be <i>possible</i> to satisfy all the various goals that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to figure out what a cost like this might look like. Firstly I think it needs up-front chargen/xp cost. Like a merit that upgrades the MA merit to unlock access to the cap bursting charm, which lets you spend some combination of motes/willpower to ignore the terrestrial keyword for the action. That way you've got a clear difference between somebody who's been initiated into the Immaculate techniques that allow them to exceed the normal limits, and the people who just know the style without the enlightenment, and the added combat cost offsets the bonuses they get.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure how it would work with charms that are once-per-scene for DBs. If you wanted to use it twice would you have to activate the cap-burster when you used it the first time? Or could you activate it after your once-per-scene allotment by using the cap-burster?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:57:07-07:00","id":857678,"title":"","content":"Re: Aquillion's post, although not disagreeing with the mechanical conclusion, I'm kind of critical of a few things in it (because there had to be someone who was, right?).<br /> <br /> 1. Are the Immaculate MA really supposed to be legendary styles for Exalted other than Dragonblooded, and some of the most impressive in the game? They are legendary within the Dragonblooded as styles that unlock power and spiritual connection for them. Otherwise, seems off base.<br /> <br /> 2. Is it really capturing people's psychology that they'd think the Immaculate Styles were terrible and the weakest martial arts in the game if they were just great for Dragonblooded Immaculates and not great for anyone else? I really doubt that as something which immediately springs to mind (or it wouldn't have taken til post #121). I think most Dragonblooded players, who are the ones who actually mainly matter, would still think &quot;Wow, these are great&quot; and be happy to take them.<br /> <br /> I would also add a note as well that the reason for the Immaculate Styles (if they're kept in the game!) to be stronger for Dragonblooded isn't *just* a sop to the feelings of Dragonblooded players or anything. It's a concrete step to dovetail with why Immaculates learn them (other than just handwaving &quot;It's their culture&quot;) - if they just get Terrestrial level effects for the Immaculate Styles, period, and that's all you get, why not just learn Five Dragon Style or something like that? Why is there this cultural tradition of learning the Immaculate Styles?<br /> <br /> (And on a tangent to that, I think thinking about other elemental and Terrestrial styles from 2e definitely makes it clearer for me about why it doesn't necessarily feel great for Solars to have Mastery effects, whether it's mechanically necessary or not. <br /> <br /> It's not because they are, as styles, &quot;for Terrestrials&quot; or &quot;their thing&quot;. It's because they represent a kind of spiritual connection and essence of the Dragonblooded. <br /> <br /> It's like if you had Lunar Hero style coming back... or better let's imagine there was a good style for Lunars called &quot;Five Faces of Luna&quot; or something like that, a style which lovingly fitted techniques to different phases of the moon and incarnations of Luna. And it's clearly meant to represent a path where Lunars get spiritually closer to Luna. And the books say that this is what Lunars believe. Then then you said that Solars get the highest benefits, and they're actually totally inaccessible to Lunars. Doesn't feel good, right?<br /> <br /> Whereas with something like Five Dragon Style, iconic to a splat and just as much for that splat, but not with any spiritual undertones of perfecting their essence, I'm happy to see a Solar punch another Solar in the face with some extra Mastery effect that pushes it up to Solar level, all while screaming &quot;Five dragons fight as one!&quot;, or &quot;The Dragonblooded host united shall never be defeated!&quot; something like that. It's not like anything is getting lost in the same way. Or Falling Blossom Style or Jade Mountain Style, even if they're sort of elemental, it's fine, because there isn't that idea that there is a deep connection to the essence of the Elemental Dragons there. Go wild.<br /> <br /> It sort of has me pondering whether it would be best to just drop the Immaculate Styles and that whole tradition, if they have to do them with Celestial and Mastery effects inaccessible to DBs. Might be better just not to have them, than have the tradition ring false and hollow because the kind of spiritual union that is represented by the highest levels of the style does not actually unlock for Dragonblooded. Then just have the Immaculate Order practice more generic elemental styles that are not in themselves a &quot;gate&quot; and just something they do in their monasteries to focus their mind and soul).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:38:33-07:00","id":858005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=857678#post857678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Aquillion's post, although not disagreeing with the mechanical conclusion, I'm kind of critical of a few things in it (because there had to be someone who was, right?).<br /> <br /> 1. Are the Immaculate MA really supposed to be legendary styles for Exalted other than Dragonblooded, and some of the most impressive in the game? They are legendary within the Dragonblooded as styles that unlock power and spiritual connection for them. Otherwise, seems off base.<br /> <br /> 2. Is it really capturing people's psychology that they'd think the Immaculate Styles were terrible and the weakest martial arts in the game if they were just great for Dragonblooded Immaculates and not great for anyone else? I really doubt that as something which immediately springs to mind (or it wouldn't have taken til post #121). I think most Dragonblooded players, who are the ones who actually mainly matter, would still think &quot;Wow, these are great&quot; and be happy to take them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are balanced like that, that means that they are basically 1e/2e Terrestrial styles in 3e. That would, yes, make them the worst martial arts in third edition, mechanically.<br /> <br /> Like, how do you think the Dragon-Blooded should react to an Anathema who has learned the Immaculate Styles? Outrage, sure, but should this Anathema be <i>less</i> dangerous than an Anathema who practiced any other martial art? That doesn't make sense. Fighting an Anathema who practices the Immaculate Styles should be an epic fight as you put down the would-be usurper who has profaned your most sacred techniques. You can't credibly run that if the Immaculate Styles are, for most people, the worst martial arts ever printed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also add a note as well that the reason for the Immaculate Styles (if they're kept in the game!) to be stronger for Dragonblooded isn't *just* a sop to the feelings of Dragonblooded players or anything. It's a concrete step to dovetail with why Immaculates learn them (other than just handwaving &quot;It's their culture&quot;) - if they just get Terrestrial level effects for the Immaculate Styles, period, and that's all you get, why not just learn Five Dragon Style or something like that? Why is there this cultural tradition of learning the Immaculate Styles? </div> </div> </div>I doubt Five Dragon Style will exist in 3e.<br /> <br /> If your question is &quot;why learn the Immaculate Styles and not something else,&quot; though, let me flip that around and ask you this: Do you want a game where the situation is &quot;why learn anything but the Immaculate Styles?&quot; Do you want a DB who learns Melee and not the Immaculate Styles to be noticeably weaker in combat than an Immaculate stylist?<br /> <br /> This is something the game did in the past, yes. I don't think it was a good decision (in practice it resulted in players contorting themselves to explain why their DB had Immaculate MA even when it made no sense; and thematically it lead to players viewing the Immaculate Styles as the &quot;real&quot; pinnacle of DB power, which I don't think they were ever meant to be.) The Immaculate Martial Arts are supposed to be a big deal, but they shouldn't express this at the expense of Dragon-Blooded Melee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like if you had Lunar Hero style coming back... or better let's imagine there was a good style for Lunars called &quot;Five Faces of Luna&quot; or something like that, a style which lovingly fitted techniques to different phases of the moon and incarnations of Luna. And it's clearly meant to represent a path where Lunars get spiritually closer to Luna. </div> </div> </div>The Hero styles have been dumped from the game precisely because that was a bad idea. Creating martial arts and then trying to turn them into native charms special to that Exalt type is completely pointless; that's not what Martial Arts are. Martial Arts are a universal charmset; they represent talents that the Exalted share among themselves and compete with each other at. They're a common ground between splats. The Sidereals are partially an exception (they have Sidereal Martial Arts as their &quot;secret techniques&quot;), but even then it isn't totally unique to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sort of has me pondering whether it would be best to just drop the Immaculate Styles and that whole tradition, if they have to do them with Celestial and Mastery effects inaccessible to DBs. Might be better just not to have them, than have the tradition ring false and hollow because the kind of spiritual union that is represented by the highest levels of the style does not actually unlock for Dragonblooded. Then just have the Immaculate Order practice more generic elemental styles that are not in themselves a &quot;gate&quot; and just something they do in their monasteries to focus their mind and soul). </div> </div> </div>That would be a mistake. As I said above, there are ways to express the idea that the Immaculate styles give DBs a sort of unique enlightenment and understanding (expressed as DB-only benefits that are flashy and impressive but which don't give you overwhelming raw power) while still letting Sidereals, Solars, etc. eke more raw power out of the style in certain ways.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, if you want to play a character who is all about being the <i>best</i> in terms of raw power, and who judges their competence based on being the best in raw power at their specialty, DBs are not the splat for you. People hate Solars for expressing that theme, but then they turn around and try to measure Dragon-Blooded by the same yardstick, and it's a mistake. That's not what the Dragon-Blooded are for (and that's, therefore, not what they'd get out of the Immaculate Style -- although it should of course still be <i>one of</i> the best options for them, just not head-and-shoulders above everything else.) Their connection to the Immaculate styles is, partially, spiritual in nature, so the benefits they get with them are not necessarily going to be of the same sort of raw power that a Sidereal or Solar who practices the styles will be able to express.<br /> <br /> I will be pretty blunt here: I believe that part of the reason DBs have the Immaculate Styles is so they go up against Anathema who have learned it (which means sometimes losing and shouting &quot;it cannot be!&quot;) Like, that's literally the main thing the Immaculate Styles offer over other charms. It's not the only reason they exist by a long shot (the monastic structure is important), but if you didn't want that, you could have the Immaculates teach secret Dragon-Blooded charms or somesuch rather than Martial Arts. If you're playing a DB, you get to turn this around and beat down the upstart Anathema who profanes your sacred techniques -- but it's supposed to be <i>hard</i>. It's not supposed to be &quot;haha, thank goodness this idiot Anathema wasted his time learning the Immaculate styles; that makes him much easier to beat down than other Anathema!&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea that the Immaculate Styles are just for Dragon-Blooded is an in-setting conceit. In terms of the stories they're meant to tell, they are <i>intended</i> to be sometimes used in ways that violate this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-02-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:10:31-07:00","id":859128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856054#post856054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't get to claim a martial art as yours like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they totally can. This is a new edition, so the devs can rewrite as much of the settings or systems as they feel like. If they wanted to write in that the DB's invented the immaculte styles all on their own and centered them around their elemental essences, which are fundamentally different from celestial essences, and so gain no particular benefit from being used by celestial exalts, then thats absolutely a thing they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:35:52-07:00","id":859139,"title":"","content":"It's already been stated that DBs can rival Solar-level competence in a specialized field, so it's entirely possible that the Immaculate Styles would be Just As Powerful as other styles, just more focused on a more specific set of principles, like foregoing protection against [element] in favor of offering more combo-able offensive charms.<br /> <br /> Like, if Water Dragon Style gets Drowning On Land Technique*, it could be entirely legitimate to say &quot;if the Exalt can't create water through their own magic, they need a source of it to stuff down their target's throat.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or if Fire Dragon Style uses Flaming Palm and Fire Breath and doesn't protect the Martial Artist against their own fire because it assumes they are already fireproof.<br /> <br /> Or if Air Dragon Style uses super high jump-and-throws for compounding falling damage and assumes that the M-Artist is already immune to falling damage, so it forgoes offering such protection to have more offensive effects because &quot;if you can't land safely from a 50-story fall why the hell are you learning this style?&quot; (and yes, this would assume that the DBs have their Animas active, because if they're slaying anathema honestly why wouldn't they?).<br /> <br /> (these may have already been stated? I skipped a few pages...)<br /> <br /> They wouldn't be *less* effective for Solars (or Sidereals or Lunars) but they <i>would</i> need to compensate with other powers, as would out-of-element DBs, which is also fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> *no, I don't mean Drowning in Blood technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-04-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:54:11-07:00","id":859150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859139#post859139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already been stated that DBs can rival Solar-level competence is a specialized field, so it's entirely possible that the Immaculate Styles would be Just As Powerful as other styles, just more focused on a more specific set of principles, like foregoing protection against [element] in favor of offering more combo-able offensive charms.<br /> <br /> Like, if Water Dragon Style gets Drowning On Land Technique*, it could be entirely legitimate to say &quot;if the Exalt can't create water through their own magic, they need a source of it to stuff down their target's throat.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or if Fire Dragon Style uses Flaming Palm and Fire Breath and doesn't protect the Martial Artist against their own fire because it assumes they are already fireproof.<br /> <br /> Or if Air Dragon Style uses super high jump-and-throws for compounding falling damage and assumes that the M-Artist is already immune to falling damage, so it forgoes offering such protection to have more offensive effects because &quot;if you can't land safely from a 50-story fall why the hell are you learning this style?&quot; (and yes, this would assume that the DBs have their Animas active, because if they're slaying anathema honestly why wouldn't they?).<br /> <br /> (these may have already been stated? I skipped a few pages...)<br /> <br /> They wouldn't be *less* effective for Solars (or Sidereals or Lunars) but they <i>would</i> need to compensate with other powers, as would out-of-element DBs, which is also fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> *no, I don't mean Drowning in Blood technique</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First of , Immaculate styles has been created to deal with spirits and gods, not against anathema. Secondly, if we really want the styles to be better for dragonblooded, it should capture the essence to the DB, which is stronger together, not personal power. Let them have synergies, when performed together. Let them have a Distract gambit like charms, but with specifics that require other trained exalted nearby. They should amplfy dragonblooded strengths. Maybe a cooperative keyword, like mastery but for DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:54:53-07:00","id":859151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859139#post859139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I like you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:14:08-07:00","id":859159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of , Immaculate styles has been created to deal with spirits and gods, not against anathema. </div> </div> </div> *shrugs* same deal: why <i>wouldn't</i> you activate your elemental banner when you're going in for a fight? Unlike Solars, DB banners offer very few social disadvatages.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859150#post859150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, if we really want the styles to be better for dragonblooded, it should capture the essence to the DB, which is stronger together, not personal power. Let them have synergies, when performed together. Let them have a Distract gambit like charms, but with specifics that require other trained exalted nearby. They should amplfy dragonblooded strengths. Maybe a cooperative keyword, like mastery but for DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they're primarily <i>elemental</i> demigods using <i>elemental</i> styles. Teamwork is somewhat secondary to that (though still present), so it would probably manifest more as an inter-style synergy instead of an overt keyword. I think I'd personally prefer that. The actual teamwork aspect is probably better represented in their native charmset.<br /> <br /> Like 5 MArtists attacking one target, one binding them in stone, one drowning them, one poisoning them, one setting them on fire and throwing them into the air and the fifth smashing them to the ground like the flaming comet they've been made into.<br /> <br /> Or something. idunno. This is a very rough example off the top of my head, something that interacts more granularly with the combat system would obviously be more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:33:16-07:00","id":859169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859159#post859159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like 5 MArtists attacking one target, one binding them in stone, one drowning them, one poisoning them, one setting them on fire and throwing them into the air and the fifth smashing them to the ground like the flaming comet they've been made into.<br /> <br /> Or something. idunno. This is a very rough example off the top of my head, something that interacts more granularly with the combat system would obviously be more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of exist in the QC antagonists that we already have. Air aspect knocks them down, then the earth aspect hits them. These aren't versions of the charms that we're going to see in the DB book, but it's something I noticed when designing encounters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:51:55-07:00","id":859183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859139#post859139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Clever stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:58:52-07:00","id":859194,"title":"","content":"To expound on things a little, I think the worries are non existent. Solars being the strongest exalts has never meant that they have to beat everyone else at a contest on anything. Sidereals can use the loom of fate and solars can't. Are sidereals stronger then solars? No, because the benefits that sidereals get from using the loom of fate aren't larger than the benefits that solars get from their native excellence. Lunars can shapeshift and solars cant. Does this make lunars stronger than solars? No, because the benefits that lunars get from shapeshifting aren't larger than the benefits that solars get from their native excellence. <br /> <br /> DB's could be better than solars at using the immaculate styles and using their heirlooms and still be weaker than solars. Those two facts can coexist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:03:00-07:00","id":859198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859151#post859151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like you.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859183#post859183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://38.media.tumblr.com/2343e47f063f8801e05281d651ef1382/tumblr_inline_nq56jqsA8Y1tpivvu_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:14:54-07:00","id":859210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=858005#post858005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your question is &quot;why learn the Immaculate Styles and not something else,&quot; though, let me flip that around and ask you this: Do you want a game where the situation is &quot;why learn anything but the Immaculate Styles?&quot; Do you want a DB who learns Melee and not the Immaculate Styles to be noticeably weaker in combat than an Immaculate stylist?<br /> <br /> This is something the game did in the past, yes. I don't think it was a good decision (in practice it resulted in players contorting themselves to explain why their DB had Immaculate MA even when it made no sense; and thematically it lead to players viewing the Immaculate Styles as the &quot;real&quot; pinnacle of DB power, which I don't think they were ever meant to be.) The Immaculate Martial Arts are supposed to be a big deal, but they shouldn't express this at the expense of Dragon-Blooded Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of shied away from reading and commenting on your response first time round (because the whole thread was a bit exhausting). I sort of don't want to reply to whole post (even though there's quite a bit I doesn't quite feel right to me) because that feels sort of shitty and Captain Hindsight now the dialogue around this question has moved on.<br /> <br /> For this though specifically I did want to comment that the theme in the earlier edition I think, for the Immaculate Martial Arts was that they had restrictions in learning - like vegan diets (even though this isn't Scott Pilgrim), meditation and so on - that made them unattractive for a Dragonblooded living a normal worldly lifestyle. Also that they were relatively expensive and their chief advantage was pretty much in upfront power in small scale combat against spirits (their most common opponents) or Anathema, giving less relative advantage to combat against other Dragonblooded and other enemies at a normal Dragonblooded scale, and less flexibility than the swashbuckler has on his path.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is still workable, but I do if so that think that rather than just level them with Melee (or do anything close) I guess notionally think I'd really rather if possible that this route - upfront power against spirits and Anathema (and obviously the latter is still quite unfavourable), at the cost of an otherwordliness to the character (perhaps mechanically expressed) and less extra utility against non-spirits - was implemented for 3e. A distinct cost that makes them not *that* useful and desirable for most Dragonblooded playing the Great Game of society, empire and adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:25:23-07:00","id":859218,"title":"","content":"Well, they're still going to require a 4-point merit, and for a DB that usually means having to choose between losing either Resources, Backing, Artifact, Arsenal, Influence, or whatever else.<br /> <br /> Which could be further compounded if their version of the martial artist merit <i>requires </i>them to forgo wealth (resources) or temporal power (backing) completely, in a pious-monk sort of way.<br /> <br /> It's not as though the charms were as easy to pick up as Melee. Melee doesn't require 4 Merit dots simply to get access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:42:07-07:00","id":859261,"title":"","content":"4 merit dots is a fairly trivial cost compared to the investment required to get good at a martial art.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure there are no &quot;versions&quot; of the martial artist merit. After all, the characters with the most compelling reason to have a different version (mortals) don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:32:04-07:00","id":859320,"title":"","content":"In the past immaculate MAs had higher XP costs and you got less from chargen and they had two gateway charms, if they add in another 4 dot merit that you need to take along side your MA merit that you need to access the immaculate styles I think that puts a big enough to weight on them to dissuade most non-celestial from taking them for power reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:32:06-07:00","id":859966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=859261#post859261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 merit dots is a fairly trivial cost compared to the investment required to get good at a martial art.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure there are no &quot;versions&quot; of the martial artist merit. After all, the characters with the most compelling reason to have a different version (mortals) don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not unthinkable that the Cloister would demand a specific regiment of their would-be students before allowing them to learn their martial arts. It's not like this would be a new thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T19:44:31-07:00","id":860059,"title":"","content":"I don't think you're likely to see Immaculate styles balanced by XP / chargen taxes (of the &quot;take these pointless prerequisites purely to be able to access Immaculate MA&quot; or &quot;you must build your character in exactly this way to access Immaculate MA&quot; style.) There's already the Martial Arts merit and the individual abilities for each Martial Art; if you take it too much further, you end up with anyone who wants to start as an Immaculate having like one charm in their style and sucking at everything else. (This was a problem in earlier versions which, IIRC, they want to fix.)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the balance-point for the Immaculate styles should be &quot;how can this be as fun as possible for everyone who wants to tell stories with it?&quot; And the best way to do that is to make it clearly &quot;Dragon-Blooded&quot; in character, somehow, while still leaving it open as an option for other people without making it pants-on-head idiotic for them; and to aim for a balance point where playing an Immaculate doesn't require sacrificing most of the rest of your character sheet on some sort of grim altar to fun.<br /> <br /> I mean, Immaculate MA shouldn't be a dominating option for DBs; but it's a big deal for them conceptually, so it should be a <i>strong</i> option, and one that is intrinsically appealing to players (just not so appealing that it encourages them to completely ignore Melee.) Excessive XP / chargen taxes aren't a good idea for something that, in a typical DB circle, you'd expect at least one or two people to take.<br /> <br /> (The other problem with using high XP charges to balance stuff is that in my experience it rarely <i>works</i>. If you made Immaculate MA much more powerful than Melee but gated it behind some sort of high XP investment, what you'd see is people either never taking it at all or gritting their teeth and plowing through it and not really enjoying it, which is bad for everyone involved.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-06-2016, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:29:37-07:00","id":860081,"title":"","content":"I don't know, in my experience the slightly-higher cost of Immaculate Martial Arts did seem to make it a genuine choice, so some people would have them but most wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:49:51-07:00","id":860135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=860081#post860081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, in my experience the slightly-higher cost of Immaculate Martial Arts did seem to make it a genuine choice, so some people would have them but most wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I've seen exactly one DB take Immaculate Martial Arts in all my many many years of playing exalted. It definitely seemed to turn people off taking it just for the power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:00:27-07:00","id":860137,"title":"","content":"I've seen a few monks take it (obviously), but I think I only saw 2 characters take it with non-monks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T03:57:25-07:00","id":861727,"title":"","content":"Earlier someone made the point that taking an immaculate martial art shouldn't be a trap for solars and taking snake style shouldn't be a trap for terrestrials.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly in agreement with the second point. DB's should be able to take advantage of the diversity of martial arts without being penalized. However the first point, that a solar who studies earth dragon style shouldn't be a chump compared to one who studies tiger style, I can live without. As long as the immaculate styles are clearly labeled as sub-optimal for characters that can use mastery versions of martial arts I don't see an issue with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 04-08-2016, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:44:59-07:00","id":861741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=861727#post861727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">trap solars terrestrials penalized solar chump compared sub-optimal</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is a chump, nothing is a trap. There is no Parallel Dawn competing with your PC, except played by a supercomputer programmed to only build the most efficient, most optimal combat suite (and only make the optimal tactical choice on every turn of the game, being ready not only to throw down with your PC in white-room paranoia combat, but to win).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=861727#post861727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see an issue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing the character you want to play and having fun, there is no issue - you've made the optimal decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-08-2016, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:14:36-07:00","id":861887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=861741#post861741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is a chump, nothing is a trap. There is no Parallel Dawn competing with your PC, except played by a supercomputer programmed to only build the most efficient, most optimal combat suite (and only make the optimal tactical choice on every turn of the game, being ready not only to throw down with your PC in white-room paranoia combat, but to win).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is a mischaracterization of the issue. If you're playing in a game with other players and the xp that you've spent to enable your character to do cool stuff during combat scenes does a good deal less than the xp that other players have spent to have their characters do cool stuff in combat scenes it is a bit disappointing. I've played in games where the level of optimization between different characters was significantly different and it was somewhat annoying. <br /> <br /> Claiming that this annoyance can't possibly be real is not helpful.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T19:59:30-07:00","id":866626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856525#post856525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Guancyto<br /> <br /> That would not be a Martial Art, which in Exalted's definition consists of techniques which use a human physiology to perform. What you got are custom snake themed whatever attribute Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the Pterok Dragon Kings, who have a Martial Art which is worthless to anyone without wings.<br /> <br /> I talked to the devs about this. You can totally have an animal Style designed to be used in that animal's form. It's just that they're never going to write one, because a Style for people in snake forms is ridiculously niche.<br /> <br /> The Pterok Style (Dagger Wing Style), on the other hand, is already written, only needs to be converted, is needed to complete the circle of Dragon King Martial Art Styles, and would work for anyone who gets wings via artifacts, spells, shapeshifting, or Wyld Mutations. Which is a fair bit less niche than &quot;people who have no limbs at all&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:44:19-07:00","id":866644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856793#post856793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it like this. A snake wouldn't make a style representing the movements of a snake, it would just move. If you already have the hood, scales, and fangs of a cobra, there is nothing more that martial arts can do to make you cobra like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then a human wouldn't make a style representing the movements of a human.<br /> <br /> Yet, we could have a Boxing Style, or a Tae Kwando/Capoeira/Kick-Dancing Style.<br /> <br /> The human already has fists and feet, and there are no ways to make him more human-like, yet there are still ways for him to fight more effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:46:14-07:00","id":866664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866626#post866626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... It's just that they're never going to write one...</div> </div> </div> </div>So any that will ever exist will be home brew, something that I don't really discuss, as I don't see the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:49:50-07:00","id":866666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866664#post866664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So any that will ever exist will be home brew, something that I don't really discuss, as I don't see the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You saw enough of a point to tell SaurOps that a Lunar with a snake form couldn't make such a Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:10:31-07:00","id":866674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866666#post866666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You saw enough of a point to tell SaurOps that a Lunar with a snake form couldn't make such a Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point being that none of that would show up in a book, so why bother?<br /> <br /> Like you said the developers told you no MA will be published that requires an inhuman form to use (Who knows about DKs? We'll have to wait, probably a long time, to see). So any instance of getting combat power from using a snake's physical systems will probably be through Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> For the written material we have the point is Solars are masters of Abilities. If there is something that a Solar cannot master it is not an Ability.<br /> <br /> If you can point me to a published material that contradicts that, I will gladly retract my statement and try to make sense of the new situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:25:52-07:00","id":866677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866674#post866674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point being that none of that would show up in a book, so why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because homebrew.<br /> <br /> Whether or not something is POSSIBLE or PERMISSIBLE makes a big deal in the realm of homebrew.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also because the principle WILL show up in official material, as soon as they get around to Dagger Wing Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:28:29-07:00","id":866678,"title":"","content":"I think that the Solar concept of excellence can handle a few degenerate edge cases in the face of 25 basic groups and an indeterminate quantity more of special cases, which will only increase dramatically in number as time goes on in comparison to, say, a few specific Dragon King styles and various odds and ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:50:28-07:00","id":866699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866677#post866677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because homebrew.<br /> <br /> Whether or not something is POSSIBLE or PERMISSIBLE makes a big deal in the realm of homebrew.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also because the principle WILL show up in official material, as soon as they get around to Dagger Wing Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see Dagger Wing Style as something that needs a tool to be used, like Archery or Single Point Shining Into the Void Style. So if someone got their hands on somehow functioning wings, they should be able to practice it and a Solar should be able to master it. So I don't see it as changing anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866678#post866678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Solar concept of excellence can handle a few degenerate edge cases in the face of 25 basic groups and an indeterminate quantity more of special cases, which will only increase dramatically in number as time goes on in comparison to, say, a few specific Dragon King styles and various odds and ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what we got so far, I just don't see it. If it is an Ability a Solar should be able to use it and master it. Note that I'm not saying that the outcome of a Solar using should be better than anyone else using it, just that to the extent that it is an Ability it should be learnable, usable, masterable by a Solar (note: I know some of those words don't exist, but y'all get the point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T07:00:35-07:00","id":866807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866699#post866699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see Dagger Wing Style as something that needs a tool to be used, like Archery or Single Point Shining Into the Void Style. So if someone got their hands on somehow functioning wings, they should be able to practice it and a Solar should be able to master it. So I don't see it as changing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what if the same thing applies to the Immaculate Styles?<br /> <br /> What if a Solar needs a fire-producing/controlling/immunity-granting tool to use Fire Dragon Style as easily as a Fire Aspect Terrestrial who can generate, control, and survive fire without a tool?<br /> <br /> It would be just like how a Solar needs a winged-backpack Artifact in order to practice Dagger Wing Style.<br /> <br /> <br /> But to be fair, I'm not saying that the Immaculate Styles should lack the Mastery keyword.<br /> <br /> I think I heard that the devs/writers specifically WANT to leave the Mastery keyword out of the Styles? And I'm willing to wait and see how they do that. But I'm right there with everyone else when I say I have NO IDEA how they intend to balance the Styles without the Mastery keyword.<br /> <br /> On the other hand... I don't care.<br /> <br /> Someone was saying that if the Immaculate Styles are simply, straight-up denied any Mastery effects, that the Immaculate Styles would be the weakest in Creation... but, that's only true for the Solar Exalted. It's very much NOT true for the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> And WHO are the Styles being made for, both in and out of the setting? The Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> The game has ALWAYS (or at least since Second Edition) gone out of its way to reward an Immaculate stylist, in little ways, for being a Terrestrial Exalt rather than a Solar. There were some perks I don't remember, regarding the style weapons.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted have EVERY OTHER Martial Arts Style in the world to enjoy Mastery. Plus, it's not like the Immaculate Styles would be alone -- there are also these weird SIDEREAL Martial Arts that play by different rules which don't favor the Solar Exalted the most.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, both the Immaculate and Sidereal Styles were made by the same Exalted Host! If the Sidereals could invent the Sidereal Martial Arts where they reign supreme over Solars, I'm willing to believe they can invent Immaculate Styles where Dragon-Blooded can achieve better results than Solars.<br /> <br /> That's not the same thing as &quot;Styles which allow Dragon-Blooded to fight Solars as superiors or even equals&quot;, mind you, because dice-pools, mote-pools, native Charms, XP-costs, and the Supernal Ability all remain a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T07:17:47-07:00","id":866815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866699#post866699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what we got so far, I just don't see it. If it is an Ability a Solar should be able to use it and master it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Solars are specifically described as the masters of <b>mortal</b> ability. Becoming and manipulating fire isn't a mortal ability. It's a Terrestrial Exalted one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:02:32-07:00","id":866832,"title":"","content":"@Sunder the Gold<br /> <br /> I'm not a SMA scholar, but from what I understood Solars need Sidereals to learn the SMA, but then could be their equal, or even better.<br /> <br /> Like I stated before, I don't believe a Solar must have a better outcome when applying an Ability. I just think, from my perspective of consistency, that this better outcome should not come from a mastery of the Ability that a Solar cannot achieve. I belive it should come from some inherent quality of the user.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866815#post866815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Solars are specifically described as the masters of <b>mortal</b> ability. Becoming and manipulating fire isn't a mortal ability. It's a Terrestrial Exalted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very valid point. It will be interesting to see if specifically inhuman Abilities will be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:04:34-07:00","id":866833,"title":"","content":"Here's a crazy idea.<br /> <br /> Remember how I said the Immaculate Styles are basically the elemental version of Sidereal Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> What if everyone who isn't a Terrestrial is absolute <i>pants</i> at the Immaculate Styles, EXCEPT for the Solar Exalted?<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Lunar Exalted could never even learn Sidereal Martial Arts, so what if the Immaculate Styles treat Celestial Exalted like <i>normal </i>Styles treat <i>Terrestrial </i>Exalted?<br /> <br /> &quot;If you don't have an elemental nature, you SUCK at these Styles&quot;. Lunars and Sidereals are stuck at the bottom level of potential for the Immaculate Styles, with the Sidereal Exalted using their &quot;achieve Mastery for normal Styles&quot; trick to perform any better.<br /> <br /> Solars could show how amazingly powerful they are, NOT by being better at Immaculate Styles than Terrestrials, but merely by managing to be better than anyone ELSE. JUST like how Solars are inferior at Sidereal Martial Arts, but still better than any non-Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:32:23-07:00","id":866849,"title":"","content":"You see, we've been presented with a new way to treat Martial Arts. They are Abilities that any &quot;mortal&quot; can practice, but only Essence users can extrapolate to supwrnatural power.<br /> <br /> While we don't know if this notion will be upheld throughout the game's development, that is what we have for now.<br /> <br /> So maintaining that line of thought, Solars should be able to take any MA to it's limit. For if it is an Ability, no matter how esoteric, a Solar should be able to get all that is possible out of it.<br /> <br /> I don't like the theme that someone can design an Ability that a Solar can't master. They might try and believe they can do it, but the greatness of the Solars' Essence will show they are wrong. <br /> <br /> If a MA enables a supernatural user to spit fire, the Solar should be able to dpit the greatest fire possible from that Ability. It might be the case that a Fire Aspect DB will get a greater flametongue out of it by boosting it with his Anima. But the greater power didn't come from some technique a Solar somehow can't master.<br /> <br /> I hope that you're into arguing semantics and game metaphysics, because that is basically what I'm doing with this subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T09:18:23-07:00","id":866867,"title":"","content":"<b>Note that the following theoretical hierarchies do not speak to power of any given Charm or Style, merely the ease with which characters can learn a Charm and access its full power (and even then, only its full power in a vacuum).<br /> <br /> <br /> Normal Styles</b><br /> Mortals --&gt; Terrestrials --&gt; Lunars/Alchemicals --&gt; Sidereals --&gt; Solars<br /> <br /> (Solars are the best at <i>learning </i>and using Martial Arts and winning kung fu duels)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal Styles</b><br /> Solars --&gt; Sidereals<br /> <br /> (Solars are somewhat inferior at <i>learning </i>and using Sidereal Martial Arts, but NO ONE ELSE CAN, and their other tools still give them the edge in kung fu duels)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Immaculate Styles</b><br /> <br /> Mortals? --&gt; Lunars/Alchemicals --&gt; Sidereals --&gt; Solars --&gt; Terrestrials<br /> <br /> (Solars are somewhat inferior at <i>learning </i>and using Immaculate Martial Arts, but they're still better than everyone who isn't a Dragon-Blood, and their other tools still give them the edge in kung fu duels)<br /> <br /> <br /> That's my theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T09:31:38-07:00","id":866875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866815#post866815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Solars are specifically described as the masters of <b>mortal</b> ability. Becoming and manipulating fire isn't a mortal ability. It's a Terrestrial Exalted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that there were already subtle elements of this in the Immaculate Styles.<br /> The pinnacle of Fire Dragon Style gives non-Fire Aspects their anima power but Fire Aspects get their existing Anima trippled in power. Factor in that 3e does more with Anima, including using anima levels for charm cost we might see more effects like that this time around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T09:38:35-07:00","id":866879,"title":"","content":"If those were hierarchies of outcome of using a skill with Ability mastery + inherent qualities I would agree with you. <br /> <br /> If they are hierarchies of Ability mastery I do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:21:18-07:00","id":866907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866879#post866879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those were hierarchies of outcome of using a skill with Ability mastery + inherent qualities I would agree with you.<br /> <br /> If they are hierarchies of Ability mastery I do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explain Sidereal Martial Arts, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:26:51-07:00","id":866910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866833#post866833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a crazy idea.<br /> <br /> Remember how I said the Immaculate Styles are basically the elemental version of Sidereal Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> What if everyone who isn't a Terrestrial is absolute <i>pants</i> at the Immaculate Styles, EXCEPT for the Solar Exalted?<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Lunar Exalted could never even learn Sidereal Martial Arts, so what if the Immaculate Styles treat Celestial Exalted like <i>normal </i>Styles treat <i>Terrestrial </i>Exalted?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;If you don't have an elemental nature, you SUCK at these Styles&amp;quot;. Lunars and Sidereals are stuck at the bottom level of potential for the Immaculate Styles, with the Sidereal Exalted using their &amp;quot;achieve Mastery for normal Styles&amp;quot; trick to perform any better.<br /> <br /> Solars could show how amazingly powerful they are, NOT by being better at Immaculate Styles than Terrestrials, but merely by managing to be better than anyone ELSE. JUST like how Solars are inferior at Sidereal Martial Arts, but still better than any non-Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it! Flip &quot;Terrestrial&quot; with &quot;Celestial&quot; and throw in &quot;Solars are the only ones who can ignore this keyword&quot;. Then Dragon-Blooded get the Mastery effect of the style. Simple, elegant.<br /> <br /> Well, except that Sidereals often practice the styles, right? Ignore them and the keyword becomes &quot;screw Lunars&quot;. Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:36:45-07:00","id":866914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866910#post866910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, except that Sidereals often practice the styles, right? Ignore them and the keyword becomes &amp;quot;screw Lunars&amp;quot;. Huh.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also Liminals, Alchemicals, possibly Getimians, all the Exalted types we know are going to show up but don't know anything about, a lot of Exigents, and potentially other supernatural MA users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:37:56-07:00","id":866915,"title":"","content":"I think there's still an overemphasis on a need of tiering and a need for every option to always be equally valid like this were a TCG or a wargame.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:53:58-07:00","id":866924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866907#post866907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain Sidereal Martial Arts, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>The statement I made on SMA is still valid. I don't know if you missed it, ignored it, or thought your reply was a valid retort.<br /> <br /> All we know is that Solars need Sidereals to learn SMAs. If the pupils will be able to match, or even exceed, the masters is still up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:22:58-07:00","id":866943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866915#post866915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's still an overemphasis on a need of tiering and a need for every option to always be equally valid like this were a TCG or a wargame.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think every single option needs to be balanced against eachother, but the really cool and common ones should be, especially since this one feels so unnecessary. DBs get a whole elemental charmset, they don't need to make sure IMA aren't better for Solars. Especially if it makes IMA look lame in comparison to every other martial art because it doesn't have the cool effects. Like how Tiger's capstone turns your anima into a raging beast that's so destructive and furious it literally rips apart your opponents anima! <br /> <br /> How cool would it be if the Fire Dragon Style capstone manifested your anima as a blazing, almost physical, creature that dealt withering damage whenever you attacked an opponent. Or something like that, I don't even know what cool stuff could be in there. I'm less concerned about the &quot;Mastery: add dexterity to the damage&quot; effects. I want them, but making the immaculate styles the least cool styles sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:52:37-07:00","id":866962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866833#post866833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a crazy idea.<br /> <br /> Remember how I said the Immaculate Styles are basically the elemental version of Sidereal Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> What if everyone who isn't a Terrestrial is absolute <i>pants</i> at the Immaculate Styles, EXCEPT for the Solar Exalted?<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Lunar Exalted could never even learn Sidereal Martial Arts,..</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they could when SMA was first released. It wasn't until the next hardback (the player's guide) that it got cut off. As they are now, the Lunars don't need it, but it definitely stung back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:16:21-07:00","id":866983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866943#post866943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think every single option needs to be balanced against eachother, but the really cool and common ones should be, especially since this one feels so unnecessary. DBs get a whole elemental charmset, they don't need to make sure IMA aren't better for Solars. Especially if it makes IMA look lame in comparison to every other martial art because it doesn't have the cool effects. Like how Tiger's capstone turns your anima into a raging beast that's so destructive and furious it literally rips apart your opponents anima!</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded get special elemental kung fu styles because they have always had special elemental kung fu styles. They aren't for Solars. Were never written or assumed to be for Solars. They might look lame for Solars? Am I supposed to feel bad about that something that Solars can take peripherally might not be so good for them? Or that I don't htink Redeemeed Immacualte #6,088 needs to have it be as compelling as other options for raw power, rather than aesthetics? SInce ultimately, that's what MAs are?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866943#post866943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How cool would it be if the Fire Dragon Style capstone manifested your anima as a blazing, almost physical, creature that dealt withering damage whenever you attacked an opponent. Or something like that, I don't even know what cool stuff could be in there. I'm less concerned about the &quot;Mastery: add dexterity to the damage&quot; effects. I want them, but making the immaculate styles the least cool styles sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of unstated assumptions as to what amounts to the least cool style and how the mechanics as presented so far (no special Mastery beenies for Solars) impact this. Since note, Dragon-Blooded get to do weird powerful shit wiht the styles out there now, unless I forgot something about being a gazelle-carp.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:36:38-07:00","id":866993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866983#post866983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded get special elemental kung fu styles because they have always had special elemental kung fu styles. They aren't for Solars. Were never written or assumed to be for Solars. They might look lame for Solars? Am I supposed to feel bad about that something that Solars can take peripherally might not be so good for them? Or that I don't htink Redeemeed Immacualte #6,088 needs to have it be as compelling as other options for raw power, rather than aesthetics? SInce ultimately, that's what MAs are?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Things were always this way&quot; is a particularly weak argument, specially when we're talking a new edition of something. While what you say may be one of things that do not change, it may also be one of those that do. I'm pretty certain the devs are giving this much thought and not just leaving it as is because that is how it has always been.<br /> <br /> I anxiously await the outcome on &quot;What Fire Has Wrought&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866983#post866983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of unstated assumptions as to what amounts to the least cool style and how the mechanics as presented so far (no special Mastery beenies for Solars) impact this. Since note, Dragon-Blooded get to do weird powerful shit wiht the styles out there now, unless I forgot something about being a gazelle-carp.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this I agree, not having Mastery doesn't necessarily mean it won't be cool. It will be interesting to see how they will alleviate the &quot;trap or one true build&quot; for DBs and other splats though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:45:15-07:00","id":866997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866993#post866993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this I agree, not having Mastery doesn't necessarily mean it won't be cool. It will be interesting to see how they will alleviate the &quot;trap or one true build&quot; for DBs and other splats though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the past it was resolved by giving Immaculate characters a crippling xp tax to learn Immaculate Charms and hobbling them at character creation.<br /> <br /> I hope there will be a better solution this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:58:01-07:00","id":867003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866993#post866993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Things were always this way&quot; is a particularly weak argument, specially when we're talking a new edition of something. While what you say may be one of things that do not change, it may also be one of those that do. I'm pretty certain the devs are giving this much thought and not just leaving it as is because that is how it has always been.<br /> <br /> I anxiously await the outcome on &quot;What Fire Has Wrought&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less &quot;They always have been this way&quot; and to me at least more &quot;This is why they were tehre in the first place.&quot; The entire idea of there being IMA is to give cool elemental kung fu styles to Dragon-Blooded. They aren't being created with an idea that they get to live in the toolbox for Solars to raid. As I gather, they're being made with an idea that the Exalt type they were invented for still has them as their signature thing. Solars can take it or leave it. They just aren't for them and I don't see this need for them to be designed such that they are as good an option for them as others.<br /> <br /> So it's not a matter of &quot;It's always been that way&quot; to me. It's a matter also of in part &quot;What about the alternative being presented is actually good?&quot; And I haven't been seeing a lot to convince me of that, especially in context of what MAs are as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866993#post866993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this I agree, not having Mastery doesn't necessarily mean it won't be cool. It will be interesting to see how they will alleviate the &quot;trap or one true build&quot; for DBs and other splats though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably some things not current present mechanically and also the fact that despite their power before, not everyone wants to play a monk or a dude with kung fu. If there were such stress on true builds and optimizations this edition I think you'd see more Melee Supernal Dawns around.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T13:32:40-07:00","id":867024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866962#post866962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, they could when SMA was first released. It wasn't until the next hardback (the player's guide) that it got cut off. As they are now, the Lunars don't need it, but it definitely stung back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Tornado Wolf. I <i>was </i>back in those days, and it DID sting. It was one of many stings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T14:44:21-07:00","id":867067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=866815#post866815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Solars are specifically described as the masters of <b>mortal</b> ability. Becoming and manipulating fire isn't a mortal ability. It's a Terrestrial Exalted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true, I don't think that is a good justification to deny Solar capacity in Immaculate styles, unless you are saying manipulating fire is somehow significantly less of a human ability than becoming a Gazelle-carp or commanding somebody's shadow to kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:01:26-07:00","id":867083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867067#post867067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While that is true, I don't think that is a good justification to deny Solar capacity in Immaculate styles</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is denying solars the styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> unless you are saying manipulating fire is somehow significantly less of a human ability than becoming a Gazelle-carp or commanding somebody's shadow to kill them. </div> </div> </div>Invoking the Chimera's Coils doesn't have the Mastery Keyword.<br /> Umbra Noose Execution doesn't depend on the Solar being a shadow.<br /> Note that Shadow-Stepping Motion and Shadow Body Dissolution, which conceivably <i>would</i> be helped by being made of shadow, also lack Mastery keywords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:02:14-07:00","id":867084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867067#post867067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that is true, I don't think that is a good justification to deny Solar capacity in Immaculate styles, unless you are saying manipulating fire is somehow significantly less of a human ability than becoming a Gazelle-carp or commanding somebody's shadow to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, manipulating fire is <i>definitely </i>more in the wheelhouse of a fire aspect than it is a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:05:29-07:00","id":867087,"title":"","content":"Solars are probably going to be better at actually using the Charms, as a note. What you know the better Excellency, 6-17 additional motes for the same dots of Essence, access to Mastery effects for all MAs to mix and match with the IMAs and so on. They just won't get a couple beenies in using them extra, which DBs might get. And we don't know the nature of those DB effects and whether they actually make them better at indivdiual Charms per se or better at the tactis of the styles or have effects a Solar wasn't going to get anyhow (like the enhanced Fire anima of Fire Dragon Style historically). Also, Dawns with MAs Supernal can master Fire Dragon style in the span of a year, rather than you know, a lifetime as in the case of Terrestrial masters.<br /> <br /> Nothing really denies Solars the IMA. The main rejection from folks at least like me is that they should somehow be substantially better than DBs at them or that DBs, who the styles were invented for both OOCly and ICly, shouldn't get any beenie a Solar couldn't also get.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:06:37-07:00","id":867089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867083#post867083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invoking the Chimera's Coils doesn't have the Mastery Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does. The description of the effect lists it under Terrestrial and the actual Terrestrial effect under Celestial, but it's definitely there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:08:37-07:00","id":867091,"title":"","content":"Also, re: Ebon Shadow, it's conceivably still within Solar Mastery because the &quot;brightest lights (i.e. the Sun) cast the deepest shadows&quot; and whatnot. You know, Night castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:11:00-07:00","id":867092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867089#post867089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it does. The description of the effect lists it under Terrestrial and the actual Terrestrial effect under Celestial, but it's definitely there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial \u2260 Mastery.<br /> &quot;All Celestial Exalted can do X&quot; does not equal &quot;Solars get this effect for being the best at everything&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:13:44-07:00","id":867096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867003#post867003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's less &quot;They always have been this way&quot; and to me at least more &quot;This is why they were tehre in the first place.&quot; The entire idea of there being IMA is to give cool elemental kung fu styles to Dragon-Blooded. They aren't being created with an idea that they get to live in the toolbox for Solars to raid. As I gather, they're being made with an idea that the Exalt type they were invented for still has them as their signature thing. Solars can take it or leave it. They just aren't for them and I don't see this need for them to be designed such that they are as good an option for them as others.<br /> <br /> So it's not a matter of &quot;It's always been that way&quot; to me. It's a matter also of in part &quot;What about the alternative being presented is actually good?&quot; And I haven't been seeing a lot to convince me of that, especially in context of what MAs are as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably some things not current present mechanically and also the fact that despite their power before, not everyone wants to play a monk or a dude with kung fu. If there were such stress on true builds and optimizations this edition I think you'd see more Melee Supernal Dawns around.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll just have to wait and see if IMAs will be so completely different from other MAs, as in not having mortal practitioners and such.<br /> <br /> To me its just a matter of consistency,<br /> <br /> Like I said previously I'm not fond of the idea of designing a MA that a Solar can't excel at. Its like telling me you're going to design a logic test for dogs that chimps aren't able to excel at, while I may be surprised and find out that it exists, its just against the widely known paradigm. <br /> <br /> You can tell me the dog gets better results because the test involves the sense of smell, but when you get to the logic part the chimp will be better.<br /> <br /> As long as IMAs share the new context of MAs that we've seen so far, that there are mortal practitioners that have the Ability without having Charms, I don't see how they should break away from the others.<br /> <br /> Also this deal about &quot;Solars have everything else, let DBs have this one thing!&quot; is pretty sorry. DBs are not the kid in the yard that needs a special toy so they can be special.<br /> <br /> They have Elemental Power, The World's Largest Panoply and Arsenal, The Realm Itself, Numbers and Organization. They are billed as Creation's premiere, dominant Exalted. They don't need a bone thrown their way, They eat the steaks.<br /> <br /> Lets hope this edition does them justice through writing them how they should be. Not by treating them like chumps that need to be pandered to to be relevant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:18:39-07:00","id":867101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867083#post867083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is denying solars the styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invoking the Chimera's Coils doesn't have the Mastery Keyword. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, ok, bad example<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbra Noose Execution doesn't depend on the Solar being a shadow.<br /> Note that Shadow-Stepping Motion and Shadow Body Dissolution, which conceivably <i>would</i> be helped by being made of shadow, also lack Mastery keywords. </div> </div> </div>Observe that the post I quoted include become<b> and manipulate fire</b>. Making your shadow kill you surely must count as manipulating it. Should the Dragon styles not have any charms that manipulate their element, just ones to become that element, then?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(complete aside, but for all that I like Avatar, I'd actually prefer the Immaculate MAs to remain not doing overt bender stuff - I liked that they were more metaphorical than that a lot of the time)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:25:02-07:00","id":867105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867101#post867101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observe that the post I quoted include become<b> and manipulate fire</b>. Making your shadow kill you surely must count as manipulating it. Should the Dragon styles not have any charms that manipulate their element, just ones to become that element, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Night castes are about the abscence of Sun, so it seems fitting that there'd be a Style that deals with Shadows that the Solars can master.<br /> And I mean, ultimately it's entirely possible that it (and any other Style) having a Mastery keyword depends more on &quot;oh man this would be really cool!&quot; rather than &quot;Solars must win at everything forever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:25:07-07:00","id":867106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867092#post867092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial \u2260 Mastery.<br /> &quot;All Celestial Exalted can do X&quot; does not equal &quot;Solars get this effect for being the best at everything&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The keywords section of the charm show that it has Mastery and Terrestrial. The Celestial keyword doesn't exist, but during an earlier version (including the playtest leak) the Terrestrial keyword was called Celestial instead (as in Celestial Martial Arts, presumably). Given that the Terrestrial keyword describes the Mastery effect, and the incorrect Celestial keyword describes the Terrestrial effect, it's not hard to figure out that they replaced Celestial with Terrestrial in the keywords line but accidentally replaced Mastery with Terrestrial in the main description instead of replacing Celestial with it. The snark is appreciated, but you're wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:28:56-07:00","id":867107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867106#post867106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The keywords section of the charm show that it has Mastery and Terrestrial. The Celestial keyword doesn't exist, but during an earlier version (including the playtest leak) the Terrestrial keyword was called Celestial instead (as in Celestial Martial Arts, presumably). Given that the Terrestrial keyword describes the Mastery effect, and the incorrect Celestial keyword describes the Terrestrial effect, it's not hard to figure out that they replaced Celestial with Terrestrial in the keywords line but accidentally replaced Mastery with Terrestrial in the main description instead of replacing Celestial with it. The snark is appreciated, but you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, seems like you're right. I missed the fact that Celestial got taken out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:31:03-07:00","id":867111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867089#post867089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it does. The description of the effect lists it under Terrestrial and the actual Terrestrial effect under Celestial, but it's definitely there.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867092#post867092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial \u2260 Mastery.<br /> &quot;All Celestial Exalted can do X&quot; does not equal &quot;Solars get this effect for being the best at everything&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I take a better look at it, something is wrong there. Lanaya appear to be right.<br /> First, the &quot;Terrestrial&quot; bit makes the Charm more powerful, not less, unlike every other Terrestrial-keyword charm in the book.<br /> Second, the &quot;celestial&quot; is <i>explicitly </i>about dragon-blooded.<br /> Third, there is<i> no such a thing</i> as a Celestial Keyword, as unlike Terrestrial and Mastery it is not defined as a system term in the MA section.<br /> And finally fourth, the Charm lists Terrestrial and Mastery on the Keywords line.<br /> <br /> So, I'm adding back &quot;becoming a divine-gazelle-carp-thingie&quot; to my argument ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:33:32-07:00","id":867113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867105#post867105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. Night castes are about the abscence of Sun, so it seems fitting that there'd be a Style that deals with Shadows that the Solars can master.<br /> And I mean, ultimately it's entirely possible that it (and any other Style) having a Mastery keyword depends more on &quot;oh man this would be really cool!&quot; rather than &quot;Solars must win at everything forever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this line of thought is straining. What does Solar Essence have to do with animals, demons, songs and etiquette that it doesn't have to do with elements?<br /> <br /> The answer is pretty obvious, so far there doesn't need to be any synergy between a Style's theme and the Exalted's Essence for them to be learned, used and mastered.<br /> <br /> The jury is still out for IMAs. But the Core Styles have nothing at all to do with this line of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:35:27-07:00","id":867115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867111#post867111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Now that I take a better look at it, something is wrong there. Lanaya appear to be right.<br /> First, the &quot;Terrestrial&quot; bit makes the Charm more powerful, not less, unlike every other Terrestrial-keyword charm in the book.<br /> Second, the &quot;celestial&quot; is <i>explicitly </i>about dragon-blooded.<br /> Third, there is<i> no such a thing</i> as a Celestial Keyword, as unlike Terrestrial and Mastery it is not defined as a system term in the MA section.<br /> And finally fourth, the Charm lists Terrestrial and Mastery on the Keywords line.<br /> <br /> So, I'm adding back &quot;becoming a divine-gazelle-carp-thingie&quot; to my argument ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was discussed in the errata threads and I believe is pretty well established that it will be fixed, as in yes Lanaya's comments are the accepted consensus on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:36:05-07:00","id":867116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867111#post867111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm adding back &quot;becoming a divine-gazelle-carp-thingie&quot; to my argument ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, there isn't a Splat that can conceivably do Gazelle-Carp better, because even though it changes you, it's a divine expression of your soul, not Shapeshifting. And solars are pretty friggin apt at divine expressions of their soul - Glorious Solar Plate, Saber and Bow - and indeed, have the most glorious souls to show off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-17-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:48:46-07:00","id":867126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867113#post867113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this line of thought is straining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you find the fact that &quot;Night&quot; is a caste for Solar Exalted straining?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867113#post867113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does Solar Essence have to do with animals, demons</div> </div> </div> </div>Training animals is a skill. I'm at a loss for what you're referring to with &quot;demons&quot;. If you mean Steel Devil or Righteous Devil, note that they focus on <i>weapons</i>, which require <b>skill</b> to wield.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867113#post867113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">songs and etiquette</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal skills.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867113#post867113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that it doesn't have to do with elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are &quot;doing&quot; while Elements are &quot;being&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867113#post867113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is pretty obvious, so far there doesn't need to be any synergy between a Style's theme and the Exalted's Essence for them to be learned, used and mastered.<br /> <br /> The jury is still out for IMAs. But the Core Styles have nothing at all to do with this line of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token, Solars not getting special benefits with IMA is already the design intent, so that's like, your opinion, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:50:06-07:00","id":867127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867116#post867116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, there isn't a Splat that can conceivably do Gazelle-Carp better, because even though it changes you, it's a divine expression of your soul, not Shapeshifting. And solars are pretty friggin apt at divine expressions of their soul - Glorious Solar Plate, Saber and Bow - and indeed, have the most glorious souls to show off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still ignoring the fact that the Core Styles have no consideration if the Style's theme resonate with the Exalted using it. All its says is the Solars are the best at MAs and that Sidereals can match them under certain circumstances. All else is speculation, and this one in particular a very poorly supported one.<br /> <br /> The Style could be about being more pumpkin like and inspiring terror like a Jack 'o' Lantern and if it was in the Core it would have Mastery effects for Solars and eventual Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:53:04-07:00","id":867128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867127#post867127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All its says is the Solars are the best at MAs and that Sidereals can match them under certain circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not getting Mastery doesn't contradict that. As illustrated earlier, even if Terrestrials got bonuses that Solars didn't, Solars would still be better a the styles simply due to how much better their Excellencies, which they get for free, are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:58:16-07:00","id":867132,"title":"","content":"The thing for me is that I expect Solars to be the best (or tied for best) with any given Ability, <i>when taken as a whole</i>. Now, I don't mind if some splat can surpass Solars in a specific niche within that ability. Maybe Alchemicals can mass craft identical mundane items better/faster than a solar or something.<br /> <br /> So, why not be fine with DBs being better than Solars at 5 out of all Martial Arts? Well, there are two things going on here:<br /> <br /> First, the system partially treating each MA as a separate Ability kind of leads me to consider that Solars should be able to do their thing at each of them. The Dragon Styles don't feel like niches within an Ability, but closer to 5 distinct Abilities to me.<br /> <br /> Second, I wouldn't actually mind if the Terrestrials were better at it. The proposed idea for implementation is what feels wrong to me. If they worked better for DBs due to synergies with their Anima Banners, Aspect Powers, Native Charms or something like that, I'd be applauding it as great design. Instead, we get Solars unable to fully master the styles to the same extent they can with every other MA Ability, and that doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> Like, If the Solars could show off their unsurpassed skill by mastering the techniques better than DBs, like in every other MA, but DBs still did better when using it because they were made for DBs and thus take advantage of things only DBs have? I would actually really like that dynamic <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(as long as there are balance checks in place for the difficulty and resources spent to acquire them so that DBs picking any other MA don't feel like chumps)</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:59:51-07:00","id":867135,"title":"","content":"The Solar excellency isn't <i>that </i>awe-inspiringly powerful any more. Lunars can easily match or even exceed it with their nifty stunt-excellency, Sidereals can exceed it pretty easily with rolled actions (though they lag behind a lot for static values), Liminals and Dragon-Blooded both start out weaker but end up with comparable or even superior exellencies by high essence values. An essence 5 DB who rolls 6 extra dice to begin with and then rerolls 5 failures is effectively adding 11 dice to their roll, which is better than what Solars can do. It costs a willpower and is obviously worse at lower essence values, so the Solar excellency is still obviously better overall, but it's not head and shoulders above what everyone else gets any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:03:52-07:00","id":867136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867126#post867126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you find the fact that &quot;Night&quot; is a caste for Solar Exalted straining?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so only Nights get the Mastery effect then? Gotcha!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867126#post867126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Training animals is a skill. I'm at a loss for what you're referring to with &quot;demons&quot;. If you mean Steel Devil or Righteous Devil, note that they focus on <i>weapons</i>, which require <b>skill</b> to wield.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not only straining, it burst at the seams and its guts are spilled all over. What does Tiger, Snake and Crane have to do with animal training? Are Tiger Stylist circus tamers? Snake Stylists snake charmers? Crane Stylists are some sort of weird falconers? C'mon man, right at all costs is not pretty to watch.<br /> <br /> By demons I refer to Black Claw, created by Mara, a demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867126#post867126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is fire breathing, free diving, parkour, gem cutting and wood carving. So elemental Styles should be able to be mastered just fine by Solars. (See how straining works?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867126#post867126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are &quot;doing&quot; while Elements are &quot;being&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the same token, Solars not getting special benefits with IMA is already the design intent, so that's like, your opinion, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know very little of how IMAs will actually turn out, so most statements on the matter will be in fact opinions. So that is like, your opinion too, man.<br /> <br /> What we have out is the Core, and that can be objectively discussed, even if some of it is still subject to interpretations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:06:38-07:00","id":867137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867135#post867135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar excellency isn't <i>that </i>awe-inspiringly powerful any more. Lunars can easily match or even exceed it with their nifty stunt-excellency, Sidereals can exceed it pretty easily with rolled actions (though they lag behind a lot for static values), Liminals and Dragon-Blooded both start out weaker but end up with comparable or even superior exellencies by high essence values. An essence 5 DB who rolls 6 extra dice to begin with and then rerolls 5 failures is effectively adding 11 dice to their roll, which is better than what Solars can do. It costs a willpower and is obviously worse at lower essence values, so the Solar excellency is still obviously better overall, but it's not head and shoulders above what everyone else gets any more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are Quick Character / Antagonists rules and probably won't reflect the playable splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:07:23-07:00","id":867138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867126#post867126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Training animals is a skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, training animals is a survival skill, and if any of the martial arts in the book were based around training animals you'd have a point. They aren't though, they're about emulating animals, like how wood dragon is about emulating the wood dragon. Also how do you explain White Reaper? Which is a style developed by Lunars, for Lunars, using glowing silver-white crescent shaped halos which wax and wane as the battle progresses. The Solar exalted looked at that, went &quot;that's super cool!&quot; then learned it and did it even better than the Lunar who made it up!<br /> <br /> In the current age White Reaper is practiced by a handful of elder lunars, and is the primary weapons of the Swords of Luna. So how come Lunars don't get this special style that was designed by them and is practiced by a small elite faction of them in the modern age. Well they do get it, but Solars still do it better because it's an MA and Solars do MA better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:19:27-07:00","id":867140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867132#post867132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I wouldn't actually mind if the Terrestrials were better at it. The proposed idea for implementation is what feels wrong to me. If they worked better for DBs due to synergies with their Anima Banners, Aspect Powers, Native Charms or something like that, I'd be applauding it as great design. Instead, we get Solars unable to fully master the styles to the same extent they can with every other MA Ability, and that doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> Like, If the Solars could show off their unsurpassed skill by mastering the techniques better than DBs, like in every other MA, but DBs still did better when using it because they were made for DBs and thus take advantage of things only DBs have? I would actually really like that dynamic <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(as long as there are balance checks in place for the difficulty and resources spent to acquire them so that DBs picking any other MA don't feel like chumps)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That still might be the case. Not having the Mastery keyword isn't the whole of the design intention. Assuming that the devs and writers are just gonna make a generic-style-but-with-no-mastery is potentially kind of disengenuous. I mean, I'm pretty sure they're more creative than that, given the amount of awesome packed into the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An essence 5 DB who rolls 6 extra dice to begin with and then rerolls 5 failures is effectively adding 11 dice to their roll, which is better than what Solars can do</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does your failure-reroll come from? Much like Solars, DBs probably aren't getting native MA charms.<br /> <br /> The Solar generally has a 5-die advantage over the DB, because if your rerolls are coming from your style, then the solar gets them too. Unless you mean that the reroll is the Terrestrial bonus in my hypothetical, in which case sure, but I'm not advocating for DBs getting those kinds of bonuses. Even <b>if</b> I was, I'd suggest to balance them with Excellencies in mind so that they <i>don't</i> trump a Solar's [charm+excellency] combo, so that DBs' versions would look impressive without actually becoming more powerful than Solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867136#post867136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so only Nights get the Mastery effect then? Gotcha!</div> </div> </div> </div>lol<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867136#post867136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not only straining, it burst at the seams and its guts are spilled all over. What does Tiger, Snake and Crane have to do with animal training? Are Tiger Stylist circus tamers? Snake Stylists snake charmers? Crane Stylists are some sort of weird falconers? C'mon man, right at all costs is not pretty to watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, good job on going for the jugular on a point you weren't clear on in the first place. Could have helped if I knew you were talking about styles.<br /> <br /> Tiger and Snake are, specifically, about the <i>human ability to emulate those animals as a fighting style</i>. Why do you think snakes and tigers don't get Martial Arts? Gee, I wonder. Lunars also don't get bonuses for being a Tiger in Tiger Style or a Snake in Snake Style. GEE I FUCKING WONDER WHY.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867136#post867136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By demons I refer to Black Claw, created by Mara, a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>K, yet it doesn't require to be a demon and doesn't depend on the fact that you're weilding demon essence<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So is fire breathing, free diving, parkour, gem cutting and wood carving. So elemental Styles should be able to be mastered just fine by Solars. (See how straining works?) </div> </div> </div>lol. The devs already decided that it's because of ~essence~ *waves arms mysticall* so uh, pretend to strain all you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We know very little of how IMAs will actually turn out, so most statements on the matter will be in fact opinions. </div> </div> </div>You're the one attaching yourself to a single dev statement and calling the entire design direction stupid. I'm trying to figure out how the devs are thinking about it so I can get in the same headspace. So yeah, it's all opinions. And you're the one shitting on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-17-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:29:10-07:00","id":867151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a style developed by Lunars, for Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div> You can tell by how the word &quot;Lunar&quot; does not appear once in the write up for White Reaper Style. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the current age White Reaper is practiced by a handful of elder lunars, and is the primary weapons of the Swords of Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div> Who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:31:33-07:00","id":867154,"title":"","content":"Something brought up here or the other thread of note, is that while Black Claw has Mastery effects, it's not actually that powerful of a style. Yet folks seem just fine taking Black Claw style Charms.<br /> <br /> That the Immacualte styles are not more powerful probably won't effect folks hwo want Water Dragon Style because they just...want it.<br /> <br /> As to why this and not other styles like Black Claw and White Reaper? Well, in Black Claw's case, Mara actually does get the Mastery benefits, so she's actually just as good as the Solar save Solar-inherent beenies. For White Reaper it's as simple that Lunars aren't very thematically tied to kung fu.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Exalted, hwoever, are thematically teid to kung fu and in fact, these particular styles. Is it consistent? No. The question I ask is why should it be?<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:34:10-07:00","id":867156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867140#post867140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, good job on going for the jugular on a point you weren't clear on in the first place. Could have helped if I knew you were talking about styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you knew to associate demons with Steel and Righteous Devil, and say the other MA themes I offered were because of mortal skill? Its best to own it up and move on instead of pretending to have made an honest mistake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867140#post867140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">K, yet it doesn't require to be a demon and doesn't depend on the fact that you're weilding demon essence</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you trying to make my point for me or something? The point is, so far, no Style has a theme resonance requirement for it to be mastered by a Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867140#post867140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lol. The devs already decided that it's because of ~essence~ *waves arms mysticall* so uh, pretend to strain all you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're the one attaching yourself to a single dev statement and calling the entire design direction stupid. I'm trying to figure out how the devs are thinking about it so I can get in the same headspace. So yeah, it's all opinions. And you're the one shitting on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how I am doing this that you say I am. I even said I'm interested in seeing how it turns out. I trust the devs to do their best, and even if I disagree with them, I won't call what they do stupid. I even agreed with Blaque and said that just because IMAs will lack mastery it doesn't mean they wouldn't be cool.<br /> <br /> I truly don't know where you're coming from with this.<br /> <br /> Disagreement is not shitting. I'm sorry you feel that way though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:36:27-07:00","id":867158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867135#post867135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar excellency isn't <i>that </i>awe-inspiringly powerful any more. Lunars can easily match or even exceed it with their nifty stunt-excellency, Sidereals can exceed it pretty easily with rolled actions (though they lag behind a lot for static values), Liminals and Dragon-Blooded both start out weaker but end up with comparable or even superior exellencies by high essence values. An essence 5 DB who rolls 6 extra dice to begin with and then rerolls 5 failures is effectively adding 11 dice to their roll, which is better than what Solars can do. It costs a willpower and is obviously worse at lower essence values, so the Solar excellency is still obviously better overall, but it's not head and shoulders above what everyone else gets any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars have it right here and now, and DBs rarely get above E3. Solars <i>begin</i> where others can maybe match it if they somehow reach E5. For pretty much all circumstances, the Solar Excellency is way better. They don't have to contort themselves like Lunars, though I think TN shanigans can be stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:43:03-07:00","id":867164,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disagreement is not shitting. I'm sorry you feel that way though. </div> </div> </div>Riiight. see:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867156#post867156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its best to own it up and move on instead of pretending to have made an honest mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>With sentences like this, it's hard to not read you as hostile. Because yes, I actually did think while writing that post that you were talking about Survival, Socialize and Performance, in an attempt to liken the Styles to other Solar charms. Because I'm not a friggin mind-reader.<br /> <br /> Which in itself is telling of how the styles are Ability-based.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867156#post867156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to make my point for me or something? The point is, so far, no Style has a theme resonance requirement for it to be mastered by a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? My point is that having a style that depends on you <i>being</i> something that Humans generally aren't isn't out of the question. I'm sorry that you're having trouble understanding that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:51:36-07:00","id":867170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867164#post867164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Riiight. see:<br /> <br /> <br /> With sentences like this, it's hard to not read you as hostile. Because yes, I actually did think while writing that post that you were talking about Survival, Socialize and Performance, in an attempt to liken the Styles to other Solar charms. Because I'm not a friggin mind-reader.<br /> <br /> Which in itself is telling of how the styles are Ability-based.<br /> <br /> <br /> And? My point is that having a style that depends on you <i>being</i> something that Humans generally aren't isn't out of the question. I'm sorry that you're having trouble understanding that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're selectively quoting out of order and out of context. And it is pretty obvious we were talking about MA Styles, as you uncannily knew, even mentioning Steel and Righteous Devil (which you still leave out because it casts doubts on you r whole argument).<br /> <br /> I disagreed with you on a line of argument you were taking. I called you out for straining said line of argument, and then for trying to make it as if you weren't.<br /> <br /> I respect you as a forum member, and greatly respect the devs for their work of passion in developing the game.<br /> <br /> There is no name calling or shitting anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:53:22-07:00","id":867172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867140#post867140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still might be the case. Not having the Mastery keyword isn't the whole of the design intention. Assuming that the devs and writers are just gonna make a generic-style-but-with-no-mastery is potentially kind of disengenuous. I mean, I'm pretty sure they're more creative than that, given the amount of awesome packed into the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a bit weird, though. The mastery keyword is used to portray &quot;Solars are boos at MA, yo&quot; in every other style. Why not use the same recourse in these 5 if the intention is that yes, as far as the actual techniques go they are as good at it as in every other style? There is already a mechanical widget to deal with that, I'd say creating another method to represent the exact same thing would shouldn't be necessary.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that Mastery is not a thing in-setting, just a way to represent how good Solars are at MA (and how good Sidereals become at it when doing whatever it is they need to do to access Mastery effects), so creating another mechanical thing that serves the same role seems strange.<br /> <br /> It would be preferable to Solars simply being unable to reach the heights of skill they can get at every other MA, but I'd probably still houserule the styles into having Mastery effects instead of whatever they turn out to have instead, just out of aesthetic preference for consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:54:36-07:00","id":867174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867140#post867140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does your failure-reroll come from? Much like Solars, DBs probably aren't getting native MA charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>...it comes from the Dragon-Blooded excellency, the very thing I was talking about in that post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:04:12-07:00","id":867181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867170#post867170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're selectively quoting out of order and out of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>One sentence was out of order to demonstrate a discordance within your post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867170#post867170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is pretty obvious we were talking about MA Styles, as you uncannily knew</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for telling me what I know and understand. I wouldn't have known otherwise.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> even mentioning Steel and Righteous Devil (which you still leave out because it casts doubts on you r whole argument). </div> </div> </div>Right, a style that's based on using a gun isn't based on the skill of weilding that gun. sure. Might wanna look at what those charms actually do. Hint: they don't create or manipulate Elements. Steel devil is literally about fighting with swords, not about being a devil or creating devils.<br /> Righteous Devil is about skill with a firewand. did you <i>read</i> the styles at all?<br /> <br /> Animal styles are specifically about the Human emulation of those animals. That's why actual tigers don't get Martial Arts or Charms, this has already been established by the Devs ever since an old-forum discussion about whether Lunars should get bonuses for being that animal in their Form Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagreed with you on a line of argument you were taking. I called you out for straining said line of argument, and then for trying to make it as if you weren't. </div> </div> </div>Light creating shadows is stranuous. Got it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I respect you as a forum member, and greatly respect the devs for their work of passion in developing the game.<br /> <br /> There is no name calling or shitting anywhere. </div> </div> </div>Not overtly, no. Yet in that same post you're implying I'm lying about my understanding for the purpose of, what, trolling you? Come on man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  typos 04-17-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:05:51-07:00","id":867182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867174#post867174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...it comes from the Dragon-Blooded excellency, the very thing I was talking about in that post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, DBs pay a point of willpower to reroll failures as well as motes, which is a point of willpower they can't spend on charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:08:18-07:00","id":867183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867174#post867174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...it comes from the Dragon-Blooded excellency, the very thing I was talking about in that post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what?<br /> *Re-reads the DB excellency*<br /> oh, oops.<br /> Still though, you're comparing an Essence 6 DB. Even at essence 5 they are, at best, equal.<br /> <br /> Edit: by which I mean it takes decades if not centuries for a DB to even come close, to a <i>starting</i> Solar's Excellence. One set of MA isn't going to change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-17-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:18:32-07:00","id":867186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867183#post867183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still though, you're comparing an Essence 6 DB. Even at essence 5 they are, at best, equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm comparing essence 5. Specialties still boost their cap, so at E5 they can add 6 dice and reroll 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:20:54-07:00","id":867188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867186#post867186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm comparing essence 5. Specialties still boost their cap, so at E5 they can add 6 dice and reroll 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point still stands: centuries.<br /> (you did initially say Essence 5, I mis-read, apologies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:28:09-07:00","id":867196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867181#post867181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not overtly, no. Yet in that same post you're implying I'm lying about my understanding for the purpose of, what, trolling you? Come on man.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what?<br /> <br /> For the very common and human desire to be right.<br /> <br /> I'm not calling you anything for it, I'm calling you on it.<br /> <br /> Look, I said:<br /> <br /> Animals, demons, song and etiquette.<br /> <br /> You say:<br /> <br /> Animal training, *what do you mean, Steel and Righteous Devil?&quot;, mortal skills.<br /> <br /> It is very clear you knew I was talking about animal styles, didn't figure I was talking about Black Claw and went for the Devil-Demon association, and associated Silver Voiced and Dreaming Pearl with mortal skills.<br /> <br /> If you still insist that I somehow misconstrued that, I apologize for misunderstanding you and putting you on a spot.<br /> <br /> So lets make this easy:<br /> <br /> <b>The fact that light casts shadows and that there is a Night Caste have no bearing whatsoever on the fact that Ebon Shadow has a Mastery effect. This is evidenced by all the other Styles that have Mastery and have no theme resonance with any Caste.<br /> <br /> Mastery comes from Solars being Martial Arts Bosses, as is stated on their splat description.<br /> <br /> That is what is written.<br /> <br /> The rationale for IMAs being different is not clear as of yet. To try and say that the rationale is Themes and that the Core Styles similarly work on this rationale is to strain a line of argument.</b><br /> <br /> Those are my arguments, address them if you wish.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:32:04-07:00","id":867198,"title":"","content":"Bolding your arguments doesn't make them better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:39:13-07:00","id":867204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867198#post867198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolding your arguments doesn't make them better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I turned that part bold to imply that those are the arguments that I wish to discuss. <br /> <br /> Is that clear enough for you now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:40:26-07:00","id":867205,"title":"","content":"To add;<br /> <br /> I don't feel that Night Castes are about casting shadows or any themes that lend to shadows (the shadow of all things being antithetical to UCS after all). They are about burning as brilliantly as the sun even when others can't see you.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the UCS exists yet there is no one to perceive it, is it still as glorious?&quot; - yes, yes it is. Force of nature and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":2721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","user":"Elkovash","date":". 04-17-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:42:05-07:00","id":867207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867196#post867196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rationale for IMAs being different is not clear as of yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is.<br /> <br /> The Five Glorious Dragon Styles were designed for the Dragon-Blooded. This is true in and out of universe.<br /> <br /> Think past the abstractions of the Charms to what that means. Think of the training.<br /> <br /> An Exalt performs breathing exercises every day until his breath burns hot like a steam bellows. Each morning he lights burning tapers on his head and shoulders, every scar is a mark of his failure to be one with the flame. He fasts for weeks on a bed of hot coals, savouring the heat as it nourishes him.<br /> <br /> Can a Solar do these things? Of course! Solars are masters of the martial arts. But to suggest a Solar can do these things better than an Exalt who the exercises were specifically designed to empower is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> A Fire Aspect has the advantage that he can already set himself on fire, for starters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:48:30-07:00","id":867216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867207#post867207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it is.<br /> <br /> The Five Glorious Dragon Styles were designed for the Dragon-Blooded. This is true in and out of universe.<br /> <br /> Think past the abstractions of the Charms to what that means. Think of the training.<br /> <br /> An Exalt performs breathing exercises every day until his breath burns hot like a steam bellows. Each morning he lights burning tapers on his head and shoulders, every scar is a mark of his failure to be one with the flame. He fasts for weeks on a bed of hot coals, savouring the heat as it nourishes him.<br /> <br /> Can a Solar do these things? Of course! Solars are masters of the martial arts. But to suggest a Solar can do these things better than an Exalt who the exercises were specifically designed to empower is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> A Fire Aspect has the advantage that he can already set himself on fire, for starters.</div> </div> </div> </div>As cool as your description is (and I truly mean it) unless you are a dev and are spoilering this part of IMAs it is not making the case clear for why IMAs don't have Mastery.<br /> <br /> If I gave White Reaper some Lunar fancy text people would just say it is not written that way. <br /> <br /> And IMAs aren't, for any practical purposes, written yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:53:03-07:00","id":867220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867216#post867216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As cool as your description is (and I truly mean it) unless you are a dev and are spoilering this part of IMAs it is not making the case clear for why IMAs don't have Mastery.<br /> <br /> If I gave White Reaper some Lunar fancy text people would just say it is not written that way.<br /> <br /> And IMAs aren't, for any practical purposes, written yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one thing, Holden's said this in a different thread.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/858366-aggiecon-47-dragonblooded-spoilers-w-bonus-sidereal-and-lunar-tibbits?p=862756#post862756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big advantages of practicing an Immaculate MA style as a non-DB are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You can teach it to DBs<br /> \u2022 You can pass for a DB more easily, maybe?<br /> \u2022 It's a pretty formidable way to kick ass<br /> \u2022 Sometimes you need to set a dude on fire?<br /> \u2022 Maybe you're trying to reconcile your Exaltation with lingering Immaculate beliefs from your upbringing?<br /> <br /> It's probably not the strongest MA option you could have picked, since it's optimized for someone else rather than designed for general use. But then, you know, neither is Black Claw, and there are plenty of people who pick that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is pretty clear that the Immaculate Styles are gonna be best when used by Dragon Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:53:54-07:00","id":867221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867196#post867196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that light casts shadows and that there is a Night Caste have no bearing whatsoever on the fact that Ebon Shadow has a Mastery effect. This is evidenced by all the other Styles that have Mastery and have no theme resonance with any Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brainstorming on a reason why it <i>would</i> is more interesting to me than falling back on &quot;Essence doesn't matter the devs are bullshitting us&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mastery comes from Solars being Martial Arts Bosses, as is stated on their splat description.<br /> <br /> That is what is written. </div> </div> </div>Ok, <i>you're </i>the one referencing what's written, so here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mastery: This keyword denotes Charms that have a greater effect when used by those Exalted who are masters of <b>mortal </b>Abilities: the Solar and Abyssal Exalted. </div> </div> </div>Do I find it weird that Ebon Shadow and Gazelle-Carp have Mastery? Sure. Does that mean that the only answer is &quot;essence can never matter in martial arts&quot;? I don't think so. I find it boring and limiting. It's much more interesting to try and understand how the devs reconcile these facts, rather than assuming they threw the concept out the windows as soon as they wrote it down and are now lying to us.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rationale for IMAs being different is not clear as of yet. </div> </div> </div>I don't think I've contested that?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To try and say that the rationale is Themes and that the Core Styles similarly work on this rationale is to strain a line of argument. </div> </div> </div>I'm not <i>saying</i> the rationale is themes. I'm trying to figure out what the rationale <i>is</i>, because the decision has already been made. I'm saying there's a clear go-to explanation: Solars are so good at MA that they rival even the people made* of fire empowered by the actual elemental dragon of fire, and the people actually empowered by the dragon of fire are pretty fucking good at it. I mean, sure, you can say &quot;the devs are wrong I'm gonna do it my way&quot;, but that's not useful.<br /> <br /> Edit: * not <i>literally</i> made of Fire, but they do have precedent for having a perfect that turns them into their element for an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-17-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:55:19-07:00","id":867223,"title":"","content":"Solars are already best at the styles as skill can do. The thing is, that is not something that they do better than DBs. DBs also do the styles as good as anyone can do.<br /> <br /> What bonuses they get in addition probably won't look like Mastery effects. And likely play on the fact that DBs you know, can as noted, do thing slike set themselves on fire.<br /> <br /> I think a thing to remember is that to an extent, Martial Arts aren't fighting by channeling any Essence in particular. THey're fighting <i>like</i> something. Tiger stylists fight <i>like</i> tigers. Ebon Shadow stylists fight as shadows. And a Fire Dragon stylist fights like the Fire Dragon. The base Ability is emulating that. Magic is emulating techniques of that Abiltiy, more orless. And because of it being Exalted, knowing a skill well will often let you know some weird shit when you get deep into it. Like how fighting as a shadow lets you teleport as a shadow. <br /> <br /> This is a skill. Solars are going to be good at that skill. It is just that when you fight like the Fire Dragon, you probably aren't going to do it with some extra bit of mastery of technique that an actual Chosen of the Fire Dragon is going to have. You're going to be still top at that skill. It just hs a different ceiling. I mean, note that Mara fights as good as you do at her style. Because, well, it's not fighting as Mara. It's fighting like her.<br /> <br /> (And even then, it's not like you took that style to be all powerful.)<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:58:25-07:00","id":867226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867151#post867151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can tell by how the word &amp;quot;Lunar&amp;quot; does not appear once in the write up for White Reaper Style. Who?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, but if they had a style where the practitioner manipulated the strands of fate in a manner emulating the pattern spiders, changing the destiny set out for the target by the stars you can't say &quot;you didn't say Sidereal so I have no idea what in the earth you're talking about by saying they have anything to do with that style.&quot;. The style gives you waxing and waning white crescents, and was designed by Lunars, literally the only thing I can think of to link it more to the moon is if the charms did different things at different times of the month.<br /> <br /> And the swords of Luna are one of the factions of the silver pact, a pretty martial one at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:58:31-07:00","id":867227,"title":"","content":"OK, here is an exercise.<br /> <br /> Your MA-focused Solar spent multiple stories challenging the 3rd Circle Demon Sifu, Suntarankal, the Crucible of Brass and Iron, passing every grueling test and has finally earned the right to learn the Demon Prince's secret style.<br /> <br /> Would you be ok with this style being inferior for the Solar than other styles, because it lacks Mastery effects due to being made by a demon, for himself, and developed by only himself and for himself for four thousands years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:59:53-07:00","id":867228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867227#post867227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, here is an exercise.<br /> <br /> Your MA-focused Solar spent multiple stories challenging the 3rd Circle Demon Sifu, Suntarankal, the Crucible of Brass and Iron, passing every grueling test and has finally earned the right to learn the Demon Prince's secret style.<br /> <br /> Would you be ok with this style being inferior for the Solar than other styles, because it lacks Mastery effects due to being made by a demon, for himself, and developed by only himself and for himself for four thousands years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But don't trust me, I'd take Sail in a desert game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, a Half-Orc Bard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:00:36-07:00","id":867229,"title":"","content":"A more relevant quote about why IMA styles lack Mastery:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/858366-aggiecon-47-dragonblooded-spoilers-w-bonus-sidereal-and-lunar-tibbits?p=862782#post862782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, yes, it's intended to signify &quot;you can still take this, but it's really not meant for you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm almost tempted to read it as implying IMA lack Mastery to keep them from being a trap for unwary Solar players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:02:35-07:00","id":867230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867216#post867216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As cool as your description is (and I truly mean it) unless you are a dev and are spoilering this part of IMAs it is not making the case clear for why IMAs don't have Mastery.<br /> <br /> If I gave White Reaper some Lunar fancy text people would just say it is not written that way.<br /> <br /> And IMAs aren't, for any practical purposes, written yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let me unpack that a bit.<br /> <br /> For a start, there is nothing here to spoiler, the origin of the styles is setting information that has been around since the Immaculate styles were first detailed in Exalted: The Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Second, White Reaper is a red herring because it has never actually been a specifically Lunar style, it just happened to be released in Glories Luna.<br /> <br /> Third, yes, of course they have been written, they have been in previous editions, and guess what? Dragon-Bloods have <i>always </i>been better at using them. They granted small, specific benefits for using the style weapons. 2.5 (an errata that was written by the current dev team) clarified that these benefits where Terrestrial only, making them the only thing in previous editions in any way analogous to Mastery Charms.<br /> <br /> Obviously this didn't stop Solar martial artists with Immaculate Charms being generally better fighters, because their martial arts were backed up by superior native Charms, mote pools and dice pools. And <i>this is still the case.</i><br /> <br /> Finally, if you want something to dig into from the current edition, here's a little teaser from the core book:<br /> <br /> &quot;The power of Terrestrial Exalted who undergo the Order\u2019s martial art training is beyond question. Immaculates spend their lives developing their Essence, and use the natural Charms of their kind mixed freely with the proprietary Immaculate martial arts styles to perform feats of martial prowess notable even among the Exalted.&quot; p72","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:10:48-07:00","id":867239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867220#post867220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is pretty clear that the Immaculate Styles are gonna be best when used by Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div> I understand and am not disputing that at all.<br /> <br /> I already stated that I'm interested in seeing how they will balance it out. By that quote it seems they're going the &quot;well yeah, it is not as good for a non DB&quot;, which in turn seems to imply that the charms will be designed to be in the Terrestrial level ballpark, hitting some Celestial if you're a DB.<br /> <br /> I hope that it is done in a way that doesn't make IMAs so good for DBs that combat characters that don't take them feel left behind.<br /> <br /> Maybe it will have some restrictions that make the other DB options attractive as well.<br /> <br /> I still maintain that the rationale for it is not clear. Did the Sidereals who designed it voluntarily made it not as good, even for themselves (As they can also access Mastery)? Is it because this time around the DBs themselves invented them and the techniques don't have that level of sophistication? Is it something else?<br /> <br /> While all the &quot;reasons&quot; I think for this reflect negatively on IMAs, maybe the devs will surprise me and I'm not left with this aftertaste in my mouth when I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:18:58-07:00","id":867246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867220#post867220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is pretty clear that the Immaculate Styles are gonna be best when used by Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's going to be the case? All we have on them so far is that they don't have mastery, and those quotes from Holden indicate that they aren't Solar-tier at the baseline (because otherwise Solars wouldn't need those justifications he provided to take them). So they're weaker than normal when used by Solars, but no better than other martial arts when used by Terrestrials. A Water Dragon-using DB isn't going to be any better at the style than a Solar, Lunar or Sidereal, and they won't be any better at doing martial arts in general than a DB using Snake either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:25:22-07:00","id":867248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2093_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2093\" data-vbnamecard=\"2093\">Crumplepunch</a> <br /> <br /> Are you saying IMA fluff is a sacred cow that won't be changed? You are sure the Sidereals designed them for the DBs, and not the DBs came up with themselves this time around?<br /> <br /> I never argued that DBs shouldn't be more powerful when using IMAs, I only argued that the extra power shouldn't come from the Ability itself, but from things inherent to DBs, like Anima and native Charms.<br /> <br /> Which, can still be true to be honest.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I've been discussing semantics here. I really don't care who is better at something than the other splat. I want to understand why and would like to find this reason to be consistent with the material we already have available, thats all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:34:45-07:00","id":867257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867226#post867226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The style\u2026 was designed by Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867226#post867226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the swords of Luna are one of the factions of the silver pact, a pretty martial one at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind. In fact, does the Ex3 Silver Pact have factions at all now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:49:52-07:00","id":867270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867221#post867221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, <i>you're </i>the one referencing what's written, so here:</div> </div> </div> </div>You might remember that I conceded you this point in one of our first exchanges in this thread. I still maintain that it is a very valid and good observation. I still look forward to seeing if IMAs will be the first &quot;non-mortal&quot; Abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867221#post867221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I find it weird that Ebon Shadow and Gazelle-Carp have Mastery? Sure. Does that mean that the only answer is &quot;essence can never matter in martial arts&quot;? I don't think so. I find it boring and limiting. It's much more interesting to try and understand how the devs reconcile these facts, rather than assuming they threw the concept out the windows as soon as they wrote it down and are now lying to us.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the thing. Those Styles come from Abilities that may be acquired by mortals. Mortal Black Claw (Dreaming Pearl, Silver Voiced) Stylists are a thing. The fact that the Charms are weird is explained by Essence. And a Solar's Essence is the best to take any mortal Ability to it's limit, and even beyond, therefore it is the best for any MA that has mortal practitioners.<br /> <br /> If IMAs have no mortal practitioners, that fact allied to your quote will pretty much resolve the internal consistency problem I'm seeing. Since that is not clear yet, we can only speculate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867221#post867221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've contested that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a general observation, some people claim it to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867221#post867221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not <i>saying</i> the rationale is themes. I'm trying to figure out what the rationale <i>is</i>, because the decision has already been made. I'm saying there's a clear go-to explanation: Solars are so good at MA that they rival even the people made* of fire empowered by the actual elemental dragon of fire, and the people actually empowered by the dragon of fire are pretty fucking good at it. I mean, sure, you can say &quot;the devs are wrong I'm gonna do it my way&quot;, but that's not useful.<br /> <br /> Edit: * not <i>literally</i> made of Fire, but they do have precedent for having a perfect that turns them into their element for an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, as you, am interested in understanding the rationale. We just approached from different angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:53:15-07:00","id":867273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867230#post867230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, White Reaper is a red herring because it has never actually been a specifically Lunar style, it just happened to be released in Glories Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it...totally was. It was introduced in Glories: Luna, Lunars brag about it being the first non-animal style ever invented and rub Sidereals faces in it, it uses moon shaped, moon coloured, halos that act like the moon, Luna favours the practitioners of the style while wearing her hunter shape, and the only people that writeup mentions who practice it are a faction of the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> WR is 100% a lunar style, but Solars are better at it. They're not better at being Lunars, but they're better at the Lunar MA because they're better at all MA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, for that matter, how far is this going to go? Is Ill Lilly not going to have the mastery keyword? What about Night Breeze? Jade Mountain? Seafaring Hero Style? Golden Jannisary? They're all elemental styles too. Either they get the same treatment, or a Solar is going to be better at grabbing a stick, imbuing it with deadly plant toxin, and animating all the plant life in the area to attack with him. Next to that, saying that a Solar can't be better with wood dragon than a DB because Wood Dragon essence is more attuned to wood aspect DBs sounds silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:56:12-07:00","id":867277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867216#post867216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> If I gave White Reaper some Lunar fancy text people would just say it is not written that way.<br /> <br /> And IMAs aren't, for any practical purposes, written yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867257#post867257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind. In fact, does the Ex3 Silver Pact have factions at all now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:10:58-07:00","id":867283,"title":"","content":"I'd appreciate you not doing that. I was responding to a different poster entirely, not to you &quot;giving White Reaper some fancy Lunar text.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, even if White Reaper was invented <i>by</i> Lunars, the Immaculate Styles were invented <i>for</i> Dragon-Blooded. There's a potent difference there, like a sword made <i>by</i> a six-fingered man versus a sword made <i>for</i> a six-fingered man. Inigo Montoya can wield the six-fingered man's sword and even beat the six-fingered man in a duel with that sword, but that doesn't change who it was made for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2016, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:11:37-07:00","id":867284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867257#post867257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> Cite that from the Ex3 book, if you don't mind. In fact, does the Ex3 Silver Pact have factions at all now?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's lots of stuff that isn't in the corebook that we have no reason to assume changed. If I'd said &quot;You might be able to get favour with the western war god, Siakal, she primarily accepts sacrifices in the form of live captives being cut and then thrown to the sea.&quot; nobody would say a thing, because there's no reason to assume that changed.<br /> <br /> Also even without that history, saying you can't see the connection between WR and the moon is like saying <a href=\"https://41.media.tumblr.com/709c6bb0ed186799e49ec32cf76ca682/tumblr_nhhf7st25q1u2z7z2o1_500.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this photo</a> doesn't appear to have anything to do with the sun and/or moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:17:05-07:00","id":867286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867283#post867283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd appreciate you not doing that. I was responding to a different poster entirely, not to you &quot;giving White Reaper some fancy Lunar text.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a free forum. You are not one of the most polite and considerate people on it.<br /> <br /> Maybe extend the courtesies you wish for yourself to others and see how it works out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:19:21-07:00","id":867287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867284#post867284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's lots of stuff that isn't in the corebook that we have no reason to assume changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case for Lunars and the Silver Pact, however. Not even remotely. <br /> <br /> Especially when one of the two devs gave a long diatribe against specifically MoEP: Lunars, Lunars, the Silver Pact, and the Silver Pact's nonsensical factions. After something like that, why on Earth would they then want to keep of the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:24:07-07:00","id":867291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867286#post867286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not one of the most polite and considerate people on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, yeah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867286#post867286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe extend the courtesies you wish for yourself to others and see how it works out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't quote your post in a different vein of the same discussion to keep my argument afloat\u2026 did I? Because that's what I'm wanting you to not do. Don't drag me under trying to stop yourself drowning just because I happen to be swimming near you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:37:49-07:00","id":867297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=856087#post856087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;You're always being hunted&quot; is a paper tiger of an issue honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be curious to hear your thoughts on this. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:42:35-07:00","id":867298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867291#post867291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, yeah.<br /> <br /> I didn't quote your post in a different vein of the same discussion to keep my argument afloat\u2026 did I? Because that's what I'm wanting you to not do. Don't drag me under trying to stop yourself drowning just because I happen to be swimming near you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You posted something that I predicted someone would and I congratulated myself on that. It felt good.<br /> <br /> The intricacies of your reasoning on when it is, or isn't, valid to quote someone are uninteresting to me. You quoted a post of mine for no other reason than snarkyness. I used a post of yours to make a point of mine. Can we call it even?<br /> <br /> Kudos to you for keeping your metaphor to an elemental motif!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:53:25-07:00","id":867302,"title":"","content":"Intricacies are half of why anyone on this forum ever disagrees with anyone else.<br /> <br /> Or, to pre-empt the person who's gonna jump on here to disagree with me, probably two-thirds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:57:16-07:00","id":867304,"title":"","content":"A fact that makes our parley a sadder event than I first presumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":".  Grammerz 04-17-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T20:26:40-07:00","id":867325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867302#post867302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intricacies are half of why anyone on this forum ever disagrees with anyone else.<br /> <br /> Or, to pre-empt the person who's gonna jump on here to disagree with me, probably two-thirds.</div> </div> </div> </div>At my table, two thirds is toxic to the solar eminence doctrine. The one half isn't even mechanically supported! Why hasn't this been errata'd yet?<br /> ...<br /> Seven twelfths.<br /> <br /> Edit: fuck flood detection!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  damn phone autocomplete 04-17-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:20:54-07:00","id":867406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867297#post867297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to hear your thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also like to hear Zelbinnean's thoughts, but I can tell you why I agree.<br /> <br /> Storytellers and players will always try to find a natural equilibrium in gameplay. Characters who fight will find fights, crafters will find things to craft, diplomats will find diplomatic crises to resolve. This is the cornerstone of an enjoyable game for everyone involved. Sure, the storyteller will throw a curveball now and then, but fundamentally if you are going to run a group that has written up illiterate Dawn combat monsters through a courtly intrigue nobody is going to have a good time.<br /> <br /> With this equilibrium in mind, the threat that the Anathema are hunted and face an omnipresent military force chasing them down wherever they go looks less like a problem and more like a feature from a game perspective. A Dragon-Blood warrior and a Solar warrior are going to spend roughly the same amount of their stories threatened with deadly force, because that's just how games work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 04-18-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T04:45:43-07:00","id":867485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's lots of stuff that isn't in the corebook that we have no reason to assume changed.</div> </div> </div> </div> From the corebook? No. From Holden having often talked about how the Swords of Lunar are <i>really really</i> stupid? I can rather comfortably assume that they'll be <i>persona non grata</i> in a setting in which the main dramatic thrust of the Lunars is fighting the Realm rather than abstractly defending the world from raksha who are innumerable hoards when they should be impoverished exiles. All of that notwithstanding the use of White Reaper Style by Lunars; hell, as Martial Arts go, it probably <i>could</i> be assumed to be disproportionately utilised by Lunars, but as a function of them being hated by almost everybody in the world and likely have to often fight when greatly outnumbered, rather than &quot;a Lunar developed it, I guess, so, y'know, solidarity and all&quot;. I would find that (along with every other depiction of White Reaper Style across two editions) to be a bit less intimate and significant than the Immaculate Dragon Bloods are to the Dragon-Styled (y'know, &quot;mentioned in the book outline&quot; significant), so it's still a massive dog-and-pony show as far as the difference between Exalted using Immaculate Styles goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:47:23-07:00","id":867622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867216#post867216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I gave White Reaper some Lunar fancy text people would just say it is not written that way. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You'll never see me seriously complaining that Lunars don't get any special benefit to practicing White Reaper or Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. I'm only slightly bitter about it, but it makes sense.<br /> <br /> See, one style was made to use wide, sweeping attacks to fight multitudes of enemies at once, and the other was designed to weaponize singing. NEITHER of these things are particular to Lunar Essence.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar (or Sidereal) wanted to design a Style more attuned to Lunar Essence than any other, it would need to be a Style that capitalizes on the ability to instantly change shape in battle. This is something that some spirits (including Fair Folk) could do, but which is normally beyond the abilities of other Exalted, and even a spirit seldom have a greater number and variety of forms than a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:03:38-07:00","id":867630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867227#post867227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, here is an exercise.<br /> <br /> Your MA-focused Solar spent multiple stories challenging the 3rd Circle Demon Sifu, Suntarankal, the Crucible of Brass and Iron, passing every grueling test and has finally earned the right to learn the Demon Prince's secret style.<br /> <br /> Would you be ok with this style being inferior for the Solar than other styles, because it lacks Mastery effects due to being made by a demon, for himself, and developed by only himself and for himself for four thousands years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends.<br /> <br /> Look above to my last post. Note how the Lunar Exalted made two different canonical Styles. Note that while both creators likely made these Styles for themselves, they did not choose to create Styles centered around things exclusively natural to Lunar Exaltation. So they incidentally created Styles where Solar Exalted would just outright perform better than them.<br /> <br /> Suntarankal might create a boxing or kicking-focused Style, just because that is a thing he wanted to do. Since nothing about punching and kicking is less natural to humans than to demons, these Styles would have Mastery-level effects for Solars.*<br /> <br /> But if Suntarankal developed something like Throne Shadow Style -- except instead of working through Shadow Fingers, the Stylist works through his Second Circle Souls -- then Solar Exalted are out of luck. Because Exalted don't HAVE Second Circle Souls.<br /> <br /> Why should a Solar player regret not being the best with a Martial Art Style designed by a Third Circle Demons for the express purpose of weaponizing one of the unique features of being a Third Circle Demon?<br /> <br /> <br /> *Suntarankal also wouldn't enjoy Mastery effects for these Charms as Mara does for her Style, because he's not designing these Styles to reflect his demonic essence. (He MIGHT enjoy Mastery effects simply because he's a living embodiment of Martial Arts mastery, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-18-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:14:24-07:00","id":867674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867630#post867630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if Suntarankal developed something like Throne Shadow Style -- except instead of working through Shadow Fingers, the Stylist works through his Second Circle Souls -- then Solar Exalted are out of luck. Because Exalted don't HAVE Second Circle Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were a necessity, if the Charms absolutely depended on using additional souls-who-are-people, the Solar shouldn't be able to even learn it in the first place, in my opinion. But if, say, the Charms in the style did things when you used it personally <i>and </i>things when used through your souls, it would for me fall into a similar situation to the one I described earlier as desirable for the Immaculate styles: Solars and Sidereals should be able to learn it and get Mastery effects, but would be unable to do the anything with their non-existing extra souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:17:37-07:00","id":867679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867485#post867485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From the corebook? No. From Holden having often talked about how the Swords of Lunar are <i>really really</i> stupid? I can rather comfortably assume that they'll be <i>persona non grata</i> in a setting in which the main dramatic thrust of the Lunars is fighting the Realm rather than abstractly defending the world from raksha who are innumerable hoards when they should be impoverished exiles. All of that notwithstanding the use of White Reaper Style by Lunars; hell, as Martial Arts go, it probably <i>could</i> be assumed to be disproportionately utilised by Lunars, but as a function of them being hated by almost everybody in the world and likely have to often fight when greatly outnumbered, rather than &quot;a Lunar developed it, I guess, so, y'know, solidarity and all&quot;. I would find that (along with every other depiction of White Reaper Style across two editions) to be a bit less intimate and significant than the Immaculate Dragon Bloods are to the Dragon-Styled (y'know, &quot;mentioned in the book outline&quot; significant), so it's still a massive dog-and-pony show as far as the difference between Exalted using Immaculate Styles goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, the Swords of Lunar probably aren't going to be a thing anymore. But the style is still pretty Lunar themed. And again I will bring up styles like Golden Jannisary, Ill Lilly, Night Breeze, ect. A Solar will be better than a fire aspect at striking a foe and immolating them in a pillar of cleansing fire, a Solar will be better than a wood aspect at animating a whole copse of trees to strike and grapple, a Solar will be better than an air aspect at flinging a needle and having it physically turning into a deadly killing wind.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to say that the Sidereals, for some unfathomable reason, worked and worked and worked until they pulled an exalted style miracle out of their ass and developed five elemental martial arts that specifically couldn't be mastered by Solar exalted, only learned, then I would buy that. I'd really question why they felt the need to do that, but I'd agree it's a reasonable explanation.<br /> <br /> The idea that Solars can't master the Dragon Styles because their essence just isn't right is BS though. Martial arts, evocations and sorcery are specifically in the system and the setting to allow Solars to do cool shit that normally their native charms can't accomplish. Like animating an enemy's shadow, or filling their soul with venomous essence of a snakebite. If they don't get the mastery keyword on IMA, which will seriously disappoint me for reasons I've already stated, then it needs to be made clear that this one miraculous exception to the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:58:29-07:00","id":867712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867679#post867679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts, evocations and sorcery are specifically in the system and the setting to allow Solars to do cool shit that normally their native charms can't accomplish. Like animating an enemy's shadow, or filling their soul with venomous essence of a snakebite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er.... I don't think that's *exactly* the reason they're in a game that's based on the genres of kung fu movies, and sword and sorcery, no. The tail is wagging the dog a bit here. The cart is going before the horse. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:12:27-07:00","id":867764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the style is still pretty Lunar themed.</div> </div> </div> </div> It glows white; that's about it. Cosmetics are not themes. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar will be better than a fire aspect at striking a foe and immolating them in a pillar of cleansing fire, a Solar will be better than a wood aspect at animating a whole copse of trees to strike and grapple, a Solar will be better than an air aspect at flinging a needle and having it physically turning into a deadly killing wind.</div> </div> </div> </div> The likelihood that Golden Janissary won't be a thing anymore either notwithstanding, whether or not its attacks resemble fire is incidental because the fire isn't actually the point, anymore than there's anything to comparing the green fire of Infernals to Dragon Blooded or elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:11:10-07:00","id":867809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867764#post867764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It glows white; that's about it. Cosmetics are not themes. The likelihood that Golden Janissary won't be a thing anymore either notwithstanding, whether or not its attacks resemble fire is incidental because the fire isn't actually the point, anymore than there's anything to comparing the green fire of Infernals to Dragon Blooded or elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems completely unnecessary, especially with evocations. So Golden Janissary and Ill Lilly can't be things anymore because they'd let Solars use MA to manipulate elements, in the same edition that introduces things like sorcerous merits that let you spew fire from your hands and evocations that encase your opponent in unbreakable ice? Keeping in mind that a Solar, even without mastery, can absolutely still learn Fire Dragon style and use all it's charms, so it's not like taking out Ill Lilly stops that from being a thing, it just makes it crappy for a Solar to take it.<br /> <br /> Or what about Dark Messiah Style? Will it's charms have mastery keywords that only Abyssals get? Same for Infernal Monster and Infernals? If that's not the case because those styles, and indeed Golden Janissary and Ill Lilly, aren't REALLY about the kind of special essence of those exalted, they're different, but IMA are, then they shouldn't even be MA, because MA aren't about using a special kind of essence that only you have, that's what native charms are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:34:44-07:00","id":867824,"title":"","content":"How about;<br /> <br /> Rather than working for years on end developing a martial arts style specifically to lock out solars from being better at it, the worked and worked and worked and pulled out of their arse a Martial Arts style that was so fundamental and supportive of essence users that almost everybody who can wield essence can 'master' it. The lack of a mastery tag being indicative of there being no more juice to squeeze from that particular lemon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:45:46-07:00","id":867830,"title":"","content":"Man, developing a martial arts style that is specifically designed to make it impossible for Solars to master seems like the most petty, spiteful thing to do ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:41:34-07:00","id":867876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867830#post867830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, developing a martial arts style that is specifically designed to make it impossible for Solars to master seems like the most petty, spiteful thing to do ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/s1Qn4nQ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> that is all....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T16:32:26-07:00","id":867903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867830#post867830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, developing a martial arts style that is specifically designed to make it impossible for Solars to master seems like the most petty, spiteful thing to do ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? The centuries of indiscriminate murder by the Wyld Hunt, that's just business, the real kicker is when they're <i>mean</i> to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T16:44:15-07:00","id":867905,"title":"","content":"There's so much wrong with so many posts in this thread that I scarcely know where to start. The idea that Sids developing the styles for DBs is somehow a deliberate attempt to lock Solars out? The idea that not having Mastery somehow makes the Solars <i>unable</i> to master a style? The idea that Dark Messiah Style won't just be Abyssal Brawl Charms in Ex3, that it'll be some sort of full-fledged martial art? Seriously, I don't even know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:03:00-07:00","id":867971,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I wonder if Exalted fans even deserves to have a well put together game. God knows they'll find a way to ruin it, regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:10:01-07:00","id":867977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867830#post867830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, developing a martial arts style that is specifically designed to make it impossible for Solars to master seems like the most petty, spiteful thing to do ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's almost like the Dragonblooded believe Solars are Anathema or something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:15:05-07:00","id":867992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867977#post867977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's almost like the Dragonblooded believe Solars are Anathema or something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> And it's almost like the Sidereals remember how the Solars almost destroyed the world for fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:39:13-07:00","id":868020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867905#post867905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so much wrong with so many posts in this thread that I scarcely know where to start. The idea that Sids developing the styles for DBs is somehow a deliberate attempt to lock Solars out? The idea that not having Mastery somehow makes the Solars <i>unable</i> to master a style? The idea that Dark Messiah Style won't just be Abyssal Brawl Charms in Ex3, that it'll be some sort of full-fledged martial art? Seriously, I don't even know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I also don't get why people are complaining so much when the Immaculate styles not having Mastery effects is also exactly how they worked in 2nd ed, and no one complained about the fact that DBs and Solars were just as good at using them back then. And some Solars took those styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:52:52-07:00","id":868030,"title":"","content":"Assuming it's even the case (which is sort of a long shot), deliberately making a martial tradition that's not as amazing for your <i>sworn enemies who you keep murdering on sight </i>sounds less like spite and more like, shit, I dunno, competence.<br /> <br /> On that note, I would be pretty happy if it turned out that individual, ridiculously exceptional Dragon-Bloods (think Ragara Myrrun) created the styles on individual occasions over the course of the Shogunate, hence why they're so well-attuned to a Dragon's strengths. BUT that Sidereals, in their role as seekers of hidden knowledge, teachers and sifus, learned and proliferated the techniques to further their own goals, and Sids are the reason that the techniques survive to the modern day and are prolific rather than being forgotten traditions that never left the mountain and died with their founders. (Most notably, the reason the Arts survived the crusagion.)<br /> <br /> Something that really emphasizes the sort of weird but effective partnership those two have, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 04-18-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:10:22-07:00","id":871337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=867679#post867679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again I will bring up styles like Golden Jannisary, Ill Lilly, Night Breeze, ect. A Solar will be better than a fire aspect at striking a foe and immolating them in a pillar of cleansing fire, a Solar will be better than a wood aspect at animating a whole copse of trees to strike and grapple, a Solar will be better than an air aspect at flinging a needle and having it physically turning into a deadly killing wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if these styles are updated by a robot with no regard for where the Terrestrial and Mastery keywords are appropriate. My Night Caste is an Ill Lilly Stylist and there's plenty of places where the charms can show she's a superior Martial Artist without the pinnacle having to give her superior elemental power, assuming it still is the pinnacle in a 3e update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:05:40-07:00","id":871399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted#post855790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book and the fan often said what in the title, but it's always declared in a vague and kinda fluffy way. Now that we have the charms for Solar, are these the parts of Solar powerset that'll make a Sidereal go &quot;It's a good thing we tried to kill them in the past&quot; and a DB go &quot;It's NOT fair !&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div>======= General Thoughts =====<br /> To bypass some of the sniping in the last several pages, Solars are the most broadly and directly powerful of the Exalted. At any given Essence/XP level, a given Solar is going to perform better in a general area of competence than another Exalt with a similar specialty. The only away around that is to define the area of competence in a narrow way, such as &quot;manipulating the elements.&quot; Other Exalts can do things the Solar can't do, but generally the application of those things will be less effective for a given task.<br /> <br /> A Solar outside their specialty is not going to be better at most things than other Exalts, spirits, or even mortals. ISP may have an Integrity Excellency, but she can't function in a court nearly as well as her Lunar Mate, who only has a Manipulation Excellency.<br /> <br /> This is all necessary for the intended Solar play experience. Solars are like action heroes, or heroes from ancient epics. They are better/faster/stronger/smarter, but they are outnumbered, with few resources, and they lack grounding and infrastructure. The lower overall power of the other splats is intrinsic to that play experience.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the greater power of the Solars is intrinsic to the intended play experience of the other splats. For example, the Dragon-Blooded would have no reason to fear the Solars if the Anathema didn't have more power. From the DB perspective, the Solars are the Great Monsters, and only by bringing to bear all their advantages and numbers in unison can they defeat them. A group of PC Dragon-Blood who destroy one vile Solar Anathema have beat the boss monster of their story arc, if not their entire campaign. That boss fight would be pretty anti-climatic if they could have done it easily at char-gen.<br /> <br /> What's changed in E3 is how the gap manifests itself. Previously, a Solar who managed to get Infinite Melee Mastery up could go through <i>n</i> average Dragon-Bloods, and with a 2/7 filter it almost required ST fiat. Now a newly Exalted Dawn Caste can be expected, assuming average rolls, to defeat an experienced DB warrior, maybe even two. BUT, the Dawn will likely be wounded, and will definitely be running low on Essence, if not tapped. The Dawn won't be able to handle another two.<br /> <br /> This is a better mechanical model for the intended play experience. Solars are powerful and terrifying, but not arbitrarily so, and thus have to treat DBs and the Wyld Hunt as life-threatening. On the flip side, the DBs have every reason to kill the Solars young, because if they put down roots and rack up XP, it will cost them dearly to put the Anathema down. if the Dawn Caste trains a few Legions with TWTT and hits E4, the Realm will be forced to spend lots of lives to save the region from him.<br /> <br /> ===== Specific Parts =====<br /> The basic parts of Solar superiority haven't changed much.<ul><li>Larger mote pools, over the long term</li> <li>Larger dice pools, or easier access to the same dice pool</li> <li>Charms with broad applicability and slightly better numbers here and there.</li> <li>Charms that break/subvert dice caps.</li> <li>Direct access to Mastery effects in MA.</li> <li>Unique access to Solar Sorcery.</li> <li>A few unique charms, such as WST.</li> <li>Crazy Craft potential (even if it costs all the XP to E5 and beyond).</li> </ul>But really, we don't know for sure, because we haven't seen the final rules for the other Exalts, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:28:21-07:00","id":871427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=871399#post871399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Crazy Craft potential (even if it costs all the XP to E5 and beyond).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really ? I purposely avoid all Ex3 Craft thread so I don't know Solar Craft is still that good.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, can people tell me what kind of crazy potential does a Supernal Craft Solar has ? As in how much time do they need to make a 5-dots Artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T14:05:08-07:00","id":871715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=871427#post871427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, can people tell me what kind of crazy potential does a Supernal Craft Solar has ? As in how much time do they need to make a 5-dots Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>(6 - Essence) months to make a 5-dot or N/A artifact, or that many weeks to make any other artifact. They can also work on a reasonably large number of artifacts at once, so you could complete multiple artifacts during that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T19:56:56-07:00","id":872014,"title":"","content":"I run a 320xp-ish game (so Essence 5). The Twilight has 15 craft charms.<br /> <br /> The Twilight generates 22 gold xp every day (it's 10 gold xp for a craft artefact roll). So, he basically doesn't need to worry about how many rolls it takes, as long as it's no higher than the terminus. He tends to get over 20 successes on each craft roll.<br /> <br /> So, he can reasonably reliably make any artefact lower than 5 in a week, though with a small failure chance for level 4s. He's got a good chance of making an artefact 5 in a month, but also a good chance of failing. About half and half probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:28:45-07:00","id":872543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=872014#post872014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run a 320xp-ish game (so Essence 5). The Twilight has 15 craft charms.<br /> <br /> The Twilight generates 22 gold xp every day (it's 10 gold xp for a craft artefact roll). So, he basically doesn't need to worry about how many rolls it takes, as long as it's no higher than the terminus. He tends to get over 20 successes on each craft roll.<br /> <br /> So, he can reasonably reliably make any artefact lower than 5 in a week, though with a small failure chance for level 4s. He's got a good chance of making an artefact 5 in a month, but also a good chance of failing. About half and half probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, are you saying he just builds up enough craft xp in the &quot;waiting period,&quot; and then just rolls to finish over again? If so, that's impressive, given he only has 15 Craft charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T19:02:07-07:00","id":872799,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I made a mistake. He's getting 31.5 gold xp a day (or specifically, 49 sxp and 7 gxp, which with Sublime Transference becomes 31.5 gxp). So 2 days of adventuring gives him enough crafting xp to make 6 rolls for an artefact.<br /> <br /> However, I should say that he can only be getting such high successes with Bright-Forging Prana once per story. So, he could probably make an Artefact 2 every few weeks, but Artefact 3 or 4 is more like once a story.<br /> <br /> The thing that slows him down isn't crafting xp, because he has so much, it's the 1/story on Bright-Forging Prana, and getting the appropriate materials.<br /> <br /> Also, he only got the charm for getting 31.5 gold xp a session like 3 sessions ago. So before that, he'd only made one artefact in 20 sessions, and in the last 3 sessions, he's made a castle (a superior project) and fixed a broken manse.<br /> I assume he'll make another artefact in the upcoming downtime. Plus one of the other PCs wants him to make her a city.<br /> <br /> So... basically, compared to the old rules, it works out similar, except he can go adventuring instead of spending months in his workshop, and it cost him tons more XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T23:29:33-07:00","id":872921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=871399#post871399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar outside their specialty is not going to be better at most things than other Exalts, spirits, or even mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one is stretching it a bit. Buying a single charm (and getting the excellency on top of it) in a non-combat ability where she has around three dots is going to make the ISP vastly better at it than the vast majority of mortals. For example, if the ISP just takings Medicine 3 and Wound-Mending Care Technique, she's going to be hard for even most dedicated mortal doctors to beat; throw on Wound-Cleansing Meditation and Flawless Diagnosis Technique, and she's already performing impossible feats of medicine while being peerless at most traditional applications.<br /> <br /> I mean, in areas where she has <i>no charms</i>, sure. But remember, she doesn't have to buy excellencies anymore, which means that taking just a few dots in an ability and buying one of the broad-ish intro charms is usually enough for a Solar to outshine all but the very greatest of mortals in that field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-24-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:19:36-07:00","id":873020,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: &quot;to be <i>able</i> to outshine.&quot; You still gotta <i>do</i> shit, because all the piles of dice and Charms in the world won't do a thing on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T11:20:04-07:00","id":873188,"title":"","content":"So after re-reading the section on immaculate monks in the setting chapter, this is the true advantage that DBs will have with the Immaculate Syles.<br /> <br /> DRAGON-BLOODED MONKS<br /> The power of Terrestrial Exalted who undergo the Order\u2019s<br /> martial art training is beyond question. Immaculates<br /> spend their lives developing their Essence, and use the<br /> natural Charms of their kind mixed freely with the proprietary<br /> Immaculate martial arts styles to perform feats<br /> of martial prowess notable even among the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11481-demonreach77","name":"Demonreach77","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:38:05-07:00","id":873474,"title":"","content":"Huh, now that's interesting. So they can use Brawl charms with Martial Arts charms on the same attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:08:13-07:00","id":873484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=873474#post873474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, now that's interesting. So they can use Brawl charms with Martial Arts charms on the same attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in that passage suggests they can do so more freely than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Reflexives cross boundaries like normal. Unless I've forgotten some 3rd MA-compatibility restriction again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:19:03-07:00","id":873491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=873484#post873484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in that passage suggests they can do so more freely than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Reflexives cross boundaries like normal. Unless I've forgotten some 3rd MA-compatibility restriction again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which version of &quot;normal&quot; you're going by. This was added in the final release:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reflexive Charms which enhance static values may generally only enhance static values deriving from their governing Ability, unless otherwise indicated. For example, Dipping Swallow Defense will only remove penalties from a Melee-based Parry attempt. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T20:29:24-07:00","id":873500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=873491#post873491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on which version of &quot;normal&quot; you're going by. This was added in the final release:</div> </div> </div> </div>So we can assume that Fists of Iron Technique will not affect bare-handed Martial Arts attacks or parries, and that Iron Battle Focus will not remove Onslaught penalties from either your MA Parry or Evasion value.<br /> <br /> Wind and Stones Defense specifically mentions that it assists Evasion, thus allowing cross-compatibility with Dodge in that particular interaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reflexive Charms which create attacks generally do so with the Ability they belong to, unless the governing Ability can\u2019t normally attack or unless otherwise noted. </div> </div> </div>So, the attack made with Thunderclap Rush Technique MUST be Brawl-based, as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, then. Mixing Reflexive Charms across Abilities is more restricted this time around.<br /> <br /> Still, I imagine that it's not about the Dragon-Blooded being able to use ANY MA Charms with their Brawl Charms, so much as a specific compatibility in the Immaculate Styles which share the elemental focus of their native Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T21:23:43-07:00","id":873520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=873500#post873500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the attack made with Thunderclap Rush Technique MUST be Brawl-based, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the case if it didn't specifically say it doesn't have to be brawl-based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:24:23-07:00","id":873771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=873520#post873520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the case if it didn't specifically say it doesn't have to be brawl-based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies; I didn't read carefully enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:18:19-07:00","id":875125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/855790-in-what-ways-are-solar-the-most-powerful-among-the-exalted?p=872921#post872921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last one is stretching it a bit. Buying a single charm (and getting the excellency on top of it) in a non-combat ability where she has around three dots is going to make the ISP vastly better at it than the vast majority of mortals. For example, if the ISP just takings Medicine 3 and Wound-Mending Care Technique, she's going to be hard for even most dedicated mortal doctors to beat; throw on Wound-Cleansing Meditation and Flawless Diagnosis Technique, and she's already performing impossible feats of medicine while being peerless at most traditional applications.<br /> <br /> I mean, in areas where she has <i>no charms</i>, sure. But remember, she doesn't have to buy excellencies anymore, which means that taking just a few dots in an ability and buying one of the broad-ish intro charms is usually enough for a Solar to outshine all but the very greatest of mortals in that field.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate on this a bit, I'm intending the comparison to be relative to the Lunar, which is why the sentence about the Lunar is in that paragraph. A Lunar sneak-thief might not be particularly good at Melee/Archery/Ranged, but they likely bought the Dexterity Excellency.<br /> <br /> As regards the mortal statement, ISP dropping a charm pick at char-gen, to me indicates her player wants her to be effective in that. ISP could certainly buy a Medicine charm. That's one of her 15 Charms, which is a notable investment, to me. Every &quot;alternate&quot; charm pick she makes detracts from her specialty. Someone like ISP is going to want lots of Melee charms, a few Dodge charms, maybe one Brawl charm for backup/grapples, and one or two Resistance charms. That doesn't leave her many other picks, even if she takes the objectively bad option of dropping BP on charms.<br /> <br /> Which all adds up to ISP being substantially more normal, and therefore less powerful, than a mortal in many areas. Hopefully that clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}